const motionPreviewData = {
  "100": ["photo",4,"分割光","侧面光让脸一半明亮、一半阴暗","Please use \"Split lighting\" (スプリットライティング), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #100\n\nWhat it is: Light from the side splits the face into lit and dark halves\nWhat the sample shows: The light swings from near the front (20°) to directly at the side (90°); the shadow on the head grows from a crescent to exactly half, splitting the face down the middle.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). the background drops to a darker scene (sky #E7E5E1)\n- Light: from the left of the frame, angle 20° → 90° (plan at the bottom right, top-right readout \"90° · ↑0°\")\n- Head: right of x = 270 + cos(angle)·√(29² − dy²) is shadow #33405A, left is light #FFC75A; at 90° the edge is the straight centre line\n- Body (half-width 56 px): right of x = 270 + cos(angle)·56 is shadow, a strip on the left edge is lit\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For dramatic, tense or moody portraits.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/100.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","人像采用分割光，灯在侧面 90°，以鼻梁为界，另一半脸处于阴影。"],
  "101": ["photo",5,"伦勃朗光","侧上方光在背光脸颊留下亮三角","Please use \"Rembrandt lighting\" (レンブラントライティング), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #101\n\nWhat it is: High side light that leaves a lit triangle on the shadow cheek\nWhat the sample shows: A light 45° to the side and 45° up comes on; the right side of the face falls into shadow except for a small inverted triangle of light on the shadow-side cheek.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). the background drops to a darker scene (sky #E7E5E1)\n- Head: right of x = 270 + 0.04·29 is shadow #33405A, left is light #FFC75A\n- Light triangle: (x 270+0.24R, y 78−0.12R), (x 270+0.7R, y 78−0.12R), (x 270+0.24R, y 78+0.5R) with R = 29 (about 13 px wide, 18 px tall), separated from the lit side by a shadow strip about 6 px wide\n- Body: lit left of centre −0.45×56 px, shadow right of +0.3×56 px; plan shows the light at 45°, top-right readout \"45° · ↑45°\"\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For portraits with a painterly, sculpted, classic look.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/101.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","老人肖像用伦勃朗光，从侧上方 45° 打光，背光侧脸颊留一小块三角亮区。"],
  "102": ["photo",6,"蝴蝶光","正面高位光在鼻下形成蝶形阴影","Please use \"Butterfly lighting\" (バタフライライティング), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #102\n\nWhat it is: High frontal light that casts a butterfly shadow under the nose\nWhat the sample shows: A light in front of the face and high above comes on; the face lights evenly on both sides and only a small symmetrical shadow falls under the chin.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). the background drops to a darker scene (sky #E7E5E1)\n- Head: entirely lit #FFC75A (no shadow side)\n- Shadow under the chin: an ellipse centred at y 78+1.06R, 0.72R wide and 0.38R tall (R = 29, about 21×11 px), colour #33405A\n- Body: lit within ±0.8×56 px of the centre, thin outer strips keep the base colour; plan shows the light on the camera side (0°), top-right readout \"0° · ↑45°\"\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For beauty and fashion portraits that flatter the face.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/102.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","美妆人像用蝴蝶光：灯在正前方、高于面部约 45°，鼻下留出小小的蝶形阴影。"],
  "103": ["photo",7,"黄金时刻","日出后或日落前的低角度暖光","Please use \"Golden hour\" (ゴールデンアワー), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #103\n\nWhat it is: The low, warm light just after sunrise or before sunset\nWhat the sample shows: The sun drops to just above the horizon; sky and ground turn orange, the left side of the person lights up and the shadows of the lamp and tree stretch far to the right.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). \n- Sun: radius 18 px, from (x 110, y −30) to (x 96, y 136), half hidden by the hills\n- Colour: sky #FAF9F7 → #FFE8BC at the top and #FFCF80 near the horizon, ground #F1F0EE → #F6DDB0; light on the figure #FFB547, shadow #3E3650\n- Head: light from the left at about 66°, shadow right of the edge; body lit on the left, shadow on the right\n- Shadows: from the foot of the lamp and tree to the right, length 0 → 150 px (#DDAA6E); top-right time 12:00 → 17:40\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For warm, nostalgic, gentle-feeling images.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/103.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","黄金时刻的田野人物，太阳接近地平线，长阴影，整体暖橙色。"],
  "104": ["photo",8,"蓝调时刻","日落后或日出前的深蓝天空时段","Please use \"Blue hour\" (ブルーアワー), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #104\n\nWhat it is: The time after sunset or before sunrise when the sky turns deep blue\nWhat the sample shows: Once the sun has set, the sky turns two bands of deep blue, the windows and street lamp come on in amber and the person becomes a dark blue shape.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). \n- Sun: radius 18 px at x 120, sinking from y 40 to y 190 while the effect reaches 70%, fading out between 40% and 80%\n- Colour: sky #2C3B5E at the top and #4A6191 near the horizon, ground #283452, buildings #34446B, figure #1C2439\n- Lights: one window in three and the lamp bulb turn #FFC75A; flat rings of 13 px and 8 px (#FFE3A3 at 35% and 60%) around the bulb\n- Top-right time 12:00 → 18:35\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For city and night scenes that need both a blue sky and glowing lights.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/104.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","蓝调时刻的港口城市，深蓝天空，暖窗灯和路灯倒映水面。"],
  "105": ["photo",9,"散景","失焦光点化为柔和光斑","Please use \"Bokeh\" (ボケ), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #105\n\nWhat it is: Out-of-focus points of light melt into soft discs\nWhat the sample shows: As the aperture opens, the in-focus person stays sharp, the buildings behind soften and the street lamps and distant lights spread into large, pale discs.\nSpec:\n- Scene 2: a street corner; buildings, trees and street lamps (x 114, 292, 494) behind a road at y 132–162; the person stands front left (feet at x 176, y 200, 124 px tall). the background drops to a darker scene (sky #E7E5E1)\n- Background blur (everything but the person): 0 → 6 px\n- Lights: the three lamps (size 1.25) and 12 more spaced 45 px apart (y 44–114, size 0.6–1.2, fixed seed); disc radius = (2.4 + 15 × effect) × size\n- Discs: opacity 100% → 55%, lamps amber #FFC75A, distant lights #FFE3A3, with a 1.2 px amber rim\n- The person stays sharp; top-right aperture f/16 → f/1.4 (8 stops)\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To lift a person or product off the background and add a soft, festive night mood.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/105.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","夜间城市人像，人物清晰，身后街灯形成大圆散景，光圈 f/1.4。"],
  "106": ["photo",10,"移轴效果","通过选择性模糊让实景像微缩模型","Please use \"Tilt-shift\" (ティルトシフト), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #106\n\nWhat it is: Blur top and bottom so a real scene looks like a miniature\nWhat the sample shows: The top and bottom bands of the street blur while only the middle band with the road, the car and the small people stays in focus, so the street looks like a model.\nSpec:\n- The street corner (buildings, trees and lamps behind a road at y 132–162) without the large person; four small people 23–26 px tall stand on the pavement (feet at y 172); the car drives from x −60 to 600 every 5 s\n- Focus band: y 66–176 stays sharp\n- Blur: y 0–42 and y 190–208 go 0 → 7 px; y 42–66 and y 176–190 go 0 → 3 px\n- Dashed lines on the band edges (6 px dash, 5 px gap, #8E8E93 at 75%)\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To make a city or event look like a toy model world.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/106.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","高角度城镇图做移轴效果，仅中间窄带清晰，上下强模糊，颜色鲜艳，像微缩模型。"],
  "107": ["photo",11,"长曝光","延长快门时间，让移动光源留下轨迹","Please use \"Long exposure\" (長時間露光), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #107\n\nWhat it is: Keep the shutter open long so moving lights become lines\nWhat the sample shows: The street turns to night; the moving car fades to almost nothing, a red tail-light line stretches out behind it and white and amber lines run along the opposite lane.\nSpec:\n- Scene 2: a street corner; buildings, trees and street lamps (x 114, 292, 494) behind a road at y 132–162; the person stands front left (feet at x 176, y 200, 124 px tall). colours go to night (sky #2C3B5E, one window in three #FFC75A)\n- Car: x −60 → 600 every 5 s; body opacity 100% → 10%\n- Tail-light line: from x −60 to the car: #FF5B4D 2.6 px at y 145 and #FF8A6E 1.4 px at y 149\n- Opposite lane: full-width lines #FFE9B8 2.6 px at y 135, #FFC75A 1.6 px at y 138.5 and #FFE9B8 1.2 px at y 141.5 (they fade in with the effect)\n- Top-right shutter speed 1/250 → 8″\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To show traffic flow, or silky water and clouds, in a single still.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/107.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","夜间道路用 8 s 长曝光，让车辆消失，只留白色车头灯与红色尾灯轨迹。"],
  "108": ["photo",12,"追随拍摄","跟随运动主体，使背景产生拖影","Please use \"Panning shot\" (流し撮り), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #108\n\nWhat it is: Follow a moving subject so only the background streaks\nWhat the sample shows: The camera follows the moving car: the car stays sharp in the middle of the frame while only the buildings, trees and lamps behind it streak sideways.\nSpec:\n- Street corner: buildings, trees and lamps behind a road at y 132–162 (no large person in front)\n- Car: without the effect it drives from x −80 to 620 in 5 s; with it, it stays at x 270 ±10 px\n- Streak: the background is drawn 12 times spread over 46 px sideways and averaged (spread 0 → 46 px)\n- Wheels: a spoke line turns 12 times per 5 s\n- Top-right shutter speed 1/1000 → 1/15\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To show the speed of a car, bike or runner in a still photo.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/108.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 1/15 s 快门追拍驶过的红车，让车身清晰，身后树木建筑横向拖影。"],
  "109": ["photo",13,"镜头眩光","强光在镜头内产生光环和光斑","Please use \"Lens flare\" (レンズフレア), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #109\n\nWhat it is: Rings and spots of light from a bright source in the lens\nWhat the sample shows: As the sun comes out from behind a building, rays appear around it and a line of light dots, hexagons and a ring runs from the sun through the centre of the frame to the opposite side.\nSpec:\n- Scene 2: a street corner; buildings, trees and street lamps (x 114, 292, 494) behind a road at y 132–162; the person stands front left (feet at x 176, y 200, 124 px tall). \n- Sun: radius 13 px, from behind a building (x 428, y 74) to open sky (x 474, y 30)\n- Rays: 8, from 17 px out from the centre of the sun to 26 px or 44 px, alternating (9 px and 27 px long; amber, 1.6 px, 75%)\n- Flare: on the line from the sun through the centre at t = 0.45, 0.8, 1.15, 1.45, 1.75 and 2.0 (t = 1 is the centre): a 7 px circle, a 13 px hexagon, a 5 px circle, a 22 px hexagon, a 9 px circle and a 30 px ring (3 px line)\n- Colours amber #FFC75A and #FFE3A3 at 40–70% × the effect\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To add glare, summer sunshine or a cinematic light feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/109.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","山景中太阳入画，彩色眩光沿太阳经过画面中心延伸至对侧。"],
  "110": ["photo",14,"鱼眼镜头","超广角使中心鼓起、直线弯曲","Please use \"Fisheye lens\" (魚眼レンズ), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #110\n\nWhat it is: Ultra-wide lens that bulges the centre and bends straight lines\nWhat the sample shows: The middle of the street scene bulges out; the vertical lines of the buildings and the lines of the road bow outward while the corners stay where they are.\nSpec:\n- Scene 2: a street corner; buildings, trees and street lamps (x 114, 292, 494) behind a road at y 132–162; the person stands front left (feet at x 176, y 200, 124 px tall). \n- Warp: a point at distance d from the centre moves to g = (1 + k) / (1 + k·d²/R²) times that distance, R = distance from the centre to a corner (289 px)\n- k: 0 → 1.25; the centre is magnified 2.25×, the corners do not move\n- Every outline is cut every 6 px before warping, so straight lines become curves\n- Top-right focal length 24mm → 8mm\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For bold, playful or peephole-like views (skateboarding, music videos).\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/110.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","城市街道用 180° 鱼眼视角，建筑边缘向外弯曲。"],
  "111": ["photo",15,"色差","高反差边缘出现不同颜色的色边","Please use \"Chromatic aberration\" (色収差), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #111\n\nWhat it is: Red and blue-violet colour fringes along high-contrast edges\nWhat the sample shows: The street scene is split into red, green and blue and the three are laid back together at slightly different sizes, so red and cyan fringes appear on the edges of the person, buildings and lamps, larger towards the sides.\nSpec:\n- Scene 2: a street corner; buildings, trees and street lamps (x 114, 292, 494) behind a road at y 132–162; the person stands front left (feet at x 176, y 200, 124 px tall). \n- Split: the image is multiplied by red #FF0000, green #00FF00 and blue #0000FF into three copies and added back together over black\n- Scale about the centre: red 1 + 2s, green 1 + s, blue 1, with s = 0 → 0.02\n- Offset: red and blue end up about 11 px apart at the left and right edges, 0 at the centre\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To add an imperfect old-lens, VHS or glitch feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/111.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给白色天空前的黑色树枝加上轻微色差，边缘出现红色与蓝紫色的色边，越靠近画面边缘越明显。"],
  "112": ["photo",16,"暗角","画面四角变暗，视线集中到中央","Please use \"Vignette\" (周辺減光（ビネット）), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #112\n\nWhat it is: The corners darken and draw the eye to the centre\nWhat the sample shows: The frame darkens smoothly from the corners while the person and the road in the middle stay bright.\nSpec:\n- Scene 2: a street corner; buildings, trees and street lamps (x 114, 292, 494) behind a road at y 132–162; the person stands front left (feet at x 176, y 200, 124 px tall). \n- Shape: an ellipse centred on the frame (vertical radius = horizontal × 208/539 × 1.35)\n- Clear out to 45% of the 334 px horizontal radius, then rgb(32,35,43) rising from 0% to 70% towards the edge\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To focus attention on the subject, or to suggest an old lens.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/112.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","海滩照片加明显暗角，四角逐渐变暗，将视线引向中央人物。"],
  "113": ["photo",17,"高调","整体明亮、接近白色且阴影很浅","Please use \"High-key\" (ハイキー), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #113\n\nWhat it is: A bright, white-toned image with very light shadows\nWhat the sample shows: The landscape and the person turn to light, near-white colours with very faint shadows, and the hump of the histogram at the bottom right moves to the right end.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Colour: sky #FAF9F7 → #FFFFFF, hills #EAEDF1 → #F5F6F8, figure #4D5A75 → #B9C0CE, shadow #33405A → #A6AEBF, sun #F5A524 → #FFD889\n- Histogram (96×46 px, 20 bars): peak centre 0.56 → 0.85, width 0.2 → 0.09\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For clean, light, gentle product shots and portraits.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/113.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","白桌上的杯瓶静物用高调，纯白背景、极浅阴影，只保留浅色调。"],
  "114": ["photo",18,"低调","以暗色为主，只突出受光部分","Please use \"Low-key\" (ローキー), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #114\n\nWhat it is: A dark image where only the lit parts stand out\nWhat the sample shows: Most of the frame sinks into darkness and the sun goes out; only the right edge of the bust, lit from the side, stays bright. The histogram hump moves to the left end.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Colour: sky #FAF9F7 → #2B2D33, hills → #313339 and #36383E, ground → #24252A, figure → #25272E; the sun and its rings take the sky colour and disappear\n- The lit right edge of the bust stays, #FFC75A → #FFB547\n- Histogram: peak centre 0.56 → 0.14, width 0.2 → 0.08\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For luxurious, tense or mysterious images.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/114.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","黑底威士忌瓶用低调，单侧光，只留受光边缘，大部分画面深黑。"],
  "115": ["photo",19,"黑白","去除颜色，仅保留明暗","Please use \"Black and white\" (モノクロ), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #115\n\nWhat it is: Remove colour and show brightness only\nWhat the sample shows: The colour drains from the same landscape; the sun and the light on the figure turn grey and the shapes read only by their brightness.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Conversion: each colour becomes the grey of its luminance (0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B), contrast ×1.25 around 140\n- For example the figure #4D5A75 → about #4D4D4D, the sun #F5A524 → about #B5B5B5\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For a timeless feel, or when shape, light and expression matter more than colour.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/115.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","海滩快照转黑白，稍提高对比度，保留天空和沙地的明度差。"],
  "116": ["photo",20,"双色调","用一种颜色映射暗部，另一种映射亮部","Please use \"Duotone\" (デュオトーン), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #116\n\nWhat it is: Show the image in two colours, one for darks and one for lights\nWhat the sample shows: The colours of the same landscape are replaced by a range between just two colours: indigo in the darks and pink in the lights.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Two colours: #1F2A5C for the dark end, #FF9FB2 for the light end\n- Conversion: from each colour’s luminance L, t = ((L − 70) / 180)^2.4, and the two colours are mixed by t (this spreads the light tones apart)\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To unify posters, music artwork or social images in brand colours.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/116.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","人像用藏蓝与粉色双色调，暗部藏蓝、亮部粉色，不引入其他颜色。"],
  "117": ["photo",21,"青橙色调","阴影偏青，肤色与高光偏橙","Please use \"Teal and orange\" (ティール＆オレンジ), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #117\n\nWhat it is: Pushes shadows to teal and skin and highlights to orange\nWhat the sample shows: In the same landscape the sky, hills, ground and the shadowed figure shift to teal while the sunlit edge of the figure and the sun shift to orange, a complementary contrast.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Teal: sky #CFE6E3, hills #8CC1BE and #62A2A1, ground #3F8083, trees #2F6A6E, figure #1D4E53\n- Orange: the light on the figure #FF9248, sun #FF8236, sun rings #FFC48C\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For a blockbuster, trailer-like look with strong colour contrast.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/117.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","城市步行人物用电影青橙色调，阴影和天空偏青，皮肤和阳光偏橙。"],
  "118": ["photo",22,"胶片颗粒","画面覆盖细微胶片质感颗粒","Please use \"Film grain\" (フィルムグレイン), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #118\n\nWhat it is: Fine, film-like grain over the image\nWhat the sample shows: Fine grain appears over the whole of the same landscape and the colours lean slightly towards a warm cream.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Grain: 2,600 squares (fixed seed), 0.8–1.7 px; 55% dark #3A3530, 45% white\n- Grain opacity: 16–38% × the effect; the grain does not move (no flicker)\n- Colour: every colour moves 16% towards #F2DDBE\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To remove the clean digital look and add an analogue film texture.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/118.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","海滩照片加细微胶片颗粒，遍布全图，黑位稍抬高并偏暖。"],
  "119": ["photo",23,"漏光","红橙色光像漏入胶片一样侵入画面","Please use \"Light leak\" (ライトリーク), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #119\n\nWhat it is: Red-orange glow as if light leaked onto the film\nWhat the sample shows: From the right edge of the same landscape a band of leaked light comes in, pale yellow on the inside and red at the edge, swaying slowly.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Shape: four tall ellipses centred 30 px outside the right edge (swaying ±6 px over the loop), vertical radius 1.1× the frame height\n- Horizontal radius and colour: 250 px #FFD089 at 35%, 170 px #FF9A3D at 40%, 95 px #FF5A3A at 45%, 45 px #FF3B30 at 50% (each grows from 0 to this radius)\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For nostalgic, summery, accidental-looking memories.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/119.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","夏日回忆照片右边缘漏入红橙色光。"],
  "120": ["photo",24,"双重曝光","两幅影像叠合在同一画面","Please use \"Double exposure\" (二重露光（多重露光）), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #120\n\nWhat it is: Two photos layered into one frame\nWhat the sample shows: The background turns white and the landscape of hills, house, trees and sun appears, scaled down, only inside the shape of the bust.\nSpec:\n- Scene 3: a bust on the left (head centre x 140, y 82, radius 28 px) and hills, a house, trees and the sun (x 432, y 54, radius 15 px) on the right. \n- Background: white #FFFFFF outside the bust\n- Inside the bust: the same landscape at 0.7×, placed so the sun sits at the top right of the head and the ridge of the hills runs across the neck\n- Inside colours: sky #D3DBE6, hills #9AA8BD and #76869F, ground #55647E, trees #3F4C66\n- Transition: the double exposure is laid over the original picture at the effect amount\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For posters and covers that tie a person to a place, a memory or an inner world.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/120.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用双重曝光把森林山景叠在侧脸剪影上：白色背景，只在人物轮廓内显示风景。"],
  "121": ["motion2",1,"预备动作","运动前先向反方向稍稍蓄力","Please use \"Anticipation\" (アンティシペーション), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #121\n\nWhat it is: Pulls back briefly before moving forward\nWhat the sample shows: A square character pulls back against its direction of travel, squashes to wind up, then shoots forward.\nSpec:\n- One move per 2.35 s (twice per 4.7 s: left to right, then right to left). A coral rounded square (86 px, radius 24) with a white arrow. It starts 108 px from the edge; the floor is at y = 178.\n- Wind-up: 0.2–0.95 s, quadratic ease-in-out. It backs off 44 px against the direction of travel, squashes to 1.22 wide × 0.76 tall and leans back 0.18 rad.\n- Launch: 0.95–1.38 s (0.43 s). From the backed-off position to the far end with backOut (s = 1.1), a slight overshoot. In the first 60% of the move it stretches up to 1.55 wide × 0.72 tall (half sine) and leans forward 0.08 rad.\n- Landing: from 1.38 s, width and height wobble in opposite directions by 0.13·e^(−7t)·sin(17t).\n- At launch, three dust puffs at the start point (gone within the first 70% of the move) and three yellow speed lines (width 8) behind it.\nWhen to use it: Use it just before a jump, dash or launch to give the move build-up and weight.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/121.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","按钮向右飞出前加上预备动作：先用 0.3 s 向反方向稍稍后拉并压扁，再飞出去。"],
  "122": ["motion2",2,"跟随动作","主体停下后，局部仍延迟摆动","Please use \"Follow-through\" (フォロースルー), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #122\n\nWhat it is: Parts keep swinging after the body stops\nWhat the sample shows: A round character slides in and stops suddenly; only the flag on its head and its tail keep swinging, then settle.\nSpec:\n- One move per 2.35 s (twice per 4.7 s, alternating direction). The body is a mint circle (radius 38). It travels 303 px at 0.15–0.85 s: it speeds up over the first 30%, then keeps a constant speed and stops abruptly at 0.85 s.\n- Flag (58 px white pole with a yellow flag): its angle is a spring pushed by the body's acceleration, a″ = −121a − 5.5a′ − 0.0175 × acceleration (natural frequency 11 rad/s). The cloth bends a further 0.6 × the pole angle.\n- Tail: seven 14 px segments (coral, width 14→6) on a slower spring, b″ = −56b − 2.8b′ − 0.012 × acceleration. Segment j uses the value from j × 22/600 s (about 0.037 s) earlier, scaled by (0.55 + 0.16j).\n- Both springs are precomputed in 1/600 s steps; drawing only looks values up.\n- In the last 0.3 s of each move the swing is faded to 0 with smoothstep, so the loop has no seam.\nWhen to use it: Use it on hair, clothes, accessories or the trim of a logo, so that the parts attached to the main body feel weighted.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/122.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","角色停下后，给头发和旗子加上跟随动作：延迟约 0.5 s 继续摆动，然后停稳。"],
  "123": ["motion2",3,"弹跳","落下后越弹越低直至停下","Please use \"Bounce\" (バウンス), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #123\n\nWhat it is: Falls and bounces lower until it stops\nWhat the sample shows: A ball drops and bounces lower each time until it comes to rest.\nSpec:\n- One drop per 2.35 s (twice per 4.7 s: yellow first, then coral). The ball has radius 26.\n- From 0.1 s it falls from 190 px above the floor. Gravity 1900 px/s²; each bounce keeps 56% of the speed (restitution 0.56); it stops when the rebound speed is below 35 px/s.\n- Sideways it moves x = 150→390 over 0.1–1.8 s with cubic ease-out.\n- Squash for 0.045 s either side of each impact: width 1 + sq, height 1 − sq, with sq up to 0.4 × min(1, impact speed ÷ 850). Impacts faster than 200 px/s flick short white lines left and right for 0.3 s.\n- The shadow gets smaller with height. Exit: 1.95–2.25 s, scale multiplied by (1 − backIn, s = 2).\nWhen to use it: Use it whenever something drops and lands: an icon, a word or a product that should feel heavy and springy.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/123.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让球从上方落下并弹跳：弹 3 次，一次比一次低。"],
  "124": ["motion2",4,"随机抖动","小幅、随机地持续晃动","Please use \"Wiggle\" (ウィグル), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #124\n\nWhat it is: Shakes in small, random, continuous jitters\nWhat the sample shows: A bell keeps jittering irregularly: not one hit, but a small shake that never stops.\nSpec:\n- A yellow bell pivoting at its top (centre, y = 34). It never stops moving.\n- Angle = the sum of four sine waves: 23, 31, 43 and 59 cycles per 4.7 s (about 4.9, 6.6, 9.1 and 12.6 Hz), amplitudes 0.085, 0.065, 0.05 and 0.035 rad (up to about 0.235 rad, 13.5°, when they line up).\n- Position also jitters: x with 29, 47 and 61 cycles (4, 3, 2 px), y with 37 and 53 cycles (2.4, 1.8 px).\n- Every frequency is a whole number of cycles per 4.7 s, so the loop joins up; the counts share no common factor, so it does not look regular.\n- The clapper (coral, radius 13) swings the other way (angle × 70 px). White vibration arcs (radius 86 and 110, width 6) flicker on both sides the whole time.\nWhen to use it: Use it on a notification, an incoming call or anything that should catch the eye, or to add a restless, handheld feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/124.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给通知铃铛加上轻微的随机抖动，角度最大约 10°，响铃期间一直持续。"],
  "125": ["motion2",5,"脉冲动画","像心跳一样有节奏地缩放","Please use \"Pulse\" (パルス), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #125\n\nWhat it is: Its size throbs like a heartbeat\nWhat the sample shows: A heart throbs like a heartbeat, a double beat each time, with rings spreading out.\nSpec:\n- A coral heart. One beat per 1.175 s (four per 4.7 s); each beat is a double \"lub-dub\".\n- Scale = 1 + 0.26·G(0.2 s, width 0.065) + 0.15·G(0.44 s, width 0.07), where G = e^(−((t − centre) ÷ width)²): a quick swell that drops straight back.\n- Two heart-shaped outlines spread from 0.16 s and 0.40 s: scale 1.2→2.4 over 0.8 s, cubic ease-out.\n- As they spread, their opacity goes 0.75→0 (the second at 60%) and the line width 8.5→1.5 px.\nWhen to use it: Use it for a like, a recording or live indicator, or a button you want pressed, to make it feel alive.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/125.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给爱心图标加上脉冲动画：每 1.2 s 放大约 10% 再恢复原样。"],
  "126": ["motion2",6,"运动路径","沿设定的曲线移动","Please use \"Motion path\" (モーションパス), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #126\n\nWhat it is: Moves along a curve that you define\nWhat the sample shows: A paper plane follows a dotted path, turning as it goes and looping the loop on the way.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 4.7 s, from off-screen left to off-screen right. The path is x = 270 + 112θ − 150·sinθ, y = 106 − 74·cosθ for θ = −π→π, which makes a loop at the top centre.\n- θ advances in proportion to time (so the speed along the path is not constant; the loop looks slower).\n- The plane turns to the path direction: angle = atan2(74·sinθ, 112 − 150·cosθ).\n- The path is shown in advance as a dotted line (width 6, dash 2/15). A mint trail of 24 segments (0.03 in θ each) follows, thinner and fainter towards the back.\nWhen to use it: Use it whenever something should follow a set route: a flying object, a car, a journey on a map.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/126.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让纸飞机沿这条曲线的运动路径在 4 s 内飞完，机头始终朝向前进方向。"],
  "127": ["motion2",7,"往返循环","正放后倒放，反复来回","Please use \"Ping-pong loop\" (ピンポンループ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #127\n\nWhat it is: Plays forward, then backward, over and over\nWhat the sample shows: A square travels to one end, then comes back along the same path as if played in reverse, again and again.\nSpec:\n- One round trip per 4.7 s: 2.35 s forward, then the same motion played backwards for 2.35 s (progress g goes 0→1→0, linear).\n- A mint rounded square (48 px, radius 13) hops from x = 92 to 447 along three arches of height 62·|sin(3πg)|, turning one full turn with g.\n- Four ghost copies, 0.045 s apart, opacity 0.1–0.4.\n- A playback bar below: blue with a play label while going forward, coral with a reverse label while going back. The progress bar and its knob follow g.\n- Vertical posts mark the two turning points.\nWhen to use it: Use it for loaders, idle animations and any move that should repeat back and forth without a cut.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/127.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让加载圆点以往返循环左右来回移动，单程 1 s。"],
  "128": ["motion2",8,"定格动画风格","抽帧后动作一顿一顿","Please use \"Stop-motion style\" (ストップモーション風), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #128\n\nWhat it is: Moves in choppy steps, with frames dropped\nWhat the sample shows: A star hops across in choppy steps at about 8 frames per second, each frame slightly off.\nSpec:\n- 38 frames per 4.7 s (about 8 per second, each held for about 0.124 s). Only those frames are drawn; nothing is drawn in between.\n- A yellow star (radius 38) hops from x = −44 to 583 along three arches of height 54·|sin(3πt)|, turning twice.\n- Each frame gets a fixed random jitter: position ±5 px across and ±4.5 px up and down, rotation ±0.15 rad, size ±5%.\n- The previous two frames stay faintly visible (opacity 0.28 and 0.12), like onion skin.\n- Black film-strip bands top and bottom (26 px each, with sprocket holes) and a frames-per-second label.\nWhen to use it: Use it for a handmade, claymation or collage look, when smooth motion feels too slick.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/128.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把这段动作做成定格动画风格：每秒 8 帧，每帧位置都轻微错开。"],
  "129": ["motion2",9,"文字乱码效果","字符随机变换后定格为正确文字","Please use \"Text scramble\" (テキストスクランブル), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #129\n\nWhat it is: Letters shuffle at random, then settle\nWhat the sample shows: Random characters keep changing, then lock into the right word from left to right.\nSpec:\n- \"HELLO\" in the first 2.35 s, \"WORLD\" in the second. Five monospaced letters (92 px).\n- Unsettled slots show random characters from A–Z (without I and O), 0–9 and #$%&@?, changing 76 times per 4.7 s (about every 0.062 s), mint at 75% opacity.\n- Slots lock from left to right: slot i at 0.45 + 0.18i s (the last at 1.17 s). A newly locked letter is yellow for 0.22 s, then white, settling with scale 1 + 0.2·e^(−14t).\n- From 1.85 s the slots return to random from right to left (slot i at 1.85 + 0.08 × (4 − i) s).\n- A bar under each slot: blue when locked, yellow for the next one to lock, navy otherwise.\nWhen to use it: Use it to bring in a headline, a number or a code name with a decoding, hacker or tech feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/129.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让标题以文字乱码效果出现：随机字符变换约 1 s，再从左到右依次定格。"],
  "130": ["motion2",10,"波浪文字","文字像波浪一样依次上下起伏","Please use \"Wave text\" (ウェーブテキスト), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #130\n\nWhat it is: Letters rise and fall in turn, like a wave\nWhat the sample shows: The letters of \"WAVE TEXT\" rise and fall one after another, like a wave.\nSpec:\n- \"WAVE TEXT\" (70 px, bold, 4 px letter spacing). Three waves per 4.7 s (1.567 s per wave).\n- Vertical offset of letter i = −28·sin(φ − 0.62i), with φ = 2π × 3 × time ÷ 4.7 (each letter lags the previous by 0.62 rad).\n- Rising letters stretch vertically (1 + 0.06·s) and shift from white towards yellow (s is the sine value, clamped to 0–1 for the colour).\n- A shadow ellipse under each letter shrinks as the letter rises.\nWhen to use it: Use it on a logo, a short heading or a caption timed to music, to add fun and rhythm.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/130.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让标志的文字做波浪文字动画：每个字依次错开，上下起伏约 20 px。"],
  "131": ["motion2",11,"路径文字","文字沿线条或曲线流动","Please use \"Text on a path\" (テキストオンパス), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #131\n\nWhat it is: Text flows along a line or curve\nWhat the sample shows: A line of text flows along a wavy line, each letter turning to follow it.\nSpec:\n- Path: y = 118 + 42·sin(2πx ÷ 330 + 0.6) for x = −70 to 609, shown 6 px below as a navy dashed line (14/10, width 5).\n- \"ALONG THE LINE • \" (42 px, bold, 2 px letter spacing) is repeated. Each character is placed at its arc-length position on the path and rotated to the path direction.\n- The text moves along the path by the length of one copy of the string every 4.7 s, so the loop joins up.\n- Letters are white; the bullet is yellow.\nWhen to use it: Use it to run text along a shape: around a logo, along a road, river or wave, or as a looping band of text.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/131.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把宣传语做成路径文字，沿波浪线从左向右流动，每 5 s 走完一轮。"],
  "132": ["motion2",12,"可变字体动画","文字粗细平滑变化","Please use \"Variable font animation\" (可変フォントアニメーション), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #132\n\nWhat it is: The weight of the letters changes smoothly\nWhat the sample shows: The same word goes smoothly from thin to very bold and back, with a slider below showing the weight.\nSpec:\n- \"MOTION\" (112 px, system-ui, 2 px letter spacing). The weight goes back and forth twice per 4.7 s: v = 0.5 − 0.5·cos(2π × 2 × time ÷ 4.7), which eases at both ends.\n- Weight = round(100 + 800v), from 100 to 900, set directly as the font weight.\n- A slider below (x = 112→427, y = 180) labelled thin on the left and bold on the right. The knob (yellow, radius 14) follows v, with the current weight shown above it.\nWhen to use it: Use it on a title, a logo or a single word to show loudness or emotion through the letters themselves.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/132.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给标题加上可变字体动画：1 s 内从 Thin 变到 Black（字重 100 到 900）。"],
  "133": ["motion2",13,"文字遮罩","镂空成文字形状，透出内部画面","Please use \"Text mask\" (テキストマスク), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #133\n\nWhat it is: Letters cut out to show a picture inside\nWhat the sample shows: Heavy letters are cut out so that a moving seascape shows only inside them; near the end of the cycle the whole picture appears.\nSpec:\n- \"OCEAN\" (weight 900, system-ui, 2 px letter spacing). The font size starts at 172 px and drops 2 px at a time until the word is at most 500 px wide.\n- The scene inside keeps moving: coral sky, a yellow sun bobbing ±6 px, blue sea below y = 116 with four white wavy lines drifting 240 px per 4.7 s in alternating directions, a sailboat crossing once per 4.7 s, clouds drifting 60 px.\n- Method: draw the word on an offscreen canvas, then composite the scene onto it with source-in, so the scene remains only inside the letters. A white 4 px outline around the letters.\n- Outside the letters the scene shows at 12% opacity; it rises to 100% at 3.45–3.85 s and returns to 12% at 4.25–4.65 s (smoothstep).\nWhen to use it: Use it to show a photo or footage inside a title or brand name, putting the word and the picture together.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/133.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把“OCEAN”做成文字遮罩，里面透出海浪视频，最后 1 s 显示完整画面。"],
  "134": ["motion2",14,"中继器","复制图形并排列旋转","Please use \"Repeater\" (リピーター), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #134\n\nWhat it is: Duplicates a shape and turns the copies\nWhat the sample shows: One shape is duplicated around a circle, and the copies turn and pulse slightly out of step.\nSpec:\n- A rounded bar (24 × 60, radius 12) is copied up to 12 times around a circle of radius 58 at the centre, each turned to face outward (angle + 90°).\n- Count: 1→12 at 0.35–1.7 s and 12→1 at 3.6–4.45 s (quadratic ease-in-out). Each new copy slides from the previous slot to its own, 30° further on (cubic ease-out).\n- The whole ring turns once per 4.7 s. Each copy pulses in size by 1 ± 0.22 twice per 4.7 s, each one 0.55 rad later than the last, so a ripple runs round the ring.\n- Colours go blue, coral, yellow, mint. The original copy has a white outline. A \"×N\" counter at the top right.\nWhen to use it: Use it for loaders, background patterns, flowers or rays: anything built from one shape repeated.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/134.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用中继器把这片花瓣复制成 12 片排成圆形，每 4 s 旋转一圈。"],
  "135": ["motion2",15,"万花筒","像万花筒一样对称展开","Please use \"Kaleidoscope\" (カレイドスコープ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #135\n\nWhat it is: Mirrored patterns spread out symmetrically\nWhat the sample shows: An 8-way symmetrical pattern turns and spreads out from the centre, like a kaleidoscope.\nSpec:\n- The area around the centre is split into eight 45° wedges; every other wedge is drawn mirrored, giving eight mirror-symmetric sections.\n- One wedge holds 13 shapes (circles, diamonds, triangles; four colours; fixed random seed). They travel outward from the centre to radius 300, one full radius per 4.7 s, wrapping back to the centre.\n- Shapes grow as they go out ((5 + 0.1r) × 0.7–1.4) and spin 0.02 rad per px. They fade in over the first 30 px and out over the last 70 px; each sways ±0.08 rad once per 4.7 s.\n- The whole pattern turns 90° per 4.7 s (two wedges, so the loop joins up).\n- A white eight-point star at the centre (radius 20 ± 4, pulsing twice per 4.7 s).\nWhen to use it: Use it for music videos, live backdrops or dreamy scene changes, wherever a pattern has to hold up on repeat.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/135.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","在标志背后加入万花筒效果：8 等分镜像对称，一边缓慢旋转一边向外展开。"],
  "136": ["motion2",16,"线条抖动","手绘线条逐帧轻微抖动","Please use \"Line boil\" (ラインボイル), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #136\n\nWhat it is: Hand-drawn lines wobble frame to frame\nWhat the sample shows: A hand-drawn line picture wobbles every few frames while the picture itself stays still.\nSpec:\n- A still line drawing (a yellow star, a white cloud, mint sparkle strokes, a faint ground line). Line widths 6–8, round caps.\n- The drawing does not move. 47 times per 4.7 s (about every 0.1 s) every point is redrawn with a fixed random offset of up to ±3.5 px in x and in y.\n- Each line is first turned into a row of points (every 6–13 px; 96 points round the cloud) and drawn as quadratic curves through the midpoints between them, so it wobbles like hand-drawn frames.\n- The offsets are a hash of the frame number and the point number, so the same frame always looks the same.\nWhen to use it: Use it on hand-drawn illustrations, icons or lettering to make even a still picture feel drawn by hand.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/136.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给手绘插画加上线条抖动：每秒 10 帧，线条只偏移 2–3 px。"],
  "137": ["motion2",17,"推入转场","下一画面把当前画面推出","Please use \"Push transition\" (プッシュ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #137\n\nWhat it is: The next scene pushes the current one out\nWhat the sample shows: The next scene slides in from the side and pushes the current one out with it.\nSpec:\n- Sea scene → mountain scene → sea scene, 2.35 s each. The change runs at 0.45–1.6 s of each half (1.15 s), cubic ease-in-out.\n- The two scenes stay joined and move together by the full frame width (539 px); no overlap and no fade.\n- Direction: sea→mountain moves left (the next scene enters from the right); mountain→sea moves right.\n- A navy line (width 6) marks the seam between the two scenes.\nWhen to use it: Use it to step through slides, photos or steps, when the change should feel continuous and moving forward.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/137.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用推入转场切到下一张幻灯片，从右侧在 0.8 s 内推入。"],
  "138": ["motion2",18,"百叶窗转场","从细条缝隙中打开下一画面","Please use \"Blinds transition\" (ブラインド), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #138\n\nWhat it is: The next scene opens through thin strips\nWhat the sample shows: Gaps in a row of thin strips widen until the next scene is fully open.\nSpec:\n- Day scene → night scene → day, 2.35 s each. Seven horizontal strips (208 ÷ 7 ≈ 29.7 px each).\n- 0.4–1.65 s (1.25 s), quadratic ease-in-out: in every strip at once, the next scene is revealed from the strip's top edge downward, opening from 0 to the full strip height.\n- The previous scene stays underneath. Neither picture moves.\nWhen to use it: Use it for a clear switch between two scenes, such as day and night or before and after, or for a retro feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/138.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用百叶窗转场切换场景：7 条横向条带，在 1 s 内打开。"],
  "139": ["motion2",19,"立方体转场","像立方体旋转一样切换画面","Please use \"Cube transition\" (キューブ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #139\n\nWhat it is: Changes scenes like a turning cube\nWhat the sample shows: Like a turning cube, the front face swings away and the next face comes round.\nSpec:\n- Face A (an \"A\" on coral) and face B (a \"B\" on mint), each 250 × 146. 2.35 s each, A→B→A.\n- Rotation 0→90° at 0.45–1.6 s (1.15 s), cubic ease-in-out, around a vertical axis through the centre of the cube (depth equal to the face width, 250).\n- Perspective: camera distance 820 px. Each face is drawn as 2 px vertical slices, each sized and placed by its perspective factor.\n- The face turning away darkens up to 55% (0.55·sinφ); the incoming face starts 55% dark and brightens (0.55·cosφ). The floor shadow follows the visible width.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show products, plans or screens one after another with a sense of depth.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/139.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","商品照片用立方体转场切换，向左转 90°，时长 0.8 s。"],
  "140": ["motion2",20,"翻页转场","像纸张一样卷起，翻到下一页","Please use \"Page curl\" (ページめくり), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #140\n\nWhat it is: Peels back like paper to show the next page\nWhat the sample shows: A page peels back from its corner and folds over, revealing the next page beneath.\nSpec:\n- Page 1 (white) → page 2 (cream) → page 1, 2.35 s each. The curl starts at the bottom-right corner, 0.35–1.75 s (1.4 s), quadratic ease-in-out.\n- The fold line moves from the corner in the direction (−1, −0.42), normalised, by 0→600 px.\n- The part beyond the fold line is mirrored across it to form the flap, the back of the page (light grey or beige), with a drop shadow (blur 14, offset 4, 4) and a white 2 px edge.\n- The next page shows where the paper has lifted, with a 50 px shadow gradient along the fold.\nWhen to use it: Use it for books, catalogues, albums or chapter breaks, where a paper feel or reading on suits the content.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/140.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用翻页转场进入下一章，从右下角在 1.2 s 内翻起。"],
  "141": ["motion2",21,"像素化转场","马赛克逐渐变粗后切换画面","Please use \"Pixelate\" (ピクセレート), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #141\n\nWhat it is: Turns into coarse blocks, then switches\nWhat the sample shows: The picture turns into coarser and coarser blocks, switches at the coarsest point, then sharpens again.\nSpec:\n- Field scene → city scene → field, 2.35 s each. At 0.2–1.9 s (1.7 s) the block size steps up and back down through 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 11, 15, 20, 27 and 36 px (coarsest at the midpoint, 1.05 s).\n- The first half shows the old scene and the second half the new one; the swap happens at the coarsest step.\n- Method: shrink the frame to width ÷ block size with smoothing on, then scale it back up with smoothing off.\nWhen to use it: Use it for game-like, retro or digital scene changes, or to blur something out as the scene switches.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/141.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用像素化转场切换：0.6 s 内马赛克逐渐变粗，在最粗时切到下一画面。"],
  "142": ["motion2",22,"玻璃碎裂","像玻璃一样碎裂，碎片飞散","Please use \"Shatter\" (ガラス割れ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #142\n\nWhat it is: Breaks like glass and the shards fly off\nWhat the sample shows: The picture cracks like glass, the shards fly off and the next scene is revealed.\nSpec:\n- Mountain scene → day scene → mountain, 2.35 s each. The impact point is (304, 92).\n- Cracks: 0.3–0.65 s. Thirteen radial lines and rings at radii of about 40, 98 and 175 (each ±15%) appear in order of distance from the centre (cubic ease-out, out to 420 px). A white flash star at the centre fades by 0.6 s.\n- The glass breaks at 0.82 s: 52 shards (13 × 4 rings) cut from the old scene fly outward at 220–480 px/s (vertical speed × 0.7, plus up to 120 upward), with gravity 1300 px/s², spinning ±4 rad/s and shrinking up to 35% over 1 s.\n- Outer rings leave later (0.035 s per ring plus up to 0.03 s at random). Each shard fades out 0.55–1.0 s after it starts moving.\n- Shards have a white 2.5 px edge; the next scene is underneath.\nWhen to use it: Use it for an impact, a break or a twist, just before a title or a result that should hit hard.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/142.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","标题出现前，用玻璃碎裂打碎前一画面：先出现裂纹，碎片再在约 1 s 内落下。"],
  "143": ["motion2",23,"爆炸图","零件分离，展示内部结构","Please use \"Exploded view\" (分解図), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #143\n\nWhat it is: Parts separate to show the structure inside\nWhat the sample shows: A phone separates into its layers to show how it is built, then assembles again.\nSpec:\n- An isometric phone built from four layers (back cover, battery, circuit board, screen). Each layer is a flat rounded plate drawn on axes scaled by 0.85 and tilted 30° either way, with 6 px thick sides.\n- Separate: from 0.45 s, 0.75 s per layer, each layer 0.08 s after the one below, backOut (s = 1.3). Height of layer i (0–3 from the bottom) = 7i + 30i × progress, so the back cover stays put.\n- While apart, each layer bobs ±3 px twice per 4.7 s, dotted guide lines join the corners, and name labels with leader lines appear on the right (in Japanese in the demo).\n- Reassemble: from 3.25 s, 0.7 s per layer, starting with the top layer, 0.07 s apart, cubic ease-in-out.\nWhen to use it: Use it to explain what is inside a product, how it works or what it is made of, at a glance.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/143.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","展示产品的爆炸图：4 个零件在 1 s 内分开，并分别标上名称。"],
  "144": ["motion2",24,"分屏","分割画面，同时展示多个场景","Please use \"Split screen\" (スプリットスクリーン), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #144\n\nWhat it is: Divides the frame to show scenes side by side\nWhat the sample shows: One full-frame scene splits into two panels, then three, each with its own scene moving.\nSpec:\n- A full-frame sea scene splits into two panels at 0.45–0.95 s (divider 539→269.5), then into three at 1.4–1.9 s (dividers at 1/3 and 2/3), and merges back into one at 3.75–4.4 s, all cubic ease-in-out.\n- The three scenes (sea, city, field) are each centred in and clipped to their own panel and keep moving inside it (waves and a sailboat, city windows switching 8 times per 4.7 s, a windmill turning twice per 4.7 s).\n- White dividers (width 6) between the panels.\nWhen to use it: Use it to compare, to show things happening at once, or to line up several people or places, such as before and after or a set of options.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/144.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用分屏同时展示三个场景：从一个画面分成两个，再分成三个，每步 0.5 s。"],
  "145": ["lp2",1,"滚动时间轴","滚动时时间轴的线条随之延伸","Please use \"Timeline on scroll\" (タイムラインアニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #145\n\nWhat it is: A timeline line grows as you scroll\nWhat the sample shows: As the page scrolls down, an orange line grows down the timeline; each dot it reaches fills in and its year and event slide in from the right. Scrolling back up reverses it.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 browser viewport. Scroll: 0→190 px over 0.3–2.3 s, 190→0 over 3.0–4.3 s (cubic ease-in-out). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- The timeline line is at x = 168: an orange line grows over a gray track (width 3). Its tip sits at scroll + 126 px, so always 126 px from the top of the viewport (42 px from the bottom).\n- Five items (2018–2026), with dots (white, radius 7.5, ring width 2.5) at page y = 72, 126, 180, 234 and 288.\n- Over the 22 px of line growth after the tip passes a dot (cubic ease-out): the ring turns orange, an inner dot grows from radius 0 to 4, and the year (18 px, orange) and event (15 px) fade in while sliding 16 px from the right.\n- Scrolling back shrinks the line and hides the items by the same formula. The scrollbar thumb on the right follows the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it for company history, milestones or a step-by-step process that reads in time order.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/145.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把公司沿革做成滚动时间轴：竖线随滚动延伸，线到达哪一年就依次显示该年内容。"],
  "146": ["lp2",2,"滚动文字显现","随着阅读，文字逐字变深","Please use \"Scroll text reveal\" (スクロールテキストリビール), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #146\n\nWhat it is: Text darkens letter by letter as you scroll\nWhat the sample shows: A light gray headline darkens one character at a time from the top left as the page scrolls, and fades back from the end when scrolling up.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport. Scroll progress p: 0→1 over 0.3–2.6 s, 1→0 over 3.2–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out). The page moves up by p × 40 px. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- A three-line headline, 24 characters in all (27 px, weight 800, 38 px line height), all light gray (#D6DBE4) at the start.\n- Character n (counting from 0) has darkness clamp(p × 26 − n): each character takes 1/26 of the progress to reach the text color (#1C2333), in step with the scroll.\n- Scrolling back fades them from the last character by the same formula. The body-text bars and the scrollbar thumb move with the page.\nWhen to use it: Use it on a short statement, such as a concept or a message from the founder, that should be read slowly.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/146.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给理念文案加上滚动文字显现：初始为浅灰色，随滚动逐字加深。"],
  "147": ["lp2",3,"堆叠卡片","滚动时卡片层层叠起","Please use \"Stacking cards\" (スタッキングカード), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #147\n\nWhat it is: Cards stack on top of each other on scroll\nWhat the sample shows: On scroll, the next card rises from below and stacks over the previous one with a small offset; the cards underneath shrink a little and darken.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport. Scroll step s: 0→1 over 0.3–1.1 s, 1→2 over 1.6–2.4 s, 2→0 over 3.2–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Three cards (371 × 124, radius 12, centered), 170 px apart on the page; each step of s moves them up 170 px.\n- They stop 14, 26 and 38 px from the top (position: sticky with the top offset 12 px larger for each card), so each new card covers the one before.\n- For each card stacked on top, the card underneath shrinks 4.5% (9% for two) around the middle of its top edge and darkens under a navy layer (up to 16%).\n- Card shadow: 14 px blur, 2 px upward. The scrollbar thumb follows the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it for steps, features or plans that should be shown one card at a time, in order.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/147.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把服务的三个步骤做成堆叠卡片：滚动时下一张从下方升起，每张比前一张错开 12 px 叠上去。"],
  "148": ["lp2",4,"滚动切换背景色","按区块切换页面背景色","Please use \"Background color change on scroll\" (背景色の切り替え), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #148\n\nWhat it is: The page background changes color by section\nWhat the sample shows: Each time the scroll moves into a new section, the whole page background blends from cream to navy to light blue; on the dark background the text turns white.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with three sections, each 168 px (one screen). Scroll: 0→168 px over 0.3–1.2 s, 168→336 over 1.8–2.7 s, 336→0 over 3.3–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Background colors: morning #FFEBD9 → night #1E2A4A → holiday #DDE6FF, painted as one color behind the whole page and blended while crossing a section boundary.\n- Blend: 0→1 between 5% and 95% of the scroll to the next section (quadratic ease-in-out), driven by scroll position, not by time.\n- Toward night the headline blends from navy to white and the body bars from beige to blue-gray; the section labels (01 MORNING …) stay orange.\n- Each section's picture (sun, moon and stars, mountain photo) moves with the page. The scrollbar thumb follows the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it on story-style pages where each chapter has its own mood, or to contrast scenes such as day and night or the seasons.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/148.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给各区块加上滚动切换背景色：滚动时从早晨区块的奶油色平滑过渡到夜晚的藏蓝色，再到假日的浅蓝色。"],
  "149": ["lp2",5,"滚动隐藏页头","向下滚动时隐藏，向上滚动时出现","Please use \"Hide-on-scroll header\" (隠れるヘッダー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #149\n\nWhat it is: Hides on scroll down, returns on scroll up\nWhat the sample shows: Scrolling down slides the header up out of view to free the screen; scrolling up even a little brings it straight back.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with a 34 px header fixed at the top. Scroll: 0→170 px over 0.3–1.1 s (down), 170→100 over 1.5–1.9 s (up), 100→230 over 2.4–2.9 s (down), 230→0 over 3.3–4.3 s (up), each with cubic ease-in-out. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- If the last movement was downward the header hides; if upward it shows. Within 34 px of the top of the page it always shows.\n- Hiding and showing both move it 36 px upward over 0.3 s (quadratic ease-in-out), like transform: translateY with a transition.\n- While scrolled, a 12 px shadow sits under the header (opacity 0→0.14 over the first 30 px of scroll). The scrollbar thumb follows the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it when screen space is tight, as on phones, to give the content more room while keeping the menu one small scroll away.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/149.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把页头做成滚动隐藏页头：向下滚动时用 0.3 s 向上隐藏，只要稍微向上滚动就重新出现。"],
  "150": ["lp2",6,"滚动监听","目录高亮当前阅读的章节","Please use \"Scrollspy\" (スクロールスパイ), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #150\n\nWhat it is: Highlights the current section in the menu\nWhat the sample shows: As the article scrolls, the table-of-contents item for the section being read lights up, and the highlight moves on when the next heading comes in.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport: a table of contents on the left (150 px wide, 4 items) and the article on the right, with headings 100 px apart. Scroll: 0→100 over 0.3–0.9 s, →200 over 1.35–1.95 s, →300 over 2.4–3.0 s, 300→0 over 3.5–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Current item = the last heading whose top is above scroll + 40 px (a trigger line 40 px below the top of the viewport).\n- When it changes, over 0.25 s (cubic ease-out) the item gets a pale orange background (126 × 26, radius 6) and an orange bar on its left (width 4), and its text turns from gray to bold orange; the previous item reverts over the same 0.25 s.\n- The table of contents stays put; only the article scrolls. The scrollbar thumb follows the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it on long articles, documentation or FAQs to show where the reader is within the whole page.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/150.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给文章目录加上滚动监听：当前阅读章节的条目显示为朱红色，切换用时 0.25 s。"],
  "151": ["lp2",7,"回到顶部按钮","往下滚动后出现，点击回到顶部","Please use \"Back-to-top button\" (トップへ戻るボタン), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #151\n\nWhat it is: Appears lower down and returns you to the top\nWhat the sample shows: After scrolling down, a round arrow button appears at the bottom right; clicking it takes the page straight back to the top.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport. Scroll 0→300 px (to the bottom of the page) over 0.2–1.7 s, cubic ease-in-out. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Button: an orange circle at the bottom right (center x = 472, y = 138; radius 19; white up arrow; 10 px shadow blur). Between 80 and 140 px of scroll it fades in while rising 10 px (cubic ease-out).\n- It is clicked at 2.6 s. While the cursor is on it, it darkens over 0.2 s (#FF5A2C → #D9431C).\n- After the click the scroll goes 300→0 over 2.66–3.26 s (0.6 s, cubic ease-in-out); below 80 px the button fades out by the same formula.\nWhen to use it: Use it on long pages such as blog posts, long landing pages or product lists, so readers can get back to the menu at the top.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/151.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给文章页加上回到顶部按钮：稍微滚动后显示在右下角，点击后用 0.6 s 滚回顶部。"],
  "152": ["lp2",8,"滚动放大","图片随滚动放大至铺满屏幕","Please use \"Zoom on scroll\" (スクロールで拡大), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #152\n\nWhat it is: An image grows to fill the screen as you scroll\nWhat the sample shows: As the page scrolls, a small photo in the middle grows to fill the window, the text around it fades away and a headline appears over the photo.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport. Scroll progress p: 0→1 over 0.3–2.3 s, 1→0 over 3.0–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Photo frame: from 155 × 90 in the middle (x = 178, y = 58, radius 8) to the full 511 × 168 window (radius 0); position, width, height and radius change in proportion to p.\n- The heading and text around it fade out while p goes 0→0.45 (opacity 1 − 2.2p).\n- While p goes 0.7→1, a white headline (26 px, 2 px letter spacing) fades in at the center of the photo. The scrollbar thumb follows the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it on travel, real-estate or brand sites to pull the visitor into the photo.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/152.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","首屏照片做成滚动放大：中央的小照片随滚动放大到铺满视口，完全展开后叠上标题。"],
  "153": ["lp2",9,"3D 倾斜","卡片随光标方向立体倾斜","Please use \"3D tilt on hover\" (3Dチルト), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #153\n\nWhat it is: The card tilts in 3D following the cursor\nWhat the sample shows: As the cursor moves over the card, the card tilts in depth to match the cursor position and a glare moves across its surface; it settles flat when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with a 220 × 132 card (radius 14) in the middle. The cursor comes in, visits points near the card's corners every 0.6 s and leaves (cubic ease-in-out). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Tilt: the cursor offset from the card center is divided by half the width and height to give −1…1; the horizontal offset × 0.32 rad (about 18°) is the rotation about Y, the vertical offset × 0.32 rad the rotation about X. The side under the cursor tips away.\n- Depth: viewer distance 520 px (like perspective: 520px); nearer parts are drawn larger.\n- On hover the tilt and glare ramp up over 0.4 s (cubic ease-out); on leave the card returns flat over the same 0.4 s.\n- Glare: a white radial light of radius 130 px at the cursor (opacity 0.42 at the center). The floor shadow shifts up to 10 px against the tilt.\nWhen to use it: Use it on member cards, product packaging or pricing cards to make them feel like objects you can pick up.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/153.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给会员卡加上 3D 倾斜：随光标位置最大倾斜 18°，反光也跟着移动。"],
  "154": ["lp2",10,"聚光灯悬停","只有光标周围变亮","Please use \"Spotlight hover\" (スポットライトホバー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #154\n\nWhat it is: Only the area around the cursor lights up\nWhat the sample shows: As the cursor moves over the dark cards, only a circle around it is lit, and the edges of nearby cards glow.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport: a dark page (#121828) with three dark cards (147 × 116, radius 10). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- The cursor keeps moving in a figure eight: x = 255 + 190·sin(2πt/4.7), y = 92 + 40·sin(4πt/4.7).\n- Inside each card only, a white radial light of radius 115 px is centered on the cursor (opacity 0.34 at the center → 0); it does not spill outside the cards.\n- Card borders (width 2) glow by distance from the cursor: an orange radial light (rgb(255,122,82)) of radius 120 px. Far edges keep only the faint base line (8% white).\n- No lag: the light sits exactly at the cursor (the usual build puts the coordinates in CSS variables used as the radial-gradient center).\nWhen to use it: Use it on dark-themed sites with rows of feature or pricing cards, to make the spot under the pointer stand out.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/154.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给特色卡片加上聚光灯悬停：在深色卡片上只照亮光标周围半径约 120 px 的范围，边框也一起发光。"],
  "155": ["lp2",11,"悬停切换图片","悬停时换成另一张照片","Please use \"Image swap on hover\" (ホバーで画像切り替え), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #155\n\nWhat it is: Hovering swaps the photo for another shot\nWhat the sample shows: With the cursor on a product card, the front photo of the T-shirt cross-fades to a back view; it returns to the front when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with two product cards (photo frame 196 × 112, radius 8, name and price below). The cursor rests on the left card, then the right one, for about 1.3 s each. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- On hover, over 0.3 s (quadratic ease-in-out), the front photo (small dot on the chest) cross-fades to the back photo (large star on the back); on leave it fades back over the same 0.3 s.\n- Two dots under the photo (radius 3) show which photo is showing (the dark dot is the current one).\n- The hover area is the whole card, including the name. The frame, name and price do not move.\nWhen to use it: Use it on e-commerce product grids to show another angle or an on-model shot without leaving the list.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/155.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给商品列表加上悬停切换图片：光标停在卡片上时，用 0.3 s 叠化为背面照片。"],
  "156": ["lp2",12,"悬停文字翻滚","文字向上翻转并替换","Please use \"Text roll on hover\" (テキストロール), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #156\n\nWhat it is: Letters roll up and swap on hover\nWhat the sample shows: With the cursor on a menu word, its letters roll up and out one by one while the same word rolls in from below in orange; it rolls back when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with three menu words (WORKS, ABOUT, CONTACT; 30 px, weight 800, 1 px letter spacing). The cursor rests on each, left to right, for about 0.85 s. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- An orange copy of each word sits 40 px below it, and both are clipped to a 39 px tall box (overflow: hidden).\n- On hover each letter, staggered by 0.035 s, moves 40 px up and out over 0.36 s (cubic ease-in-out) while its orange copy rises into place.\n- On leave the letters roll back down with the same stagger and timing.\nWhen to use it: Use it on header menus or buttons to give short text links a tactile response.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/156.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给主导航加上悬停文字翻滚：光标悬停时文字逐字向上翻出，每字间隔 0.035 s，同样的朱红色文字从下方翻入。"],
  "157": ["lp2",13,"悬停图片预览","悬停列表项时显示对应照片","Please use \"Hover image reveal\" (ホバーで画像プレビュー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #157\n\nWhat it is: Hovering a list item shows its photo\nWhat the sample shows: With the cursor on a row of a text-only list, that row's photo fades in beside the cursor and follows it.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with a text-only list of four rows (39 px rows, 17 px names). The cursor moves down the rows, about 1 s on each. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Hovered row: over 0.25 s (cubic ease-out) the name shifts 8 px right and the name and the arrow at the right turn orange; on leave they return over 0.25 s.\n- Photo: that row's photo (132 × 84, radius 6, drop shadow) appears 26 px right of the cursor, a little above it, kept inside the window vertically.\n- Over the same 0.25 s the photo goes from opacity 0 to 1 and from 0.85× to 1×. It follows the cursor without lag; moving to the next row fades the old photo out as the new one comes in.\nWhen to use it: Use it on lists of work, projects or properties that stay text-only and light, while letting people check a photo for the rows they care about.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/157.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把设施列表做成悬停图片预览：光标停在某行时，用 0.25 s 在光标旁显示该行照片，并跟随光标移动。"],
  "158": ["lp2",14,"浮动标签","开始输入时标签上移","Please use \"Floating label\" (フローティングラベル), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #158\n\nWhat it is: The label floats up when you start typing\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the field shrinks the label and moves it onto the top border, leaving the field free for typing; empty and unfocused, the label moves back inside.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with a 300 × 46 field (radius 8) holding the label \"メールアドレス\" (email address, 15 px). The field is clicked at 0.65 s, and a click outside at 3.95 s removes focus. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- While focused or not empty, over 0.24 s (cubic ease-out) the label shrinks 15 → 11.5 px and moves from the middle of the field onto the top border (left padding 14 → 10 px); the border is masked in white behind it.\n- While focused, over 0.15 s (cubic ease-out) the border turns from gray to orange and 1.5 → 2.2 px wide, and the label turns orange.\n- \"hello@example.com\" is typed one character per 0.075 s from 1.0 s and deleted one per 0.03 s from 3.2 s. Once empty and unfocused, the label moves back inside over the same 0.24 s.\n- The text caret blinks every 0.9 s (it stays on while typing).\nWhen to use it: Use it on forms with many fields, to keep each label visible without taking extra space.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/158.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","表单输入框使用浮动标签：获得焦点时，标签用 0.24 s 缩小并移到边框顶线上。"],
  "159": ["lp2",15,"实时校验","输入时即时显示对错","Please use \"Inline validation\" (インラインバリデーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #159\n\nWhat it is: Shows right or wrong while you type\nWhat the sample shows: While the email address is half typed the field turns red with an \"invalid format\" message; the moment it is complete it switches to a green check and \"OK\".\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with a 300 × 44 email field (radius 8). Clicked at 0.45 s, clicked away at 4.2 s. \"hana@example.com\" (16 characters) is typed one character per 0.115 s from 0.75 s and deleted one per 0.03 s from 3.6 s. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- From the second character until the last one is typed it is invalid: over 0.15 s (cubic ease-out) the border turns red (#E5383B), the fill pale red (#FFF1F1), and a red \"!\" circle with \"形式が正しくありません\" (invalid format, 13 px) appears below.\n- When the last character makes it valid, over 0.25 s the border turns green (#1E9E5A), a green circle (radius 11, bouncing in with GSAP elastic.out(1, 0.3)) with a white check appears at the right end, and \"OK\" appears below.\n- While focused, the border turns from gray to navy and 1.5 → 2.2 px wide over 0.15 s. Once deletion starts, the messages go away.\nWhen to use it: Use it on sign-up or contact forms so people notice mistakes before they submit.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/159.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给联系表单加上实时校验：邮箱地址未输完整时显示红色“格式不正确”，正确后显示绿色对勾。"],
  "160": ["lp2",16,"加载按钮","点击后在按钮内显示加载中到完成","Please use \"Loading button\" (ローディングボタン), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #160\n\nWhat it is: Shows loading, then done, inside the button\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the submit button shrinks it to a circle with a spinner inside; when it finishes it widens into a green \"Done\" with a check.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with an orange pill button, 220 × 36, labeled \"送信する\" (Send). It is clicked at 0.8 s. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Over 0.85–1.15 s (0.3 s, cubic ease-in-out) it shrinks from 220 to 36 px wide, a circle; the label fades in the first third of the shrink.\n- From 1.1 to 2.3 s a white spinner (radius 10, line width 3, 0.7π arc) turns once every 0.7 s inside the circle.\n- Over 2.25–2.45 s the color goes orange → green (#1E9E5A) and a white check draws over 2.25–2.5 s; over 2.45–2.8 s (cubic ease-in-out) it widens 36 → 150 px, the check moves 26 px left and \"完了\" (Done) appears.\n- It fades out over 3.9–4.1 s and the original \"送信する\" button comes back, rising 6 px, over 4.1–4.4 s (cubic ease-out).\nWhen to use it: Use it on buttons that make people wait a moment for a result, such as submit, purchase or save.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/160.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把提交按钮做成加载按钮：点击后用 0.3 s 收缩成圆形并显示加载圆环，完成后变成绿色对勾和“完成”。"],
  "161": ["lp2",17,"视图过渡","列表中的照片直接展开为详情页","Please use \"View transition (shared element)\" (ビュートランジション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #161\n\nWhat it is: A list photo expands into the detail page\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking a photo in the list grows that same photo into the image at the top of the detail page while the rest changes to the detail page; going back shrinks it into place.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with three photos in a list (143 × 80, radius 6). The middle photo is clicked at 0.75 s, and \"← 一覧へ\" (back to list) on the detail page at 3.05 s. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Forward: over 0.85–1.45 s (0.6 s, cubic ease-in-out) the clicked photo moves and resizes continuously from its list slot to the 479 × 94 image at the top of the detail page (radius 8). It stays one photo throughout.\n- The other photos and the heading fade out over the first 62% of the move; the detail title, text and back button fade in over the last 40%. At 50% the URL changes from /works to /works/02.\n- Back: over 3.15–3.75 s (0.6 s) the same move runs in reverse to the list slot.\n- This is how the View Transitions API looks when the list photo and the detail photo share the same view-transition-name.\nWhen to use it: Use it on galleries or product pages that go back and forth between a list and a detail view, so people never lose track of what they opened.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/161.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从作品列表进入详情页时使用视图过渡：被点击的照片用 0.6 s 直接放大到详情页顶部。"],
  "162": ["lp2",18,"灯箱","点击图片后在变暗的背景上放大","Please use \"Lightbox\" (ライトボックス), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #162\n\nWhat it is: Opens an image large over a dimmed page\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking a thumbnail in the gallery dims the page and shows that photo large in the center; the × shrinks it back into its thumbnail.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport with four thumbnails (108 × 72, radius 6). The third is clicked at 0.75 s, and the × at the top right at 3.0 s. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Open: over 0.85–1.3 s (0.45 s, cubic ease-out) a dark overlay (rgb(14,18,28), opacity 0 → 0.82) covers the page and the clicked thumbnail grows to 261 × 128 in the center.\n- Over the second half of the open, \"3 / 4\" appears below the photo, previous/next arrows at the sides and a × at the top right.\n- Close: over 3.05–3.4 s (0.35 s, cubic ease-in-out) the same move runs in reverse and the photo returns to its thumbnail.\nWhen to use it: Use it for case studies, portfolios or product photos that should be seen large without leaving the page.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/162.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让施工案例照片可以在灯箱中查看：点击后背景变暗、照片在中央放大，用左右箭头切换上一张和下一张。"],
  "163": ["lp2",19,"图片热点","点击图片上的圆点显示说明","Please use \"Hotspots\" (ホットスポット), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #163\n\nWhat it is: Dots on an image open notes when clicked\nWhat the sample shows: White dots pulse on the product picture; clicking one opens a tooltip about that part, and clicking another dot swaps the tooltip.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport: a product picture (a backpack) on the left, name and price on the right, with two dots on the picture (white circle, radius 8, drop shadow; orange center, radius 4). One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Pulse: from each dot a white ring (width 2) grows from radius 8 to 20 while fading from 0.75 to 0 opacity, every 1.57 s (a third of 4.7 s), two rings half a period apart.\n- At 0.9 s the upper dot is clicked: a tooltip (136 × 48, radius 8, with a pointer toward the dot) appears to its left over 0.25 s (cubic ease-out), rising 6 px.\n- At 2.4 s the lower dot is clicked: the first tooltip fades over 0.25 s and the next one opens to the right of the lower dot. A second click at 3.8 s closes it.\nWhen to use it: Use it on products, floor plans or maps, to explain different spots within one picture.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/163.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给商品照片加上图片热点：在特色部位放置脉动的圆点，点击后用 0.25 s 弹出说明气泡。"],
  "164": ["lp2",20,"倒计时","显示距截止时间的剩余时间并递减","Please use \"Countdown timer\" (カウントダウンタイマー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #164\n\nWhat it is: Counts down the time left to a deadline\nWhat the sample shows: The hours, minutes and seconds under \"キャンペーン終了まで\" (until the campaign ends) count down every second; only the digits that change slide up and out as new ones come in from below.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport: an orange gradient band with \"キャンペーン終了まで\" (until the campaign ends) and six digit tiles for hours, minutes and seconds (34 × 50 each, radius 6, 32 px digits). This card alone runs once per 9.4 s (the pack cycle).\n- It starts at 02:15:04 and counts down one second at a time, nine times, every 1 s from 0.4 s, ending at 02:14:55. At 4.4 s, 02:15:00 → 02:14:59 rolls the minutes over.\n- Only the tiles whose digit changes animate: over 0.32 s (cubic ease-in-out) the old digit slides up and out and the new one slides in from below, clipped to the tile.\n- At 9.4 s it goes back to 02:15:04 with a plain cut.\nWhen to use it: Use it before a limited-time offer or an application deadline, to make the time left plain to see.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/164.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给活动截止时间加上倒计时：以时:分:秒显示，每次数字变化时新数字用 0.3 s 从下方滚入。"],
  "165": ["lp2",21,"动态形状分隔线","持续摆动的波浪形区块分隔线","Please use \"Animated shape divider\" (シェイプディバイダー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #165\n\nWhat it is: A wavy section divider that keeps moving\nWhat the sample shows: Where a blue section meets a white one, two layered wave shapes keep swaying slowly.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport: a blue gradient section on top (#3B64E8 → #8FA9F7) and a white section below, with two wave shapes layered at the boundary. One loop takes 4.7 s (two per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Back wave (white, opacity 0.45): centered at y = 100, the sum of a sine with wavelength 260 px, amplitude 8 px and one with wavelength 130 px, amplitude 4 px.\n- Front wave (white): centered at y = 110, wavelength 300 px / amplitude 9 px plus wavelength 110 px / amplitude 3.5 px; it runs into the white section below.\n- With phase a = 2π·t/4.7, the back wave uses a + 1 and −2a, the front wave −a and 2a + 0.5. The two sines in each wave run in opposite directions, so the shape keeps changing and returns to where it started every 4.7 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it where section edges should look soft rather than ruled, on sites about the sea, summer or children, for example.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/165.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","在首屏与下一节之间加入动态形状分隔线：叠放两层白色波浪，缓慢地反向持续摆动。"],
  "166": ["lp2",22,"点赞动画","点击后爱心迸发弹出","Please use \"Like button animation\" (いいねアニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #166\n\nWhat it is: The heart pops with a burst when liked\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the heart fills it red with a springy pop, small particles burst around it and the count beside it goes up by one; clicking again undoes it.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport: a post card with an outlined heart (line width 2.4) and the count \"128\" on the right. The heart is clicked at 0.9 s and clicked again at 3.3 s to undo. One pass takes 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- In the 0.1 s before the click it squeezes to 0.78×; at the click it fills red (#F23D5C), grows 0.78 → 1.45× in 0.12 s (cubic ease-out), then settles to 1× as 1 + 0.45·e^(−7t)·cos(15t).\n- 0.08–0.58 s after the click: a red ring (radius 15 → 33, opacity 0.5 → 0) and six small particles in six directions (red, yellow, orange) flying out from radius 24 to 37 as they fade.\n- Count: 0.05–0.35 s after the click (cubic ease-out) 128 slides up and out and a red 129 comes in from below; undoing slides it back down to 128.\n- Undo: the heart goes back to an outline and dips to 0.84× and back over 0.4 s around the click (no particles).\nWhen to use it: Use it on like, favorite or save buttons, to confirm the tap clearly and pleasantly.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/166.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给帖子的点赞按钮加上点赞动画：点击后爱心填充红色并弹到 1.45×，周围散开小颗粒，数字加 1。"],
  "167": ["lp2",23,"向下滚动提示","持续循环、引导向下滚动的动画","Please use \"Scroll-down cue\" (スクロールダウンの合図), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #167\n\nWhat it is: A looping cue that invites you to scroll down\nWhat the sample shows: Below the hero, the word \"SCROLL\", a dot inside a mouse outline and arrows on either side keep repeating a downward motion.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport. Centered below the hero: \"SCROLL\" (11 px, 3 px letter spacing) and a mouse outline (24 × 38, radius 12, line width 2.2). One beat takes 1.57 s (three per 4.7 s, six per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- The orange dot inside (5 × 9) drops 14 px over the first 70% of the beat (quadratic ease-in-out), fades out between 45% and 75%, and reappears at the top on the next beat.\n- 40 px to each side, two down-chevrons (line width 2.5) per side, half a beat apart, drift 24 px downward; their opacity follows a sine, 0 → 0.8 → 0.\nWhen to use it: Use it when the hero fills the screen and people need a hint that the page goes on below.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/167.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","在首屏下方加入向下滚动提示：鼠标轮廓内的小圆点约每 1.5 s 向下移动并消失，循环播放。"],
  "168": ["lp2",24,"背景视频","首屏背景中播放视频","Please use \"Background video\" (背景動画), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #168\n\nWhat it is: A video plays behind the hero section\nWhat the sample shows: In the hero background, clouds and waves keep moving, while the headline and button sit still on top.\nSpec:\n- A 511 × 168 viewport. Background footage (sky, clouds, mountains, sea) fills the hero, with a still headline (28 px, white) and button on top. The footage loops every 4.7 s (twice per 9.4 s pack cycle).\n- Clouds: the far layer repeats every 170 px and moves 170 px right per 4.7 s (about 36 px/s); the near layer repeats every 340 px and moves 340 px per 4.7 s (about 72 px/s). The mountains stay still.\n- Sea: three waves (y = 118, 130, 146; amplitude 2.5–3 px; wavelength 90, 60, 120 px); only the middle one runs the other way and moves two wavelengths per 4.7 s (the other two move one wavelength to the right).\n- For legibility, a 12% navy layer covers the footage, a gradient darkens the left 300 px (opacity 0.45 → 0), and the headline has a shadow (10 px blur).\n- A playing badge (pause, muted) sits at the bottom right. On a real site the video uses autoplay, muted, loop and playsinline.\nWhen to use it: Use it on hero sections for travel, hotels, restaurants or recruiting, where atmosphere and motion say more than one photo.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/168.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","首屏使用背景视频：静音循环播放，左侧叠加深色渐变，保证标题清晰可读。"],
  "169": ["camera2",1,"垂直升降镜头","相机整体垂直上下平移","Please use \"Pedestal\" (ペデスタル), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #169\n\nWhat it is: Move the whole camera straight up or down\nWhat the sample shows: The camera moves straight up without changing its direction; the horizon stays centred while the person and buildings slide down.\nSpec:\n- Camera: moves straight up from 1.0 m to 3.2 m; direction (yaw, pitch) and focal length (330 px) stay fixed\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 7 m ahead and slides down the frame, leaving at the bottom feet first; a tower stands 3.5 m right, 26 m away\n- Because the pitch does not change, the horizon stays at the centre of the frame (#031 Crane up tilts down while rising)\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the height (↕ 1.0m → ↕ 3.2m)\nWhen to use it: To show a shelf or a building from bottom to top smoothly, or to change the eye level without tilting.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/169.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","保持镜头朝向不变，用垂直升降镜头从眼睛高度直线上升到约 3 m。"],
  "170": ["camera2",2,"横滚镜头","相机绕镜头光轴旋转一整圈","Please use \"Barrel roll\" (バレルロール), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #170\n\nWhat it is: Roll the camera a full turn on its axis\nWhat the sample shows: The camera rolls a full turn around its lens axis; the horizon goes all the way round and comes back level.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position fixed (height 1.5 m); roll only, 0 → 2π rad (360°); the whole picture turns around the frame centre\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.6 s (3.1 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 7 m ahead; horizon, buildings and person all turn by the same angle, and white shows in the corners while turning\n- Hold: 3.6–4.2 s. After a full turn the picture equals the start, so the final 0.5 s cross-fade is invisible (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the angle (↻ 0° → ↻ 360°)\nWhen to use it: For aerial or drone footage that needs energy, or to show dizziness and confusion.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/170.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让无人机画面用横滚镜头旋转一整圈，用时 3 s。"],
  "171": ["camera2",3,"移动延时","相机边移动边拍的延时摄影","Please use \"Hyperlapse\" (ハイパーラプス), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #171\n\nWhat it is: A time-lapse shot while the camera travels\nWhat the sample shows: The camera travels forward along a street while the sun, clouds and passers-by run in fast forward: a time-lapse that moves.\nSpec:\n- Camera: moves forward 0 m → 22 m (height 1.6 m, pitch +0.05 rad) while the sun, clouds and figures fast-forward through 12 hours (#039 Time-lapse keeps the camera still)\n- Timing: 0.4 s to 4.1 s (3.7 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Street: 12 buildings at x = ±7.5 m (5–55 m deep, 8–16 m tall) approach the camera and leave the frame\n- Sun: travels left to right along an arc, angle -1.25 rad → +1.25 rad, always 170 m ahead of the camera; three clouds drift 140 m right in total, wrapping every 80 m; six small figures cross an 11 m wide street\n- Building shadows fall away from the sun and swing as it moves (translucent grey); the mountains move with the camera so they keep their size\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows the clock and the distance travelled (06:00 · 0m → 18:00 · 22m)\nWhen to use it: To cover a long distance and a long stretch of time in one sweep through a city or a building.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/171.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","拍一段从车站走到公园的移动延时：云朵流动，行人像快进一样移动。"],
  "172": ["camera2",4,"长镜头","不切换，一个镜头连续拍到底","Please use \"Long take\" (長回し), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #172\n\nWhat it is: One continuous shot with no cuts\nWhat the sample shows: One continuous shot follows a walking person with no cut; the bar at the bottom stays a single unbroken strip.\nSpec:\n- Join: none; for 4.2 s one shot keeps following the person (#041 Jump cut splits it into five)\n- Subject: a person walks at constant speed from front left (x = -3.4 m, 5.2 m deep) to back right (x = 2.8 m, 9.6 m deep); legs and arms swing by sin(t×7)×0.42 rad\n- Camera: trucks right 0 m → 1.4 m after the person while turning, yaw = atan2(person x - camera x, depth)×0.8; height 1.4 m\n- Bottom strip: one blue bar labelled \"1ショット・カットなし\" (one shot, no cut) with a playhead, showing there is no break\n- Return: stops at 4.2 s, then cross-fades back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the elapsed time (NO CUT 0.0s → 4.2s)\nWhen to use it: To keep tension and presence unbroken, or to show a sequence of movement as one flow.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/172.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从准备到出发用一个长镜头拍完，跟着人物，中间不切镜头。"],
  "173": ["camera2",5,"斯坦尼康","消除抖动，平稳流畅地移动","Please use \"Steadicam\" (ステディカム), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #173\n\nWhat it is: Smooth, floating movement with no shake\nWhat the sample shows: The camera glides forward after a walking person with only a slow, gentle sway and no jitter, unlike handheld.\nSpec:\n- Camera: moves forward at a constant 1.7 m/s (8 m per 4.7 s); height 1.45 m, pitch -0.02 rad; no easing\n- Sway: height ±3.5 cm (2 cycles per 4.7 s), sideways ±5 cm (1 cycle), yaw ±0.012 rad, roll ±0.006 rad, all sine waves with integer periods, slow and wide (#034 Handheld is fast and irregular)\n- Subject: a person walks 5 m ahead of the camera at the same speed; legs and arms take 5 strides per 4.7 s\n- Trees: 3.6 m tall at x = -5 m and 3.2 m tall at x = +5 m, every 8 m (the two rows offset by 4 m); the mountains and sun move with the camera\n- 8 m is a multiple of the grid (2 m) and tree (8 m) spacing, so it loops seamlessly every 4.7 s; top-right readout shows \"STEADICAM\"\nWhen to use it: To make a walking move look smooth and cinematic.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/173.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用斯坦尼康跟拍走廊里人物的背后，平稳无晃动。"],
  "174": ["camera2",6,"背后跟拍","跟在主体身后移动","Please use \"Follow shot\" (フォローショット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #174\n\nWhat it is: Follow behind the subject as they move\nWhat the sample shows: The camera trails a weaving walker along the same path a few metres behind; the person stays near the centre, seen from the back.\nSpec:\n- Path: the person walks the curve x = 1.8·sin(2.2s), depth z = 4 + 9s (s from 0 to 1), from 4 m to 13 m away\n- Camera: follows on the same curve at s-0.4 (about 3.6–3.9 m behind) and always faces the person, yaw = atan2(person x - camera x, person z - camera z); height 1.5 m\n- Timing: 0.3 s to 4.2 s (3.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)); legs and arms swing by sin(s×30)×0.42 rad\n- The person stays near the centre of frame, seen from behind; posts and a rock beside the path sweep past in the foreground (#029 Tracking shot runs alongside)\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s); top-right readout shows the distance to the person (FOLLOW 3.6–3.9m)\nWhen to use it: To enter a place together with a character, or for a third-person, game-like view.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/174.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用背后跟拍拍摄在林中行走的人物背影，稍微落后一点跟着。"],
  "175": ["camera2",7,"固定镜头","相机固定不动，只有主体移动","Please use \"Locked-off shot\" (ロックオフ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #175\n\nWhat it is: Camera fixed; only the subject moves\nWhat the sample shows: A person crosses in front of a tripod-fixed camera and a car passes behind; the camera does not move by a pixel.\nSpec:\n- Camera: completely fixed (height 1.4 m, facing forward, focal length 330 px); only the subjects move\n- Subject: a person crosses left to right at constant speed 6.5 m ahead (x = -6.2 m → +6.2 m in 4.7 s); legs and arms swing by sin(u×7)×0.42 rad\n- A grey car crosses right to left 15 m away (x = +16 m → -16 m in 4.7 s)\n- Both start and end outside the frame, so it loops seamlessly every 4.7 s\n- A grey tripod mark at bottom left; top-right readout shows \"LOCKED\" (#040 Freeze frame stops the footage time; here time runs and only the camera is still)\nWhen to use it: To make the subject stand out by contrast, for fixed-point observation, or as a base for time-lapse and compositing.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/175.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用固定镜头拍十字路口：相机固定在三脚架上，只有行人和车辆经过。"],
  "176": ["camera2",8,"穿越镜头","穿过窗户或门进入下一个空间","Please use \"Fly-through\" (フライスルー), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #176\n\nWhat it is: Fly through an opening into the next space\nWhat the sample shows: The camera flies toward a wall with a window, passes through the opening and comes out into the place beyond.\nSpec:\n- Camera: moves forward 0 m → 12.5 m (height 1.3 m, direction fixed); a wall with a window stands 8 m ahead and the camera passes through it\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.6 s (3.1 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Wall: a pale grey plane 80 m wide and 14 m tall with a window 2.4 m wide and 2.2 m tall (sill at 0.15 m); through it a person (0.3 m right, 14.5 m away), trees, buildings and mountains are visible\n- Pass-through: the wall stops being drawn 0.25 m in front of the camera; by then the window edge is outside the frame (half-width about 1580 px), so it vanishes unseen\n- After the pass the place beyond fills the frame and the camera closes to 2 m from the person (#035 FPV drone shot keeps weaving between trees)\n- Return: hold 3.6–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows the distance to the window (\"窓まで 8.0m\" → \"通過\", passed)\nWhen to use it: To enter a building as an opening move, or to travel from one place to another in a single move.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/176.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用穿越镜头从窗户进入房间，一直推到桌子上方。"],
  "177": ["camera2",9,"低角度镜头","从低处向上拍","Please use \"Low angle\" (ローアングル), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #177\n\nWhat it is: Shoot from low down, looking up\nWhat the sample shows: The camera drops to near the ground and looks up; the person looks big and the buildings tower.\nSpec:\n- Camera: lowers from 1.5 m to 0.35 m while the pitch goes 0 → +0.32 rad (about 18° up); no movement forward or back\n- Timing: 0.6 s to 2.2 s (1.6 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 4.5 m ahead; an 11.8 m tower stands 3 m left, 22 m away. As the camera looks up, person and tower stretch upward and the horizon drops\n- Hold: stays at the low angle from 2.2 s to 4.2 s (time to read the composition itself)\n- Return: cross-fade back to eye level over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s); top-right readout shows angle and height (↗ 0° · 1.5m → ↗ 18° · 0.4m)\nWhen to use it: To make a person look powerful or large, or to emphasise the height of a building.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/177.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","英雄登场用低角度镜头，从贴近地面处向上拍。"],
  "178": ["camera2",10,"高角度镜头","从高处向下拍","Please use \"High angle\" (ハイアングル), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #178\n\nWhat it is: Shoot from above, looking down\nWhat the sample shows: The camera rises and looks down; the person looks small and the ground fills most of the frame.\nSpec:\n- Camera: rises from 1.5 m to 4.5 m while the pitch goes 0 → -0.5 rad (about 29° down); no movement forward or back\n- Timing: 0.6 s to 2.2 s (1.6 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 5 m ahead; as the camera looks down they shrink and move lower, the ground grid fills most of the frame and the horizon leaves at the top\n- Hold: stays at the high angle from 2.2 s to 4.2 s (#031 Crane up keeps rising to 9 m; 13 Bird's-eye view looks straight down at 90°)\n- Return: cross-fade back to eye level over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s); top-right readout shows angle and height (↘ 0° · 1.5m → ↘ 29° · 4.5m)\nWhen to use it: To make a person look vulnerable or small, or to explain a situation from above.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/178.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","迷路孩子的场景用高角度镜头，从稍高处向下拍，让孩子显得很小。"],
  "179": ["camera2",11,"POV 镜头","以角色的视线观看","Please use \"POV shot\" (POVショット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #179\n\nWhat it is: See through a character's eyes\nWhat the sample shows: Seen through a character's eyes: the walking sway and the hands at the bottom say first person, and the person ahead waves at you.\nSpec:\n- Camera: walks forward 0 m → 3.2 m at the character's eye height of 1.6 m; 0.3 s to 4.2 s (3.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Walking sway: height ±3 cm (6 cycles per 4.7 s), roll ±0.008 rad (3 cycles), added only while moving\n- Hands: blue rounded hands at both bottom corners (±178 px from centre), a white phone in the right one; they move with the body, so the hands stay still and the world sways\n- The other person, 7.5 m ahead, raises both arms and waves only from 1.6 s to 3.4 s (looking at you); two posts in the foreground\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s); top-right readout shows \"POV\"\nWhen to use it: To put the viewer in the character's place, or for a game-like or VR-like feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/179.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","开门走进房间的那一刻用 POV 镜头，以角色本人的视线拍摄。"],
  "180": ["camera2",12,"过肩镜头","越过一人的肩膀拍另一人","Please use \"Over-the-shoulder\" (オーバーザショルダー), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #180\n\nWhat it is: Frame one person over another's shoulder\nWhat the sample shows: The back of one person's head and shoulder sit at the edge of frame and the other person is seen past them; the foreground is soft, the subject sharp.\nSpec:\n- Framing: the back of the foreground person's head and shoulder (grey, 0.62 m left, 1.15 m away) fill the left edge; the other person (blue, 0.32 m right, 3.1 m away) is seen past the shoulder\n- Focus: the foreground shoulder is blurred 2.6 px, the other person is sharp and framed from the chest up\n- Camera: height 1.55 m, yaw +0.05 rad; pushes in slowly 0 m → 0.35 m from 0.5 s to 3.4 s (cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\n- The other person sways arms and legs by 0.35·sin(u×5) rad, as if talking\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows \"OTS\"\nWhen to use it: To show who is facing whom in a conversation and to focus on the other person's expression.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/180.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","对话用过肩镜头拍摄，前景的肩膀稍微虚化。"],
  "181": ["camera2",13,"鸟瞰镜头","从正上方垂直向下拍","Please use \"Bird's-eye view\" (バーズアイ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #181\n\nWhat it is: Straight down from directly overhead\nWhat the sample shows: Looking straight down from overhead: road, people, cars and trees appear as top-down shapes, and more comes into view as the camera rises.\nSpec:\n- Camera: points straight down (pitch -π/2 = -90°) and rises from 9 m to 15 m, directly above the origin\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Ground: a 2 m grid and a 3.2 m wide road (white dashed centre line) drawn as one plane; six trees as circles and three buildings as squares, seen from above\n- Subjects: a person (head circle and shoulder ellipse) walks 5.2 m up the right side of the road, a car (1.8×4 m) drives 6.8 m down the left side; both move in proportion to the progress p\n- As the camera rises everything shrinks and more of the ground comes into view (10 High angle looks down at a slant)\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows \"↓ 90° · 9m → 15m\"\nWhen to use it: To show layout and paths like a diagram, or for a god's-eye overview.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/181.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从正上方用鸟瞰镜头拍十字路口，人和车以从上往下看的样子移动。"],
  "182": ["camera2",14,"深焦镜头","从近处到远处全部清晰","Please use \"Deep focus\" (ディープフォーカス), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #182\n\nWhat it is: Near and far all in sharp focus\nWhat the sample shows: From the flower in front to the person and buildings behind, everything comes into sharp focus at the same time.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position, direction and focal length all fixed (height 1.1 m); only the blur amounts change\n- Blur: the foreground flower (0.75 m left, 2 m away) goes 5 px → 0 px and the background (person 0.9 m right, 9 m away; buildings; mountains) goes 6 px → 0 px, both sharpening together (#033 Rack focus blurs one side)\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Focus markers: blue corner brackets on both the flower (half-width 46 px) and the person (half-width 30 px), opacity 0 → 1 as focus arrives\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows the aperture (f/1.8 → f/16)\nWhen to use it: When the viewer may look anywhere in the frame, or to show several things happening at different depths at once.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/182.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","前景的杯子和后方的人物都要清晰，所以用深焦镜头。"],
  "183": ["camera2",15,"定场镜头","开场交代地点的远景","Please use \"Establishing shot\" (エスタブリッシングショット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #183\n\nWhat it is: A wide opening shot that shows the place\nWhat the sample shows: A wide, high view of the whole town; the camera pushes in slowly and a location caption appears at bottom left.\nSpec:\n- Camera: wide lens (focal length 220 px, shown as 16mm), height 4.5 m, pitch -0.06 rad; pushes in slowly from -5 m to -2.5 m\n- Timing: 0.3 s to 4.2 s (3.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Scene: eight city buildings 30 m away, a tower 16 m right and 36 m away, three clouds and mountains; a small person 1 m left, 12 m away gives the scale\n- Location caption: from 0.9 s to 1.3 s a white card reading \"EXT. CITY – DAY\" (158×30 px, blue bar on its left) fades in at bottom left while moving up 8 px, then stays\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s); top-right readout shows \"16mm WIDE\"\nWhen to use it: At the start of a scene to say where we are, or whenever the place or time changes.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/183.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","开头先用能看到整个城镇的定场镜头，同时显示地名。"],
  "184": ["camera2",16,"大特写","只放大眼睛或指尖等局部","Please use \"Extreme close-up\" (エクストリームクローズアップ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #184\n\nWhat it is: Fill the frame with one small detail\nWhat the sample shows: From a close-up of the face to a frame filled by nothing but the eyes.\nSpec:\n- Camera: the face's right eye (0.06 m left of centre, 1.66 m high) 1.3 m ahead is placed at the centre of frame; the camera does not move\n- Focal length: 610 px → 2040 px (shown as 44mm → 148mm, about 3.3×); f = 610 × (2040/610)^p, where p is a cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)) from 0.5 s to 3.4 s\n- Face: a blue head (radius 0.16 m) with white eyes (ellipses 0.045×0.028 m), dark pupils (radius 0.016 m), highlights and white brows; it starts as a close-up of the whole face (head about 150 px across) and ends with only the eyes filling the frame\n- Background: trees and buildings blurred 3 px, leaving the frame as the lens closes in\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows the focal length and the abbreviation (44mm CU → 148mm ECU)\nWhen to use it: For the emotional peak, or to make the viewer notice one small detail.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/184.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","眼泪落下的瞬间，用只拍眼睛的大特写。"],
  "185": ["camera2",17,"插入镜头","插入同一场景中的细节","Please use \"Insert shot\" (インサートショット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #185\n\nWhat it is: Cut in to a detail of the same scene\nWhat the sample shows: A big close-up of the watch on the person's wrist is cut into the scene for 1.3 s, then it returns to the same shot.\nSpec:\n- Join: two straight cuts (0 frames); to the detail at 1.6 s and back to the scene at 2.9 s (the detail lasts 1.3 s)\n- Main shot (A): fixed camera (height 1.4 m); a person stands 0.6 m left, 6 m away, with a watch (dark dot) on the wrist; a post 2.2 m right, 4 m away\n- Detail (INSERT): a big close-up of the wrist from the same scene; a blue sleeve (600×92 px, rotated -0.35 rad) on pale blue, a white dial (radius 58 px), dark hands and a blue second hand that makes one turn in 1.3 s\n- Bottom strip: three sections A (grey), detail (blue), A (grey) with a playhead; what is cut in belongs to the same scene (21 Cutaway shows a different subject)\n- Top-right readout shows \"SHOT A\" → \"INSERT\" → \"SHOT A\"; at 4.7 s it cuts straight back to the start\nWhen to use it: To show a small object or a hand action, or to point out an important prop.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/185.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","转动钥匙时用插入镜头拍手部特写，然后马上切回。"],
  "186": ["camera2",18,"变形剪切","平滑衔接相同构图的两段画面","Please use \"Morph cut\" (モーフカット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #186\n\nWhat it is: Blend two takes so the join disappears\nWhat the sample shows: Two takes of the same person are joined by smoothly interpolating position and pose, so nothing jumps as in a jump cut.\nSpec:\n- Take 1 (0–2.0 s): fixed camera (height 1.45 m); the person stands 0.4 m left, 3.3 m away, arms and legs at -0.45 rad. Take 2 (from 2.45 s): 0.35 m right, +0.55 rad. Both sway slightly by 0.12·sin(t×3) rad\n- Morph (2.0–2.45 s, 0.45 s): the position is interpolated with a quadratic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.45,0,0.55,1)), and the two poses are drawn at the same interpolated position and cross-faded\n- Only during the morph a blur of sin(q×π)×2.2 px is applied to the whole frame to soften the join (#041 Jump cut lets the position jump)\n- Bottom strip: take 1 (grey), morph (blue, narrow), take 2 (grey) with a playhead\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start of take 1 over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows \"TAKE 1\" → \"MORPH\" → \"TAKE 2\"\nWhen to use it: To tighten an interview or narration, or to remove a slip without drawing attention.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/186.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用变形剪切去掉采访中说错重来的部分，让接缝看不出来。"],
  "187": ["camera2",19,"淡出到黑场","画面逐渐变暗直至全黑","Please use \"Fade to black\" (フェードアウト), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #187\n\nWhat it is: The picture darkens to black\nWhat the sample shows: The whole picture sinks to black, and the next scene brightens out of the black.\nSpec:\n- Fade out: from 1.4 s to 2.6 s (1.2 s) black (rgb(20,20,24)) is laid over the outgoing picture with opacity 0 → 100%, quadratic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.45,0,0.55,1))\n- Black: fully black from 2.6 s to 3.1 s; at 2.9 s the incoming picture is swapped in unseen, with a straight cut\n- Fade in: from 3.1 s to 4.3 s (1.2 s) the black goes from 100% → 0 with the same easing\n- Camera: fixed in both pictures (A at height 1.4 m; B at height 1.6 m, pitch +0.1 rad); the subjects do not move either\n- Alternates A→B and B→A every 4.7 s (9.4 s for the round trip); top-right readout shows \"FADE OUT\" / \"FADE IN\"; the viewfinder marks stay over the black\nWhen to use it: For a chapter break, a long passage of time, or the end of a story.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/187.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","场景结尾用 1 s 淡出到黑场，下一场景再从黑场中淡入。"],
  "188": ["camera2",20,"圈出","圆形窗口收拢，画面变黑","Please use \"Iris out\" (アイリスアウト), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #188\n\nWhat it is: A circle closes down to black\nWhat the sample shows: A circle closes down on the person until the frame is black, then opens again on the next scene.\nSpec:\n- Iris out: from 1.3 s to 2.7 s (1.4 s) the circular window shrinks from radius 340 px to 0 (quadratic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.45,0,0.55,1))); outside the circle is black (#141418)\n- Centre of the window: the current picture's subject, the person's head in A (0.6 m left, 1.63 m high, 7 m away) or the car in B (1.2 m right, 0.9 m high, 9 m away), projected to the screen\n- Black: 2.7–3.1 s; at 2.9 s the incoming picture is swapped in with a straight cut\n- Iris in: from 3.1 s to 4.4 s (1.3 s) the circle grows from 0 to 340 px around the incoming picture's subject\n- Edge: while the radius is at least 1 px, a 2 px blue circle marks the rim; the camera is fixed in both pictures\n- Alternates A→B and B→A every 4.7 s (9.4 s for the round trip); top-right readout shows \"IRIS OUT\" / \"IRIS IN\"\nWhen to use it: For a silent-film or cartoon-style ending, or a playful break.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/188.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","以老电影的风格，用圈出收拢到主角身上，结束这个场景。"],
  "189": ["camera2",21,"切出镜头","切到其他对象后再切回","Please use \"Cutaway\" (カットアウェイ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #189\n\nWhat it is: Cut to something else, then back\nWhat the sample shows: From the speaker to the listening audience and back; what is cut in is a different subject.\nSpec:\n- Join: two straight cuts (0 frames); to the other subject at 1.7 s and back to the scene at 3.0 s (1.3 s away)\n- Main shot (A): fixed camera (height 1.4 m); a person 5.5 m away talks, swinging arms and legs by 0.45·sin(u×6) rad, with a grey lectern 0.9 m to the right\n- Other subject (CUTAWAY): the listening audience, five people 3.1–4.6 m away in blue and pale blue with both arms up, bouncing by |sin(t×9+i)|×5 cm; no background (a different place)\n- Bottom strip: A (grey), other subject (blue), A (grey) with a playhead (17 Insert shot shows a detail of the same scene)\n- Top-right readout shows \"SHOT A\" → \"CUTAWAY\" → \"SHOT A\"; at 4.7 s it cuts straight back to the start\nWhen to use it: To show a reaction, or to hide a time skip or a removed slip.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/189.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","讲话途中用切出镜头切到观众的反应，再切回来。"],
  "190": ["camera2",22,"交叉剪辑","交替呈现同时发生的两个场景","Please use \"Cross-cutting\" (クロスカッティング), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #190\n\nWhat it is: Alternate between two simultaneous scenes\nWhat the sample shows: Two scenes happening at the same time, a runner and a car, alternate in shorter and shorter cuts.\nSpec:\n- Two scenes share one clock: A is a runner (0.3 m left, depth 15 m → 4.5 m, legs at u×12), B is a car in the city (1 m right, depth 17 m → 4.5 m); both close in over 4.7 s\n- Cuts: straight cuts between A and B at 0 / 1.1 / 2.0 / 2.7 / 3.3 / 3.8 / 4.2 / 4.5 s; the shots shorten 1.1 → 0.9 → 0.7 → 0.6 → 0.5 → 0.4 → 0.3 s to raise the tension\n- Each scene keeps running while the other is on screen (when it comes back, its subject has moved on)\n- Camera: A at height 1.3 m, fixed, with four posts in the foreground; B at height 1.6 m, pitch +0.06 rad, fixed, with the city and sun\n- Bottom strip: eight alternating sections A (grey) and B (blue) with a playhead; the last 0.3 s cross-fades back to the start of A\n- Top-right readout shows \"SCENE A\" / \"SCENE B\"\nWhen to use it: To build tension between things happening at once, such as a chase or a rescue.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/190.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用交叉剪辑交替展示逃跑的人和追赶的车，镜头逐渐变短。"],
  "191": ["camera2",23,"子弹时间","时间静止，相机绕主体旋转","Please use \"Bullet time\" (バレットタイム), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #191\n\nWhat it is: Time stands still while the camera circles\nWhat the sample shows: Time nearly stops at the top of a jump while the camera circles around the person.\nSpec:\n- Footage time: runs normally for 0–1.5 s, at 0.1× from 1.5 s to 3.3 s (only 0.18 s of footage in 1.8 s), then normally again (footage time = u - 1.62)\n- Subject: a person 9 m away jumps on a parabola over footage time 0.6–2.6 s (peak 1.1 m, arms raised); during the slow part they seem to hang near the top (45–54% through); nine leaves fall on the same footage time\n- Camera: during the slow part it travels on a circle of radius 6 m around the person from -0.6 rad to +0.6 rad (about 69°), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)); always facing the centre, height 1.6 m, pitch -0.05 rad\n- The next 4.7 s pass circles the other way (+0.6 → -0.6 rad), so the 9.4 s loop is seamless (#030 Orbit does not stop time)\n- A dashed circle of radius 1.3 m on the ground and a ring of trees at 10 m; top-right readout shows \"×1.0\" → \"BULLET ×0.1\" → \"×1.0\"\nWhen to use it: To show a decisive moment in three dimensions, or as the highlight of an action scene.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/191.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","在跳跃最高点用子弹时间：让时间停住，只有相机绕着人物转。"],
  "192": ["camera2",24,"蒙太奇","用一连串短镜头压缩时间","Please use \"Montage\" (モンタージュ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions, part 2\".\nMotion Prompt #192\n\nWhat it is: A run of short shots condensing time\nWhat the sample shows: Seven short shots show thirty days of training; straight cuts, with the date jumping at top right.\nSpec:\n- Seven shots joined by straight cuts (0 frames): 0.75 / 0.7 / 0.65 / 0.65 / 0.65 / 0.6 / 0.7 s (4.7 s in all); the date at top right jumps DAY 1 → 3 → 7 → 12 → 20 → 28 → 30\n- Shots: 1 tracking a runner (legs at t×14), 2 a jump in the park, 3 sunrise (sun rising from 4 m to 12 m), 4 arms raised from a low angle, 5 walking in the city (focal length 420 px), 6 circling the person from -0.3 to +0.3 rad, 7 arms raised in front of a flag\n- Thirty days of training condensed into 4.7 s; camera position, height and focal length change with every shot (#041 Jump cut keeps the same framing)\n- Bottom strip: seven sections, only the current shot in blue; the last 0.3 s cross-fades back to the start of the first shot\nWhen to use it: To show a long period of change or effort in a short time.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/192.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera2.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用蒙太奇表现一个月的练习，连续排列约 7 个短镜头。"],
  "193": ["artstyle",1,"水彩画","颜色晕染、留出纸白的淡雅画","Please use \"Watercolor\" (水彩画), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #193\n\nWhat it is: A pale painting with soft bleeds and white paper showing\nWhat the sample shows: The line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun becomes a pale transparent watercolor, with colors bleeding and pooling and the white paper left showing.\nSpec:\n- Medium: transparent watercolor on paper\n- Look: colors that bleed and pool, white paper left unpainted, pale colors overall\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For picture books, illustrations or seasonal cards that should feel soft and hand-painted.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/193.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用水彩画画一只在窗边睡觉的猫，保留晕染和纸的留白，只用淡色。"],
  "194": ["artstyle",2,"厚涂油画","颜料堆厚，笔触清晰可见","Please use \"Impasto oil painting\" (油絵（厚塗り）), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #194\n\nWhat it is: Thick paint with visible brush and knife marks\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a richly colored oil painting with thick paint; brush strokes and knife marks stand out as ridges.\nSpec:\n- Medium: oil paint laid on thickly (impasto)\n- Look: brush strokes and palette-knife marks stay as raised ridges; strong, dense colors\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For posters and art pieces that should feel rich, heavy and hand-made.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/194.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用厚涂油画画一瓶向日葵，让堆起的笔触和刮刀痕迹清晰可见。"],
  "195": ["artstyle",3,"水墨画","只用墨色浓淡与晕染来画","Please use \"Ink wash painting (sumi-e)\" (水墨画), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #195\n\nWhat it is: Painted only with shades and washes of black ink\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a picture in one black ink on washi paper, shaped only by dark and pale ink, bleeds and soft washes.\nSpec:\n- Medium: one black ink on washi paper\n- Look: drawn only with dark and pale ink, bleeds and soft washes; no color\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For a quiet, Japanese feel with plenty of empty space.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/195.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用水墨画画雾中的山和小船，只用一种墨的浓淡和晕染，不用颜色。"],
  "196": ["artstyle",4,"浮世绘木版画","轮廓线加平涂色块的木版画","Please use \"Ukiyo-e woodblock print\" (浮世絵), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #196\n\nWhat it is: A woodblock print with outlines and flat colors\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes an Edo-period color woodblock print: the house turns into a tiled-roof Japanese house, the tree into a pine, the sun into a red circle, and the sky fades from deep indigo at the top.\nSpec:\n- Medium: Edo-period multi-color woodblock print\n- Look: thin, even black outlines, flat areas of color, slight misregistration between blocks, washi fibers and uneven printing\n- Sky: graded from deep indigo at the top to pale below, with a band of mist across it; the sun as a red circle (the sample leaves out Mount Fuji, waves, people and text)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For Japanese subjects shown boldly with flat color and line.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/196.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用浮世绘木版画画傍晚的港口小镇：细墨轮廓线、平涂色块，天空从上往下渐淡。"],
  "197": ["artstyle",5,"点彩画","用一个个小色点排列成画","Please use \"Pointillism\" (点描), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #197\n\nWhat it is: Painted with small dots of color placed side by side\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a picture made only of dots of color; sky, house, tree and ground are all built from clearly visible, fairly large dots.\nSpec:\n- Technique: only dots of color placed side by side; no lines or filled areas\n- Dot size: large enough to stay visible on a small card (tiny dots read as watercolor)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For a bright picture with a hand-made, rhythmic texture.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/197.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用点彩画画公园的长椅和树，点要大到看得清，不用线条。"],
  "198": ["artstyle",6,"彩色铅笔画","细笔触层层叠加，可见纸纹","Please use \"Colored pencil drawing\" (色鉛筆画), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #198\n\nWhat it is: Fine pencil strokes layered over textured paper\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a hand-drawn colored pencil picture, with layered fine strokes and white paper grain showing through.\nSpec:\n- Medium: colored pencils on paper\n- Look: color built up from layered fine strokes; the paper grain shows through in white\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For friendly, hand-drawn illustrations, including ones for children.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/198.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用彩色铅笔画画早餐的面包和咖啡，用细线层层叠涂，露出纸纹。"],
  "199": ["artstyle",7,"麻胶版画","刻版印出的粗黑白线条","Please use \"Linocut print\" (リノカット), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #199\n\nWhat it is: Bold black-and-white lines cut into a block\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a black-and-white print from a carved block, made only of bold lines and shapes with no gray or blur.\nSpec:\n- Medium: a carved linoleum block, printed\n- Look: bold lines in pure black and white, with rough marks left by the carving\n- Avoid: gray, blur and gradients\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For posters, T-shirts or logos that need a strong black-and-white look.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/199.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用麻胶版画画骑自行车的人，只用黑白，不要灰色，保留粗糙的刻刀痕迹。"],
  "200": ["artstyle",8,"彩绘玻璃","黑色铅条分隔的透光彩色玻璃","Please use \"Stained glass\" (ステンドグラス), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #200\n\nWhat it is: Glowing colored glass divided by black lead lines\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a glass picture divided by black lead lines; sky, hill, house and tree each turn into pieces of colored glass with light shining through.\nSpec:\n- Material: pieces of colored glass joined by lead, as in a window\n- Look: areas of color divided by thick black lines, glowing as light passes through\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out) (this sample is cropped slightly wider so the lead lines of the hill show)\nWhen to use it: For a solemn or festive decorative look that glows with light.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/200.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把一只展翅的鸟做成彩绘玻璃，用粗黑铅条分隔，光透过彩色玻璃。"],
  "201": ["artstyle",9,"波普艺术","原色色块、粗黑轮廓加少量网点","Please use \"Pop art\" (ポップアート), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #201\n\nWhat it is: Primary-color areas, bold black outlines and a few halftone dots\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes flat primary colors with bold black outlines, with halftone dots here and there.\nSpec:\n- Look: flat areas of primary color with bold black outlines; a few halftone dots here and there\n- Feel: 1960s silkscreen prints\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For eye-catching ads, social images or merchandise.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/201.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用波普艺术画一个汉堡：平涂原色、粗黑轮廓，背景加少量网点。"],
  "202": ["artstyle",10,"霓虹灯招牌","在暗墙上用发光灯管勾出形状","Please use \"Neon sign\" (ネオンサイン), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #202\n\nWhat it is: Shapes drawn with glowing tubes on a dark wall\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes glowing neon tubes on a dark brick wall; the house, tree, sun and the line of the hill glow and bloom.\nSpec:\n- Material: a dark brick wall and glowing neon tubes\n- Look: shapes drawn only with tube lines, with the light blooming around them; the sample uses red, yellow and green tubes\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For a night-time mood or a shop or bar sign look.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/202.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把一个咖啡杯做成霓虹灯招牌：暗色砖墙上只用发光灯管的线条，让光晕开。"],
  "203": ["artstyle",11,"装饰艺术（Art Deco）","金与黑、放射直线与左右对称","Please use \"Art Deco\" (アールデコ), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #203\n\nWhat it is: Gold and black, radiating straight lines and symmetry\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a gold-and-black poster: straight rays spread out from the sun, and geometric straight-line ornament is arranged almost symmetrically.\nSpec:\n- Color: mostly gold and black\n- Look: radiating straight rays, geometric straight lines and near-symmetrical ornament\n- Feel: a 1920s poster (no text in the sample)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For a luxurious, classic and glamorous look.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/203.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用装饰艺术风格画酒店入口海报：以金和黑为主，放射状直线和左右对称装饰，不放文字。"],
  "204": ["artstyle",12,"新艺术运动（Art Nouveau）","以花草曲线勾边的装饰风格","Please use \"Art Nouveau\" (アールヌーボー), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #204\n\nWhat it is: Ornament framed by flowing curves of plants and flowers\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a poster from around 1900: outlines turn into flowing thick curves, and leaves, grass and sun rays become ornaments of vines and flowers around the house and tree.\nSpec:\n- Look: thick, flowing curved outlines, framed with ornaments of curving vines and flowers\n- Color: muted ochre, olive and dusty vermilion\n- Feel: a poster from around 1900 (no text in the sample)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For elegant, decorative packaging, labels or posters.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/204.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用新艺术运动风格设计茶叶罐标签：以藤蔓和花朵的流动曲线勾边，用暗土黄和橄榄绿。"],
  "205": ["artstyle",13,"Risograph 孔版印刷","两三种油墨略微错位叠印","Please use \"Risograph print\" (リソグラフ), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #205\n\nWhat it is: Two or three inks overlapping slightly out of register\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a print in two inks, yellow and teal; the two layers overlap slightly out of register, with ink grain and paper texture visible.\nSpec:\n- Medium: stencil printing with two or three inks (Risograph)\n- Look: misregistration between layers, ink grain and paper texture stand out; the sample uses yellow and teal\n- Note: two colors blended smoothly look like a duotone (#116); keep the offset and grain\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For the feel of zines, flyers and indie posters.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/205.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 Risograph 孔版印刷做唱片店传单：只用黄色和青绿两种油墨，让版的错位和油墨颗粒看得见。"],
  "206": ["artstyle",14,"层叠纸雕","彩纸剪开层层叠放，靠阴影做出纵深","Please use \"Layered paper art\" (重ね切り絵), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #206\n\nWhat it is: Cut colored paper stacked in layers, with shadows giving depth\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes many layers of cut colored paper; shadows fall where the layers step, giving depth.\nSpec:\n- Material: cut colored paper stacked in many layers\n- Look: shadows fall at each step between layers, giving depth\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For warm, dimensional visuals like a picture book or a card.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/206.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用层叠纸雕做海底的鱼和珊瑚：叠很多层剪好的彩纸，用层间阴影做出纵深。"],
  "207": ["artstyle",15,"扁平插画","只有平涂色块，没有线条和阴影","Please use \"Flat illustration\" (フラットイラスト), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #207\n\nWhat it is: Flat fills only, with no outlines or shading\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a picture made only of flat areas of color, with no outlines and no shadows.\nSpec:\n- Look: shapes made only of flat fills of color\n- Avoid: outlines, shadows and gradients\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For clean illustrations on websites, in apps or in slides.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/207.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用扁平插画画居家办公的人：不要轮廓线、阴影和渐变，只用平涂色块。"],
  "208": ["artstyle",16,"线稿","只用单色线条，不上色","Please use \"Line art\" (ラインアート), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #208\n\nWhat it is: Drawn only with lines in one color, no fill\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a detailed drawing in one dark navy pen on cream paper, with every roof tile, leaf, blade of grass and sun ray drawn in line.\nSpec:\n- Medium: one dark navy pen on cream paper\n- Look: fine lines only, with every detail drawn in; the line weight varies\n- Avoid: fills and shaded areas\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For coloring pages, field guides or packaging where the beauty of the line should show.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/208.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用线稿画老街景：只用一支深蓝色笔的细线，不上色，不画阴影面。"],
  "209": ["artstyle",17,"像素画","用方格像素画出的游戏风","Please use \"Pixel art\" (ドット絵（ピクセルアート）), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #209\n\nWhat it is: Game-style pictures drawn in visible square pixels\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a flat, game-style picture made of square pixels, with no depth and every pixel clearly visible.\nSpec:\n- Look: low resolution with every pixel (square) clearly visible\n- View: a flat picture seen from the front, with no depth (for a build of cubes, see Voxel art #210)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For game-like or retro icons and banners.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/209.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用像素画画勇者和宝箱：正面的平面画，低分辨率，方格清晰可见。"],
  "210": ["artstyle",18,"体素艺术","用小立方体堆成的3D","Please use \"Voxel art\" (ボクセルアート), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #210\n\nWhat it is: 3D built from small stacked cubes\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a 3D diorama of stacked small cubes; the house, tree, sun and hill are all made of cubes with light on top and shade on the sides.\nSpec:\n- Build: everything as a 3D model of small stacked cube blocks\n- Look: light and shade on the top and side faces of each cube so it reads as 3D; rendered slightly from above\n- Note: not a flat pixel-art picture (#209)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For game-like 3D or a cute diorama.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/210.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用体素艺术做一座有灯塔的小岛：全部用小立方体搭成，稍微俯视，每个面都有明暗。"],
  "211": ["artstyle",19,"低多边形（Low poly）","用三角面拼成的3D","Please use \"Low poly\" (ローポリ), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #211\n\nWhat it is: 3D built from flat triangular faces\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes 3D made only of triangular faces; each face has its own shade, so the forms look faceted.\nSpec:\n- Build: 3D made only of triangular faces with no gaps\n- Look: each face has its own shade of color; faceted forms\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For simple, modern 3D backgrounds or icons.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/211.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用低多边形做山和湖的风景：只用无缝拼接的三角面，每个面明暗不同。"],
  "212": ["artstyle",20,"纸模型","纸张折叠粘贴组成的立体模型","Please use \"Papercraft\" (ペーパークラフト), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #212\n\nWhat it is: Paper folded and glued into 3D models\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a photo of models folded from colored card stock: the house is a box, the tree and sun are polyhedra, and folds, glue tabs and cut edges show.\nSpec:\n- Build: 3D models of colored card stock, cut from a template, folded and glued\n- Look: crisp fold edges, small glue tabs sticking out, white cut edges of the paper; a photo taken on a desk from the front at an angle\n- Note: not a white-only relief, and not the flat stacked layers of Layered paper art (#206)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For hand-made 3D product images, or to show crafts and teaching materials.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/212.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用纸模型做一个小动物园：用彩色卡纸折叠组装，拍成能看到折痕和粘贴边的照片风。"],
  "213": ["artstyle",21,"黏土动画风","用黏土捏成、留着指纹的立体造型","Please use \"Clay animation style\" (クレイアニメ風), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #213\n\nWhat it is: Clay models with fingerprints still visible\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes 3D models made of clay, with fingerprints and clay texture on the surface.\nSpec:\n- Material: 3D models made of modeling clay\n- Look: rounded forms with fingerprints and clay texture left on the surface\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For friendly, playful characters and scenes.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/213.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把早餐餐桌做成黏土动画风：用黏土模型，保留指纹和黏土质感。"],
  "214": ["artstyle",22,"刺绣","用彩线在布上绣出图案","Please use \"Embroidery\" (刺繍), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #214\n\nWhat it is: A picture stitched into fabric with colored thread\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes embroidery in colored thread on fabric, with the stitches and the weave of the cloth visible.\nSpec:\n- Material: fabric and colored thread\n- Look: the direction of each stitch and the weave of the cloth are visible\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: For merchandise, packaging or seasonal greetings that should feel warm and hand-made.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/214.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用刺绣做一枚季节花朵的布章：用彩线绣在布上，让针脚和布纹看得见。"],
  "215": ["artstyle",23,"合成器浪潮（Synthwave）","80年代风的霓虹网格与条纹夕阳","Please use \"Synthwave\" (シンセウェイヴ), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #215\n\nWhat it is: 1980s-style neon grid and striped sunset\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes an 1980s neon world: the ground is a glowing purple and cyan grid, the sun a big striped sunset, and the house and tree neon outlines.\nSpec:\n- Color: purple, cyan and pink neon\n- Look: a neon grid for the ground, a big sunset with horizontal stripes, neon outlines\n- Feel: 1980s retro-futurism\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out) (this sample is cropped taller so the grid on the ground shows)\nWhen to use it: For retro-futuristic music, game or event visuals.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/215.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用合成器浪潮风格画一辆在海边公路上的跑车：紫色和青色的霓虹网格地面，加一颗带横条纹的大夕阳。"],
  "216": ["artstyle",24,"蓝图","蓝底白线的设计图","Please use \"Blueprint\" (ブループリント（設計図風）), one of the names in \"Art styles for image generation\".\nMotion Prompt #216\n\nWhat it is: A technical drawing in white lines on blue\nWhat the sample shows: The same line drawing becomes a technical drawing in fine white lines on blue, with a few dimension and construction lines.\nSpec:\n- Look: a drawing in fine white lines on a blue ground\n- Lines: a few dimension and construction lines (the sample has no numbers or text)\n- Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)\nWhen to use it: To show how a product works, or to give a \"being planned\" feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/216.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把新椅子的构想画成蓝图：蓝底白色细线，加少量尺寸线和辅助线。"],
  "217": ["diagram",1,"维恩图","用重叠的圆表示共同点","Please use \"Venn diagram\" (ベン図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #217\n\nWhat it is: Overlapping circles that show what is shared\nWhat the sample shows: Two circles slide in from the sides and overlap, and only the shared part turns dark blue.\nSpec:\n- Circles: two circles of radius 78 px; A on the left in light blue with a blue outline, B on the right in light gray with a gray outline; only the overlap is filled dark blue\n- Motion: fade in from 0.3 s to 0.7 s (ease-out), then the centers move from ±150 px to ±44 px from the middle between 0.5 s and 1.6 s (cubic ease-in-out)\n- Labels: A and B (26 px) on the outer side of each circle\n- #240 Concentric circle diagram nests circles inside each other; a Venn diagram sets them side by side and overlaps only part\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show what two or more things share and where they differ, on one slide.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/217.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用维恩图比较线上课程和线下课程：两个圆，在重叠处写三个共同点。"],
  "218": ["diagram",2,"四象限矩阵（2×2）","用纵横两条轴分成四块","Please use \"2x2 matrix\" (4象限マトリクス（2×2）), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #218\n\nWhat it is: Two axes that split items into four quadrants\nWhat the sample shows: Two axes grow out from the center, four areas appear and dots are placed; only the top-right area and its dot are blue.\nSpec:\n- Axes: grow out from the center from 0.4 s to 1.0 s (168 px to each side, 86 px up and down, cubic ease-in-out), with arrowheads at the right and top ends\n- Areas: four 154×78 px boxes with 10 px corners, 8 px from the axes; they fade in over 0.35 s in the order top-right, top-left, bottom-left, bottom-right, starting at 1.0 s, 0.08 s apart. Top-right is light blue, the rest light gray\n- Dots: seven dots from 1.45 s, 0.1 s apart, each popping in over 0.3 s (ease-out-back, a slight overshoot); the one in the top-right is blue (radius 12 px), the others gray (radius 8 px)\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To sort options by two criteria and point to the one to aim for (top right).\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/218.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把 10 个新业务候选放进四象限矩阵：横轴是市场规模，纵轴是实现难易度，突出右上象限。"],
  "219": ["diagram",3,"逻辑树","把一个问题按分支拆解","Please use \"Logic tree (issue tree)\" (ロジックツリー), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #219\n\nWhat it is: One question broken down into branches\nWhat the sample shows: From the \"?\" box on the left, the tree branches to the right, 1 → 2 → 4, joined by elbow lines.\nSpec:\n- Root: a 66×50 px blue box with a white \"?\" at the left (x = 82), popping in at 0.4 s over 0.3 s (ease-out-back)\n- Level 2: two 76×34 px mid-blue boxes at x = 248; their elbow lines draw from 0.75 s to 1.15 s and the boxes pop in at 1.05 s and 1.13 s\n- Level 3: four 92×26 px light-blue boxes at x = 426; their lines draw over 0.4 s starting at 1.35 s, 0.06 s apart, and the boxes pop in from 1.65 s, 0.08 s apart\n- Lines: gray, 3 px, from the right edge of the parent, bending halfway down or up, into the left edge of the child (drawn with cubic ease-in-out)\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To break a problem or goal down completely and list causes or actions.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/219.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用逻辑树拆解“销售额为什么不增长”，分三层，从左向右分支。"],
  "220": ["diagram",4,"金字塔图","由下往上叠起的层级","Please use \"Pyramid diagram\" (ピラミッド図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #220\n\nWhat it is: Layers stacked from the base to the top\nWhat the sample shows: A triangle in four layers stacks up from the bottom, each layer dropping into place; only the top layer is dark blue.\nSpec:\n- Shape: a triangle from y = 16 (apex) to y = 192 (base), 336 px wide at the base, cut into four layers with 6 px gaps\n- Colors from the bottom: light gray, light blue, mid blue, dark blue\n- Motion: from the bottom layer up, 0.32 s apart (0.4, 0.72, 1.04, 1.36 s), each layer drops 34 px into place over 0.4 s while fading in (ease-out)\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show stages that build on each other, or levels that get smaller toward the top.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/220.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用金字塔图展示马斯洛需求层次的五个层级，从下往上叠，只把最上层的颜色加深。"],
  "221": ["diagram",5,"思维导图","从中心向四周发散联想","Please use \"Mind map\" (マインドマップ), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #221\n\nWhat it is: Ideas branching out from a central topic\nWhat the sample shows: Six curved branches grow from the central \"テーマ\" (topic) to both sides, then thinner twigs with small word nodes.\nSpec:\n- Center: a 100×44 px blue rounded box with white text \"テーマ\" (19 px), popping in at 0.4 s over 0.3 s (ease-out-back)\n- Branches: six cubic Bézier curves (3 px), three to each side, growing over 0.5 s from 0.7 s, 0.09 s apart, each ending in a 54×24 px node; mid blue and gray alternate\n- Twigs: thinner 2.5 px curves grow from the branch ends over 0.35 s (from 1.45 s), each ending in a small 40×18 px node\n- Shape: curved branches and word nodes, unlike the nested rings of #240 Concentric circle diagram\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: For brainstorming, or to spread out and organize ideas around one topic.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/221.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用思维导图为新产品想名字：产品放在中心，分 6 个分支，每个分支 2 个方案。"],
  "222": ["diagram",6,"流程图","用菱形分支一步步走完流程","Please use \"Flowchart\" (フローチャート), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #222\n\nWhat it is: Steps you follow, with diamond-shaped decisions\nWhat the sample shows: Start → step → diamond decision → step → end appear in one row, with a loop arrow from the decision back to the first step; then a dot walks the path, loops back once and goes on to the end.\nSpec:\n- Shapes: start and end are 66×36 px pills (gray), steps are 72×40 px boxes (light blue), the decision is a diamond 92 px wide and 72 px tall (blue, white \"?\"), all in one row at y = 80\n- Order: they pop in at 0.4, 0.8, 1.2, 1.6 and 1.95 s (0.3 s, ease-out-back); the arrows between them grow over 0.22 s from 0.6, 1.0, 1.4 and 1.75 s, with 10 px heads\n- Loop: an arrow from the bottom of the diamond down to y = 172 and back up into the first step draws from 2.0 s to 2.45 s\n- Marker: a dark gray dot (radius 8 px) follows start → step → decision → loop → step → decision → step → end from 2.6 s to 3.8 s (cubic ease-in-out), appearing 2.5–2.65 s and leaving 3.8–4.0 s\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show a procedure step by step, including where it branches on a condition.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/222.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把报销流程画成流程图，5 步以内，用菱形表示“是否超过上限”的分支。"],
  "223": ["diagram",7,"循环图","箭头连成一圈，循环往复","Please use \"Cycle diagram\" (サイクル図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #223\n\nWhat it is: Arrows in a ring that keeps going round\nWhat the sample shows: Circles numbered 1 to 4 sit on a ring, arrows draw one after another until the ring closes, then a blue highlight goes round once.\nSpec:\n- Layout: four light-blue circles (radius 26 px, numbered 1–4) at the top, right, bottom and left of an ellipse 128 px wide and 70 px tall (radii), popping in from 0.4 s, 0.32 s apart\n- Arrows: arcs along the ellipse from each circle to the next (mid blue, 3 px, 13 px heads), drawn over 0.28 s from 0.7 s, 0.32 s apart; the ring closes at 1.94 s\n- Highlight: from 2.2 s to 3.8 s a solid blue fill moves 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, 0.4 s per step, with soft edges\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show a process that returns to the start and keeps repeating, such as PDCA.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/223.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用循环图展示 PDCA：4 个阶段排成一圈，用箭头连到下一个阶段。"],
  "224": ["diagram",8,"鱼骨图","以鱼骨的形状列出原因","Please use \"Fishbone diagram\" (フィッシュボーン図（特性要因図）), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #224\n\nWhat it is: Causes laid out like the bones of a fish\nWhat the sample shows: A spine runs right to the head (the result); slanted bones join it from above and below, each with small side bones (the causes).\nSpec:\n- Spine: after the tail (0.35–0.6 s), a line from x = 52 to x = 404 (dark gray, 3 px, 14 px head) grows from 0.45 s to 1.0 s; the head, a 92×56 px blue box reading \"結果\" (result), pops in at 0.95 s\n- Bones: six bones from x = 150, 258 and 366 on the spine, slanting up-left and down-left (62 px across, 80 px up or down, mid blue, 3 px), drawn over 0.35 s from 1.1 s, 0.14 s per column, the lower ones 0.07 s later\n- Side bones: at 36% and 68% along each bone, a 26 px horizontal line to the left (gray, 2.5 px), growing over 0.22 s just after the bone, 0.08 s apart\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To list the possible causes of one result, grouped by kind.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/224.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用鱼骨图找出解约增加的原因：鱼头写“解约增加”，鱼骨分为人员、产品、价格、客服 4 根。"],
  "225": ["diagram",9,"散点图","用点的分布看两个数字的关系","Please use \"Scatter plot\" (散布図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #225\n\nWhat it is: Dots that show how two numbers relate\nWhat the sample shows: Small blue dots pop in from left to right on L-shaped axes, scattered upward to the right, and a dashed trend line follows.\nSpec:\n- Axes: L-shaped axes from x = 96 to 448 and y = 24 to 184 (gray, 2.5 px) with three light horizontal grid lines; they stay for the whole cycle\n- Dots: 52 dots (fixed seed) of radius 5 px in blue, scattered upward to the right, each popping in over 0.28 s (ease-out-back) from left to right between 0.4 s and 1.65 s according to its x\n- Trend line: a gray dashed line (7 px dash, 8 px gap) grows from bottom-left to top-right from 1.85 s to 2.5 s\n- Unlike #226 Bubble chart: many small dots, all the same size\n- End: the axes and grid stay; only the data fades out from 4.15 s to 4.55 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To show whether two numbers are related, for example whether one rises when the other does.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/225.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用散点图展示广告费和销售额的关系：12 个月每月一个点，再叠一条虚线趋势线。"],
  "226": ["diagram",10,"气泡图","用圆的大小表示第三个数字","Please use \"Bubble chart\" (バブルチャート), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #226\n\nWhat it is: Circle size shows a third number\nWhat the sample shows: Five semi-transparent circles of different sizes grow one by one on L-shaped axes; only the largest is dark blue.\nSpec:\n- Axes: the same L-shaped axes and grid lines as #225 Scatter plot; they stay for the whole cycle\n- Circles: five, radius 14–44 px, semi-transparent fill (opacity 0.5; the largest is dark blue at 0.42) with a 2.5 px outline in the same color\n- Motion: from 0.45 s, 0.24 s apart, each grows over 0.5 s with a small overshoot (ease-out-back)\n- Unlike #225 Scatter plot: only a few points, and the circle size carries a third number\n- End: the axes and grid stay; only the data fades out from 4.15 s to 4.55 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To compare three numbers at once: across, up and size.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/226.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用气泡图展示 5 个商品：横轴是价格，纵轴是满意度，气泡大小代表销售额。"],
  "227": ["diagram",11,"热力图","用颜色深浅填充表格的格子","Please use \"Heatmap\" (ヒートマップ), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #227\n\nWhat it is: Table cells shaded by their value\nWhat the sample shows: The cells of a 12 × 5 table fill with shades of blue in a wave from top-left to bottom-right, then turn back to gray the same way.\nSpec:\n- Table: 12 columns × 5 rows of 30×28 px cells (4 px corners, 4 px gaps), with short gray bars as row labels on the left\n- Colors: from light gray to one of five blues (light to dark) by value; the values (fixed seed) form a wave\n- Fill: each cell takes its color over 0.32 s (ease-out) starting at 0.4 s + column × 0.075 s + row × 0.06 s, so it spreads diagonally from top-left to bottom-right\n- Clear: from 3.95 s + column × 0.025 s + row × 0.02 s each cell goes back to gray over 0.22 s (cubic ease-in-out)\n- The table itself (cells and labels) stays for the whole cycle\nWhen to use it: To show at a glance where a table, such as weekday by hour, is high or low.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/227.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用热力图展示按星期和时段统计的到店人数：7 行 × 12 列，人越多蓝色越深。"],
  "228": ["diagram",12,"雷达图","用蛛网的形状比较多个项目","Please use \"Radar chart\" (レーダーチャート), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #228\n\nWhat it is: A spider web that compares several items\nWhat the sample shows: On a six-axis spider web, a gray polygon spreads out from the center, then a blue one spreads with a slight overshoot.\nSpec:\n- Scale: four nested hexagons up to radius 86 px (the outer one darker) and six spokes; they stay for the whole cycle\n- Comparison: a gray polygon (values 0.46–0.74, fill opacity 0.22) spreads out from the center from 0.4 s to 1.1 s (ease-out)\n- Main: a blue polygon (values 0.92, 0.58, 0.84, 0.4, 0.76, 0.52; fill opacity 0.28, 3 px outline, dots on the corners) spreads from 0.95 s to 1.85 s, a 55:45 blend of ease-out and ease-out-back for a slight overshoot\n- End: the axes and grid stay; only the data fades out from 4.15 s to 4.55 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To compare the balance of several items, or the strengths and weaknesses of two things.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/228.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用雷达图比较本公司和竞争对手：价格、质量、服务等 6 个项目，本公司用蓝色叠在上面。"],
  "229": ["diagram",13,"仪表图","用半圆表盘和指针显示达成率","Please use \"Gauge chart\" (ゲージチャート), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #229\n\nWhat it is: A half-circle dial and needle that show progress\nWhat the sample shows: The needle of a half-circle dial swings past, wobbles and settles at 72%; the blue band and the number follow the needle.\nSpec:\n- Dial: a half-circle band of radius 120 px and 30 px thick (gray), with ticks every 10% (longer at 0, 50 and 100%)\n- Needle: starts at 0.5 s and follows a damped spring 1 − e^(−3.2t)·cos(7.5t), swinging past and wobbling before it settles at 72%\n- Band and number: the band is blue up to the needle, and the percentage (26 px) below matches the needle\n- End: from 4.1 s to 4.5 s the needle, band and number go back to 0% (cubic ease-in-out; one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To show with one number how far you are toward a target.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/229.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用仪表图展示本月销售目标的达成率：半圆表盘，指针指向 72%。"],
  "230": ["diagram",14,"组合图（柱形图＋折线图）","柱形和折线叠在一张图里（左右两个刻度）","Please use \"Combo chart (bar + line)\" (複合グラフ（棒＋折れ線）), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #230\n\nWhat it is: Bars and a line on one chart, with two scales\nWhat the sample shows: Six bars grow against the left scale (gray ticks), then a line is drawn left to right against the right scale (blue ticks).\nSpec:\n- Axes: the left axis and its five ticks are gray, the right axis and its five ticks blue, with three light grid lines; they stay for the whole cycle\n- Bars: six light-blue bars 36 px wide grow up over 0.36 s (ease-out), from 0.4 s, 0.12 s apart\n- Line: a 3.5 px blue line joins six points from left to right between 1.3 s and 2.2 s at an even speed; the points are ring markers (radius 7 px) popping in from 1.25 s, 0.18 s apart\n- End: the axes and grid stay; only the data fades out from 4.15 s to 4.55 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To show two numbers with different units on one chart, such as sales and margin.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/230.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用组合图展示每月销售额和利润率：销售额用柱形对应左侧坐标轴，利润率用折线对应右侧坐标轴。"],
  "231": ["diagram",15,"象形图（图标阵列）","用人或物的图标数量表示比例","Please use \"Pictogram chart (icon array)\" (絵グラフ（ピクトグラム）), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #231\n\nWhat it is: A count of people or icons that shows a share\nWhat the sample shows: Ten person icons appear in gray in one row, the first three turn blue one by one, and \"30%\" counts up.\nSpec:\n- People: ten faceless person icons, 80 px tall and 32 px apart, in a single row (a grid would read as a heatmap)\n- Entrance: they pop in from 0.35 s, 0.06 s apart, over 0.3 s each (ease-out-back), all gray\n- Color: the first three turn from gray to blue over 0.25 s each, from 1.25 s, 0.22 s apart\n- Number: \"30%\" (46 px, blue) on the left counts up from 0 between 1.25 s and 1.94 s, with \"10人中3人\" (3 in 10 people) below\n- End: the axes and grid stay; only the data fades out from 4.15 s to 4.55 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To make a share feel like a count of people, for readers who do not like numbers.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/231.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用象形图展示有副业的人所占比例：一排 10 个人形图标，其中 3 个涂成蓝色。"],
  "232": ["diagram",16,"百分比堆积条形图","把条按比例分段，比较构成","Please use \"100% stacked bar chart\" (帯グラフ（100%積み上げ）), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #232\n\nWhat it is: Bars split by percentage to compare the breakdown\nWhat the sample shows: Four bars of the same length fill from left to right, dotted lines join the borders between neighbouring bars, and the first part shows its %.\nSpec:\n- Bars: four bars 390 px long, 28 px tall and 16 px apart, each cut into four parts (dark blue, mid blue, light blue, gray) with 2 px gaps\n- Motion: from the top bar down, 0.16 s apart, each fills from left to right over 0.7 s (cubic ease-in-out)\n- Dotted lines: gray dotted lines (4 px dash, 4 px gap) join the same border on neighbouring bars, fading in from 1.6 s to 2.0 s\n- Percent: a white number (16 px) in the middle of each first part, fading in over 0.25 s from 0.75 s after its bar starts\n- End: the axes and grid stay; only the data fades out from 4.15 s to 4.55 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To compare only the breakdown (shares) of each group, not the totals.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/232.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用百分比堆积条形图比较各年龄段使用的设备：4 个年龄段画成等长的条，用虚线连接分界。"],
  "233": ["diagram",17,"甘特图","在日期刻度上用横条排出工作期间","Please use \"Gantt chart\" (ガントチャート), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #233\n\nWhat it is: Bars on a date scale that show when each task runs\nWhat the sample shows: A date scale (1–8) on top and tasks A–E on the left; bars start at staggered columns and grow to the right one after another.\nSpec:\n- Scale: dates 1–8 across the top (52 px columns) with light vertical lines; they stay for the whole cycle\n- Tasks: five rows A–E on the left, 27 px apart; bars are 20 px tall with 6 px corners, running A 0–2, B 1.5–3.5, C 3–4.5, D 3.5–6.5 and E 6–8 (in columns)\n- Motion: from 0.4 s, 0.3 s apart, each bar grows from its left end to the right over 0.5 s (ease-out)\n- Color: D is dark blue, the others mid blue\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show how long each task in a project takes, and how the tasks overlap and follow each other.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/233.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用甘特图排网站制作的工期：8 周的时间刻度，用横条排出 5 项工作的时间段。"],
  "234": ["diagram",18,"时间轴","在一条线上按时间顺序排列事件","Please use \"Timeline\" (タイムライン), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #234\n\nWhat it is: Events in order along one line\nWhat the sample shows: One line is drawn from left to right; as its tip passes each point, a dot and a month label appear, alternating above and below. The last one is blue.\nSpec:\n- Line: from x = 36 to x = 503 at y = 106 (dark gray, 3 px), drawn from 0.4 s to 2.0 s (cubic ease-in-out), with an arrowhead at the right end\n- Dots: five (April, June, August, October, December: 4月 … 12月), each popping in over 0.25 s at the moment the tip reaches it (radius 7 px; the last one blue, 10 px)\n- Labels: from each dot a 22 px stem grows up or down, alternating, to a 64×32 px rounded tag (white with the month in 18 px; the last one blue with white text), over 0.3 s\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show events in time order: a history, how something came about, or a plan.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/234.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用时间轴展示公司沿革：在一条横线上按年份排 5 个事件，标签上下交替放置。"],
  "235": ["diagram",19,"漏斗图","人数逐级减少的漏斗","Please use \"Funnel chart\" (ファネル図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #235\n\nWhat it is: Numbers narrowing stage by stage\nWhat the sample shows: Four centered bars grow out from the middle one after another from the top, each shorter than the one above, joined by light gray trapezoids.\nSpec:\n- Bars: 470, 350, 236 and 132 px wide, 34 px tall, 10 px apart, 7 px corners; light blue, mid blue, mid blue, dark blue\n- Motion: from the top, 0.36 s apart starting at 0.4 s, each bar grows out from the middle over 0.45 s (ease-out)\n- Joints: light gray trapezoids (opacity 0.8) narrowing from the bar above to the bar below fill the gaps\n- Numbers: 100, 58, 27 and 9 in the middle of the bars (20 px), fading in over 0.25 s from 0.3 s after each bar starts\n- The bars are separate and centered so they do not read as #220 Pyramid diagram upside down\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show how the count drops at each stage, such as visit → sign-up → purchase.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/235.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用漏斗图展示落地页从访问到购买的过程：4 个阶段，每段写上人数，居中排列、逐级变短。"],
  "236": ["diagram",20,"客户旅程地图","并列各阶段的行为和心情起伏","Please use \"Customer journey map\" (カスタマージャーニーマップ), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #236\n\nWhat it is: Actions and feelings at each stage\nWhat the sample shows: Five stage headers and action cards line up, then a feeling line rises and falls from left to right, with a smiling or frowning mark on each point.\nSpec:\n- Frame: five columns with vertical dividers; the stage headers on top are plain rounded boxes (not arrows; the middle one gray), appearing from 0.35 s, 0.1 s apart\n- Actions: a white card under each header (text as gray bars), rising 8 px while it appears over 0.3 s, from 0.6 s, 0.1 s apart\n- Feeling: against a dotted neutral line at y = 150, a smooth blue curve (3.5 px) through +0.35, +0.7, −0.6, +0.15 and +0.85 (× 36 px) is drawn from left to right between 1.25 s and 2.25 s\n- Marks: as the line reaches each point a face (radius 12 px) pops in: a blue smile above the neutral line, a gray frown below it\n- There are no arrows across lanes (unlike #238 Swimlane diagram)\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To see what customers do at each stage and where their mood drops.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/236.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","为报名线上英语课的人做一张客户旅程地图：分 5 个阶段写出行为和心情，用一条线表示心情起伏。"],
  "237": ["diagram",21,"矩形树图","用方块大小表示整体的构成","Please use \"Treemap\" (ツリーマップ), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #237\n\nWhat it is: Rectangle sizes show the parts of a whole\nWhat the sample shows: A dashed outer frame fills up with seven rectangles of different sizes, biggest first.\nSpec:\n- Frame: a 439×172 px dashed outline (6 px dash, 6 px gap); it stays for the whole cycle\n- Rectangles: seven, with 5 px corners: the large A on the left (206×172 px, dark blue), then B (140×96 px), C, D and three small ones; dark blue, mid blue, light blue, gray\n- Motion: from 0.4 s, 0.22 s apart, each grows from 0.55× to full size over 0.4 s with an overshoot (ease-out-back) while fading in\n- Labels: letters at the top-left of A–D (A in 24 px white, the others 20 px)\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show at a glance how much of the whole each part takes up.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/237.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用矩形树图展示按商品划分的销售额构成：方块大小对应销售额，最大的商品用深蓝色。"],
  "238": ["diagram",22,"泳道图","按负责人分泳道排列步骤","Please use \"Swimlane diagram\" (スイムレーン図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #238\n\nWhat it is: Lanes for each person or team split the steps\nWhat the sample shows: Three lanes named on the left (顧客 customer, 営業 sales, 制作 production); step boxes appear one by one, moving between lanes, joined by elbow arrows.\nSpec:\n- Lanes: three white lanes 60 px tall, with gray lane names (18 px) in a 62 px column on the left; they stay for the whole cycle\n- Boxes: five 56×30 px rounded boxes from x = 138 to 474, in the lanes customer → sales → production → sales → customer, popping in over 0.28 s (ease-out-back) from 0.4 s, 0.38 s apart; the last one dark blue\n- Arrows: from the right edge of the previous box, across and then up or down into the next (dark gray, 2.5 px, 9 px head), growing over 0.26 s from 0.24 s before each box\n- Unlike #233 Gantt chart: no date scale; the lane names and the arrows crossing lanes carry it\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show who does what, and when, in a process shared by several people or teams.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/238.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用泳道图画出从咨询到交付的流程：分成客户、销售、制作 3 条泳道，用箭头连接各步骤。"],
  "239": ["diagram",23,"V 形流程图","横向排列箭头形状的步骤","Please use \"Chevron process\" (矢羽根図（シェブロン）), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #239\n\nWhat it is: Arrow-shaped steps in a row\nWhat the sample shows: Arrow-shaped steps 1 to 5 slide in from the left one after another, each with short notes below; the blue gets darker to the right.\nSpec:\n- Shape: five chevrons 104 px wide and 74 px tall (point depth 24 px, 6 px gaps); from the second on, the left side is notched to fit the one before\n- Colors: light blue, light blue, mid blue, mid blue, dark blue, with the numbers 1–5 (24 px) in the middle\n- Motion: from 0.4 s, 0.3 s apart, each slides in from 34 px to the left over 0.42 s while fading in (ease-out)\n- Notes: two gray bars (62 px and 44 px long) under each step, fading in over 0.3 s from 0.25 s after the step starts\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show steps that follow each other, such as a training schedule or a rollout, in one row.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/239.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 V 形流程图展示 5 天培训的安排：横向排 5 个箭头，每个下面写两行内容。"],
  "240": ["diagram",24,"同心圆图","用嵌套的圆逐层缩小市场范围","Please use \"Concentric circle diagram\" (同心円図), one of the names in \"Diagrams and charts for slides\".\nMotion Prompt #240\n\nWhat it is: Nested circles that narrow down a market\nWhat the sample shows: Outer, middle and inner circles grow from the same center one after another, nested inside each other, with the labels TAM, SAM and SOM.\nSpec:\n- Circles: filled circles of radius 91, 61 and 31 px on one center (light blue, mid blue, dark blue from the outside), with a faint gray guide ring for the outer circle that stays\n- Motion: from the outer circle in, 0.45 s apart (0.4, 0.85, 1.3 s), each grows from the center over 0.5 s, a 60:40 blend of ease-out and ease-out-back for a slight overshoot\n- Labels: TAM and SAM in the bands between the circles, SOM in the inner circle (18 px), fading in over 0.3 s from 0.55 s after each circle starts\n- Unlike #217 Venn diagram: the circles are nested, not set side by side\n- End: the whole figure fades out from 4.1 s to 4.5 s and the card stays empty until the 4.7 s loop\nWhen to use it: To show how you narrow down from the whole to the part you target, as in TAM, SAM and SOM.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/240.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/diagram.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用同心圆图展示线上学习的市场规模：从外到内分为 TAM、SAM、SOM 三层，并写上金额。"],
  "001": ["motion",1,"弹性入场","元素弹跳着出现","Please use \"Pop-in\" (ポップイン), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #001\n\nWhat it is: Pops into view with a small bounce\nWhat the sample shows: An app icon pops in with a bounce, then a notification badge pops in a moment later.\nSpec:\n- One pop per 2.35 s (twice per 4.7 s cycle: a star on coral first, then a heart on blue).\n- Icon: 116 px rounded square (radius 30). From 0.28 s, scale 0→1 with a spring: 1 − e^(−6.5t)·cos(15t), peaking at about 1.26.\n- At the same time, rotation −0.35 rad (about −20°) → 0 with a spring: 1 − e^(−6t)·cos(11t).\n- Badge: yellow circle, radius 25, with \"1\", at the icon's top-right (+52, −52). Starts at 0.62 s with spring 1 − e^(−7t)·cos(17t).\n- Exit: 1.86–2.12 s. Scale is multiplied by (1 − backIn, s = 2.2), so it swells slightly and then shrinks to 0.\n- Floor shadow: 62 × 8 ellipse that scales with the icon (clamped to 0–1).\nWhen to use it: Use it to bring in a small element such as an icon, button or badge with a light accent.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/001.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让标志以弹性入场出现，时长约 0.4 s，略微超出目标尺寸后回弹。"],
  "002": ["motion",2,"交错动画","多个元素错开时间依次出现","Please use \"Stagger\" (スタガー), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #002\n\nWhat it is: Items appear one after another, slightly offset in time\nWhat the sample shows: Chart bars rise one after another from the left, each slightly delayed.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 2.35 s. Seven bars (width 44, gap 20, heights 52, 84, 68, 112, 92, 136, 158), coloured blue, coral, yellow, mint in rotation.\n- Bar i (0-based) starts at 0.15 + 0.12·i s and grows from 0 to full height in 0.5 s with backOut (s = 2.6), anchored at the baseline, overshooting and settling.\n- White dot (radius 6.5, 16 px above the bar top): starts 0.34 s after its bar with spring 1 − e^(−7t)·cos(16t).\n- Exit: bars shrink with cubic ease-in over 0.26 s starting at 1.78 + 0.045·i s; dots vanish first, over 0.2 s from 1.70 + 0.045·i s.\nWhen to use it: Use it to bring in several items (list rows, chart bars, cards) in sequence and lead the eye across them.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/002.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用交错动画让五张卡片从左到右依次入场，每张间隔 0.08 s。"],
  "003": ["motion",3,"放射爆发","元素出现时向外迸出线条和圆点","Please use \"Burst\" (バースト), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #003\n\nWhat it is: Lines and dots burst outward as something appears\nWhat the sample shows: A like heart fills in, and a ring, lines and dots burst outward at the same moment.\nSpec:\n- One burst per 2.35 s. A heart (size 46, 7 px outline) sits in the centre.\n- Anticipation: 0.3–0.5 s, scale 1→0.7 (quadratic ease-in-out).\n- Trigger at 0.5 s: the heart fills with coral and scale returns 0.7→1 with spring 1 − e^(−6.5t)·cos(16t).\n- Ring: yellow, radius 44→90 while line width goes 16→0, over 0.6 s with quintic ease-out.\n- 10 radial lines (yellow/mint alternating, width 9): outer end radius 64→130 (y scaled 0.82); length 36 shrinks to 0 between 0.22 and 0.7 s after the trigger.\n- 10 dots (coral/blue alternating, radius 8→4.8): radius 58→150 on an ellipse (x ×1.45, y ×0.78), fading out 0.3–0.72 s after the trigger. The heart fill fades at 1.92–2.2 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it to mark the instant something is triggered or achieved, such as a like, a success or a correct answer.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/003.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","爱心出现时加一次放射爆发：8 根短线在 0.3 s 内淡出。"],
  "004": ["motion",4,"线条描绘","线条像被画出来一样逐渐延伸","Please use \"Line draw\" (ラインドロー), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #004\n\nWhat it is: A line extends as if it were being drawn\nWhat the sample shows: A chart line draws itself on, and is later erased from its starting end.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 4.7 s. Drawn as a trim path: animate the visible range (start fraction to end fraction) of each stroke.\n- Axes (L shape, width 6) draw at 0.08–0.7 s; the line (mint, width 11, a smooth curve through 7 points, round caps) draws at 0.4–1.95 s. Both use cubic ease-in-out.\n- While drawing, a yellow dot (radius 12, white centre radius 5) rides the leading tip.\n- Arrowhead: opens at 1.9–2.2 s with backOut (s = 2.5); wings 26 long, 20 wide.\n- A coral circle (radius 26, width 7) is drawn around one peak at 2.2–2.8 s, clockwise from the top.\n- Erase: circle 3.5–4.0 s, line 3.65–4.45 s, axes 3.85–4.55 s, each shrinking from its starting end. The arrowhead fades at 4.3–4.45 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it when the stroke itself is the point: charts, routes, underlines, hand-drawn circles.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/004.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让图表曲线从左侧开始，在 1.2 s 内逐渐描绘出来。"],
  "005": ["motion",5,"遮罩显现","文字从不可见的边界后移出","Please use \"Mask reveal\" (マスクリビール), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #005\n\nWhat it is: Text rises into view from behind an invisible edge\nWhat the sample shows: Headline text slides out from behind an invisible edge marked by a single line.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 2.35 s. Divider line (coral, 380 × 6, y = 124): grows from the centre at 0.1–0.5 s (cubic ease-in-out), shrinks away at 2.05–2.3 s.\n- Top text (bold 98 px, white): clipped to the area above the line (y 8–119); moves up into place from 120 px below at 0.35–1.0 s, quintic ease-out.\n- Bottom text (32 px, yellow): clipped to the area below the line (y 129–181); moves down into place from 60 px above at 0.55–1.15 s, quintic ease-out.\n- Exit: top text moves 150 px up at 1.7–2.05 s (backIn, s = 1.2, dipping slightly first); bottom text moves 70 px down at 1.75–2.05 s (cubic ease-in).\n- Opacity never changes; the text is hidden only by leaving the clip area.\nWhen to use it: Use it for titles and headings that should appear in a clean, composed way.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/005.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让标题从下方通过遮罩显现，时长 0.6 s，各行稍微错开。"],
  "006": ["motion",6,"打字机效果","文字像打字一样逐字出现","Please use \"Typewriter\" (タイプライター), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #006\n\nWhat it is: Text appears one character at a time, as if typed\nWhat the sample shows: Text is typed into an input field one character at a time, then the send button lights up and is pressed.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 4.7 s. Nine characters appear in a white input field (471 × 92, radius 30), one every 0.24 s starting at 0.3 s (typing ends at 2.46 s).\n- Each new character settles from scale 1.35 to 1: 1 + 0.35·e^(−16t).\n- Cursor (coral, 5 × 44) sits after the last character: solid while typing, otherwise blinking with a 0.94 s period (on for 0.5 s).\n- Send button (radius 30): grey, then a blue disc appears from 2.58 s with spring 1 − e^(−6.5t)·cos(15t).\n- Press: the button shrinks by up to 20% at 2.96–3.21 s (half sine). At 3.13–3.41 s the text moves 70 px up while fading out.\n- The cursor returns to the start once the text is half faded (about 3.27 s); at 3.51–3.81 s the blue fades.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show someone typing: a prompt, a search query, a chat message.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/006.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给这句话添加打字机效果，每个字 0.05 s，末尾保留光标。"],
  "007": ["motion",7,"数字递增","数字快速增长到目标值","Please use \"Count-up\" (カウントアップ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #007\n\nWhat it is: A number runs up quickly to its final value\nWhat the sample shows: A number races upward and locks onto its final value.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 4.7 s. Fades in at 0.1–0.4 s and out at 4.0–4.4 s.\n- Number (bold 104 px): 0→2,480 over 0.45–2.9 s. Value = round(target × (1 − (1 − p)^4)): fast at first, slow at the end.\n- Thousands separator included. Every digit has the same width and the number is right-aligned, so it does not jitter sideways.\n- Lands at 2.9 s: colour switches white→yellow and scale does a small bounce, 1 + 0.07·e^(−7t)·cos(15t).\n- Up-arrow chip on the left (mint circle, radius 34): appears from 0.35 s with spring 1 − e^(−7t)·cos(14t); while counting it shakes vertically by 6 px × (1 − p)^3 × sin(30u).\n- Bar below (330 × 12, blue→mint gradient): fills in proportion to value ÷ target.\nWhen to use it: Use it to make a figure feel big or growing: revenue, user counts, completion rates.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/007.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用数字递增让数字在 1.5 s 内从 0 增长到 1,280，末尾减速。"],
  "008": ["motion",8,"动态排版","文字随含义和节奏移动、缩放与旋转","Please use \"Kinetic typography\" (キネティックタイポグラフィ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #008\n\nWhat it is: Words move, scale and turn in time with what is said\nWhat the sample shows: Words move the way they mean: one stretches, one bounces, one spins, one slams down.\nSpec:\n- Four words, 1.175 s each (bold 88 px). Each exits in its last 0.2 s, fading out while moving 46 px up (cubic ease-in).\n- Stretch (blue): horizontal scale 0.3→1 with spring 1 − e^(−4.2t)·cos(12t); vertical scale is 1/√(horizontal).\n- Bounce (yellow): characters staggered by 0.1 s; height 78 px × |sin(πt/0.4)| × e^(−2.6t); squashed vertically by up to 16% at each contact.\n- Spin (mint): characters staggered by 0.12 s; rotation −360°→0° over 0.62 s with backOut (s = 1.3); scale 0→1 over 0.25 s, cubic ease-out.\n- Slam (coral, 100 px, slanted): scale 3.4→1 at 0.02–0.2 s with cubic ease-in.\n- After impact: horizontal shake 10 px × e^(−9t) × sin(38t), vertical squash 20% × e^(−11t), and 8 radial lines for 0.4 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it to make key words from narration or lyrics memorable through how they move.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/008.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把旁白做成动态排版，重读词放大，并对齐节拍出现。"],
  "009": ["motion",9,"缓动","动作通过加减速变化而非匀速移动","Please use \"Easing\" (イージング), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #009\n\nWhat it is: Motion speeds up and slows down instead of moving at one speed\nWhat the sample shows: Two squares cover the same distance in the same time: the top one at constant speed, the bottom one eased.\nSpec:\n- One round trip per 4.7 s. Two 62 px squares (radius 16) travel 316 px horizontally: out at 0.2–1.75 s (1.55 s), hold 0.8 s, back at 2.55–4.1 s.\n- Top (constant): linear motion; shape and colour never change.\n- Bottom (eased): cubic-bezier(.86, 0, .14, 1). Slow start, very fast middle, slow stop.\n- The bottom square stretches horizontally up to 1.5× and flattens to 0.8× in proportion to speed (speed ÷ 3.6, clamped to 0–1).\n- Behind it: 3 speed lines (up to 150 px × 0.8–1.25) and 4 ghost copies lagging 0.035 s each.\n- Each rail shows 12 dots marking positions at equal time intervals (evenly spaced on top, bunched at both ends below).\nWhen to use it: Use it on any move, scale or rotation so the motion accelerates and decelerates instead of looking mechanical.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/009.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","为这段移动添加缓出，使其逐渐减速停下。"],
  "010": ["motion",10,"过冲回弹","越过目标后回到目标位置并停稳","Please use \"Overshoot\" (オーバーシュート), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #010\n\nWhat it is: Goes a little past the target, then settles back\nWhat the sample shows: A gauge needle swings past its target, comes back and settles.\nSpec:\n- One pass per 4.7 s. Semicircular gauge (radius 128, stroke 26). Target is 0.7 of the sweep (126° from the left end).\n- Starts at 0.25 s: value = 0.7 × (1 − e^(−4.6t)·cos(10.5t)). About 0.3 s later it is roughly 25% past the target, then it oscillates and settles on the target.\n- The part beyond the target is drawn in coral. A yellow tick marks the target.\n- The filled arc is a blue→mint gradient; the needle is white, width 9.\n- Return: from 3.7 s, value = 0.7 × e^(−7.5t)·cos(8.5t) back to 0 (dipping slightly below 0 before it stops).\nWhen to use it: Use it to give an arriving element energy and a springy feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/010.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给仪表指针加上过冲回弹：先超出目标约 10%，再回弹到位。"],
  "011": ["motion",11,"挤压与拉伸","通过压扁和拉长表现弹性","Please use \"Squash & stretch\" (スクワッシュ＆ストレッチ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #011\n\nWhat it is: Squashes and stretches so that it feels elastic\nWhat the sample shows: A bouncing character squashes on landing and stretches as it takes off.\nSpec:\n- A round character, radius 37. One bounce per 1.175 s (four per 4.7 s), a 92 px parabola. It drifts ±150 px sideways on a sine wave over the cycle.\n- On the ground (first and last 10% of each bounce): vertical scale goes between 0.52 (moment of impact) and 1.28 (moment of leaving) on a quadratic curve.\n- In the air: vertical scale = 1 + 0.28 × s^3, where s is the time offset from the apex (0 at the apex, 1 at take-off and touchdown), so it is stretched where it moves fast.\n- Horizontal scale is always 1 ÷ vertical (volume is preserved). The transform is anchored at the feet.\n- The shadow gets smaller and thinner with height. Short yellow lines flick out left and right at each landing (for about 18% of a bounce).\nWhen to use it: Use it to give a character or logo weight and softness.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/011.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给球落地时加上轻微的挤压与拉伸。"],
  "012": ["motion",12,"形状变形","一种形状平滑变成另一种","Please use \"Shape morph\" (モーフィング), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #012\n\nWhat it is: One shape turns smoothly into another\nWhat the sample shows: A shape changes smoothly from circle to square to star to heart, with its colour.\nSpec:\n- Four shapes, 1.175 s each: circle → square with rounded-off corners → star → heart → back to circle. Base radius 64.\n- Each segment holds first, then morphs to the next shape between 0.62 s and 0.04 s before its end (0.58 s).\n- Every outline is stored as 240 points; points with the same index are linearly interpolated. Progress uses backOut (s = 1.6), so it overshoots slightly.\n- Colour: blue → coral → yellow → mint, blended with quadratic ease-in-out.\n- During the morph the scale swells by 1 + 0.07 × sin(π × progress).\n- Four dots below; the dot for the current shape is larger and coloured.\nWhen to use it: Use it to turn one icon or logo into another without a cut.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/012.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用形状变形让圆形在 0.8 s 内变成星形，同时由蓝色变成黄色。"],
  "013": ["motion",13,"液态动效","形状像液体一样流动和融合","Please use \"Liquid motion\" (リキッドモーション), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #013\n\nWhat it is: Shapes move and merge like liquid\nWhat the sample shows: A blob stretches out, breaks into drops and merges back into one.\nSpec:\n- Lead circle (radius 44): moves 300 px right at 0.35–1.45 s with cubic-bezier(.7, 0, .2, 1), rising 34 px on a sine arc while moving; returns the same way at 2.7–3.8 s.\n- Seven circles follow the same path, each 0.065 s later, radius tapering 44→15, wobbling ±6 px vertically.\n- Even while it rests, three small circles (radius 15, 13, 11) move in and out between 34 and 64 px from it, twice per cycle.\n- Merged look: draw the circles in white → blur 9 px → threshold the alpha (soft only between 112 and 144) → fill what remains with colour.\n- Fill is a diagonal gradient mint → blue → violet (#7C5CFF), with a white elliptical highlight on the lead circle.\nWhen to use it: Use it for an organic, soft look in logos, backgrounds and connecting moves.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/013.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让标志以液态动效入场，由液滴汇聚成形。"],
  "014": ["motion",14,"运动拖尾","运动物体身后留下逐渐淡去的轨迹","Please use \"Motion trail\" (モーショントレイル), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #014\n\nWhat it is: A fading trail follows a moving object\nWhat the sample shows: A ball moving in a figure eight leaves a fading trail of copies behind it.\nSpec:\n- A ball (coral, radius 25, white centre radius 11) traces a figure eight once per 4.7 s: x = 196·sin(a), y = 62·sin(2a), with a advancing at constant speed.\n- 15 copies, each placed 0.105 rad (about 0.079 s) further back along the path.\n- Copy radius goes 22→6 and opacity is 0.9 × (1 − i/15) + 0.05, so older copies are smaller and fainter.\n- Copy colour runs coral → yellow → blue from newest to oldest.\n- Draw the oldest copy first and the ball itself last.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show speed or a path: flying objects, cursors, points of light.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/014.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给飞行圆球添加五层逐渐淡出的拖尾。"],
  "015": ["motion",15,"粒子效果","大量小碎片喷出并散开","Please use \"Particles\" (パーティクル), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #015\n\nWhat it is: Many small pieces fly out and scatter\nWhat the sample shows: Particles keep shooting up from an emitter, spread out and fall.\nSpec:\n- 84 particles, emitted from the bottom centre (horizontal centre, 20 px above the bottom edge).\n- Initial velocity: ±190 px/s horizontally, 250–400 px/s upward. Gravity 470 px/s² (parabolic paths).\n- Each particle repeats with a period of 2.35 s or about 1.57 s, with a random start offset (fixed seed, so every run looks the same).\n- Lifetime up to 1.5 s: fade in over the first 0.06 s, fade out over the last 30%. Scale 1.15→0.7.\n- Shapes are circles, squares and triangles (size 5–11 px) in blue, coral, yellow and mint, spinning at up to ±4.5 rad/s.\nWhen to use it: Use it to add celebration or liveliness, in place of confetti or sparks.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/015.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","成功时从底部喷出四种颜色的粒子，在 1.5 s 内全部落下。"],
  "016": ["motion",16,"视差","远近图层以不同速度移动形成纵深","Please use \"Parallax\" (パララックス), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #016\n\nWhat it is: Near and far layers move at different speeds to show depth\nWhat the sample shows: A landscape pans sideways; near layers move more and far layers move less, creating depth.\nSpec:\n- Camera pan: ±108 px on a sine wave, one round trip per 4.7 s.\n- Each layer is offset by pan × factor in the opposite direction. Factors from back to front: stars 0.05, moon 0.1, far ridge 0.28, middle ridge 0.6, front hill and trees 1.25, nearest dark shapes 2.1.\n- Far layers use darker colours close to the background, nearer layers brighter ones; the nearest layer is a large dark silhouette along the bottom.\n- Every layer is drawn at least 200 px beyond both sides of the frame so its ends never show.\nWhen to use it: Use it to give flat artwork or photos depth: backgrounds, landscapes, scrolling scenes.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/016.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把风景拆成三层，近层滚动更快，形成视差。"],
  "017": ["motion",17,"遮罩转场","扩大的形状内部显现下一场景","Please use \"Mask transition\" (マスクトランジション), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #017\n\nWhat it is: The next scene appears inside a growing shape\nWhat the sample shows: A circle- or star-shaped window grows, showing the next scene inside it.\nSpec:\n- Day scene → night scene → day scene, 2.35 s each. The change runs at 0.45–1.6 s of each half (1.15 s), cubic ease-in-out.\n- The next scene is drawn on top of the current one, clipped to a shape; the shape grows until it covers the frame.\n- Day→night: a circle from the sun's centre (112, 104), radius 0→470.\n- Night→day: a five-point star from the moon's centre (427, 104), outer radius 0→1150, rotating 1.2 rad (about 69°) as it grows.\n- While it grows, the edge of the shape has a white outline (width 7).\nWhen to use it: Use it to change scenes starting from an object in the frame, such as a sun, logo or button.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/017.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用遮罩转场切换场景，让圆从中心在 0.7 s 内扩展开。"],
  "018": ["motion",18,"图形转场","图形覆盖画面后揭示下一场景","Please use \"Shape transition\" (シェイプトランジション), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #018\n\nWhat it is: Shapes cover the screen and uncover the next scene\nWhat the sample shows: Coloured bands sweep across and cover the frame; when they leave, the next scene is there.\nSpec:\n- Day → night → day, 2.35 s each. Four horizontal bands (height 52; blue, coral, yellow, mint) whose ends are slanted by 80 px.\n- Cover: 0.38–1.0 s. Each band's leading edge travels from one side of the frame to the other. Bands are delayed by 14% of the phase each, and each uses cubic ease-in-out over 58% of the phase.\n- At 1.0 s, when everything is covered, the scene underneath is swapped for the next one.\n- Uncover: 1.12–1.75 s. Each band's trailing edge follows with the same delays and curve, exposing the next scene.\n- Direction: left to right for day→night, mirrored for night→day.\nWhen to use it: Use it to change scenes with shapes in brand colours: chapter breaks, topic changes.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/018.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用四条斜向色带从左侧扫入，完成图形转场。"],
  "019": ["motion",19,"液态转场","液体流入画面并替换场景","Please use \"Liquid transition\" (リキッドトランジション), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #019\n\nWhat it is: Liquid flows in and replaces the scene\nWhat the sample shows: Paint-like liquid drips down from the top and fills the frame, becoming the next scene.\nSpec:\n- Day → night → day, 2.35 s each. Two liquid layers, both moving top to bottom with quadratic ease-in-out.\n- Layer 1 (flat colour: blue for day→night, coral for night→day): 0.35–1.5 s. Layer 2 (the next scene itself, clipped to the liquid shape): 0.7–1.8 s.\n- The liquid front moves from y = −110 to 130 px below the bottom edge. Its edge waves with two sine waves (amplitudes 13 px and 8 px), strongest midway.\n- Seven drips (30–54 px wide, round tips) hang from the front; length = base 30–110 px × (0.25 + 0.9 × wave strength), greatest midway.\n- Merged look: draw the shape in white → blur 7 px → threshold the alpha → fill with the colour (or the next scene).\nWhen to use it: Use it for a soft, organic scene change, for example in food, beauty or creative videos.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/019.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用蓝色墨水从顶部滴落铺满画面，完成液态转场。"],
  "020": ["motion",20,"穿越缩放","放大并穿过物体进入下一场景","Please use \"Zoom through\" (ズームスルー), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #020\n\nWhat it is: Zooms into an object and passes through it into the next scene\nWhat the sample shows: The camera pushes into the hole of a letter O and comes out in the next scene.\nSpec:\n- Scene X (ZOOM on yellow) → scene Y (GO! on blue) → scene X, 2.35 s each.\n- The current scene is scaled around the centre of an O's hole (radius 24.5). Maximum scale is 1.08× the value at which the hole covers the whole frame (about 14×).\n- Scale = maxScale^p (exponential zoom, which reads as constant speed).\n- p = 0.8 × cubic ease-in (0.25–1.2 s) + 0.2 × cubic ease-out (1.2–1.65 s): accelerate in, slow down at the end.\n- Inside the hole the next scene is placed at 1/maxScale. When the zoom ends it is exactly at full size, and the view switches to the next scene.\nWhen to use it: Use it to dive into a logo or letter and move to the next scene with momentum.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/020.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用穿越缩放加速穿过标志中字母 O 的孔洞，进入下一场景，时长 0.6 s。"],
  "021": ["motion",21,"翻转","像卡片翻面一样展示另一侧","Please use \"Flip\" (フリップ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #021\n\nWhat it is: Turns over like a card to show the other side\nWhat the sample shows: A card turns over around its vertical axis and shows its other side.\nSpec:\n- A card (300 × 156, radius 22). Front (blue, Q) ⇄ back (yellow, A), 2.35 s each.\n- Rotates 180° at 0.45–1.5 s (1.05 s) with backOut (s = 1.5), going slightly past 180° and coming back.\n- Card width = original width × |cos θ|. The face artwork is swapped as it passes 90°.\n- Perspective: the card is drawn in thin vertical slices whose height varies by up to ±20% × sin θ from one side to the other (far side shorter, near side taller).\n- During the turn it scales up 8% and lifts 6 px on a sine curve; a dark overlay with opacity 0.34 × |sin θ| shades the face. An elliptical shadow sits on the floor.\nWhen to use it: Use it for two things that are sides of one another: question and answer, before and after.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/021.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让价格卡片在 0.5 s 内翻转，展示背面的详情。"],
  "022": ["motion",22,"扫光","光带扫过物体表面","Please use \"Light sweep\" (ライトスイープ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #022\n\nWhat it is: A band of light crosses a surface\nWhat the sample shows: A band of light crosses the surface of a logo badge at an angle.\nSpec:\n- One sweep per 2.35 s. The light is drawn only inside a clip of the badge (400 × 112, radius 28, blue gradient).\n- Light band: a 116 px wide white gradient (opacity 0.72 in the middle, 0 at the edges) plus a thin 12 px band (opacity 0.5) 78 px away, rotated 0.42 rad (about 24°).\n- It moves from 130 px left of the badge to 130 px right of it (660 px) at 0.45–1.5 s, quadratic ease-in-out.\n- Sparkle: a four-point star at the top-right corner at 1.38–1.98 s; size 30 × sin(πq) × (1 + 0.2(1 − q)), rotating 0.9 rad.\n- The badge itself does not move.\nWhen to use it: Use it to give a logo, badge or button a premium finish.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/022.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","标志停稳后，让一道柔和扫光从左上移到右下。"],
  "023": ["motion",23,"故障效果","画面像发生故障一样错位和分色","Please use \"Glitch\" (グリッチ), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #023\n\nWhat it is: The picture breaks up as if it were malfunctioning\nWhat the sample shows: Text slices shift sideways, colours split and small bars appear, with no brightness flashing.\nSpec:\n- White bold text (104 px). It glitches twice per 4.7 s: 0.55–1.25 s (5 steps) and 2.9–3.74 s (6 steps); otherwise it is still.\n- Each step lasts 0.14 s and shows one fixed disturbance (stepped, not smoothly animated).\n- Colour split: a coral copy shifted 7–16 px left and 2 px down, a cyan (#22D3EE) copy shifted the same amount right and 2 px up, with the white text on top.\n- Slice shift: 2–4 horizontal strips (10–35 px tall, y 40–150) are displaced 18–64 px to the left or right.\n- Three small colour bars (coral, cyan, yellow; 30–120 wide × 5–12 tall) at random positions.\n- Background brightness never changes (no full-frame flashing). The random values use a fixed seed.\nWhen to use it: Use it for a digital, error or uneasy feel, as an accent on titles and scene changes.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/023.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给标题添加 0.3 s 的轻微故障效果，少量分色，不要闪屏。"],
  "024": ["motion",24,"冲击震动","物体落下时带动整个画面震动","Please use \"Impact shake\" (インパクトシェイク), one of the names in \"Motion graphics moves\".\nMotion Prompt #024\n\nWhat it is: The whole frame shakes when something lands\nWhat the sample shows: A heavy headline slab drops with a thud and the whole frame shakes from the impact.\nSpec:\n- One drop per 2.35 s (a yellow slab first, then a coral one). The slab is 250 × 100, radius 18.\n- Fall: 0.3–0.62 s from above the frame to the floor, cubic ease-in (accelerating). While falling it is stretched 1.12× vertically.\n- Lands at 0.62 s. The whole frame shakes for 1.1 s: x 15 px × e^(−5t) × sin(2π·5t), y 11 px × e^(−5t) × cos(2π·6.5t), rotation 0.02 rad × e^(−5t) × sin(2π·5t + 0.6).\n- For 0.3 s after landing the slab squashes vertically by up to 22% and recovers (it widens by the same amount; anchored at its base).\n- Four background blocks hop up to 24 px, 0.03–0.06 s late, over 0.5 s. Six white lines and six dust puffs spread from the floor and fade within 0.55 s.\n- Exit: the slab moves 300 px up at 1.85–2.2 s (backIn, s = 1.6).\nWhen to use it: Use it to land an important headline or number with weight and force.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/024.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/motion.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","标题落地时添加冲击震动，在 0.4 s 内停稳。"],
  "025": ["camera",1,"水平摇镜头","机位固定，向左或右转动镜头","Please use \"Pan\" (パン), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #025\n\nWhat it is: Pivot the camera left or right\nWhat the sample shows: The camera stays in place and pivots from left to right; because it is a rotation, near and far layers slide sideways by the same amount.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position fixed (height 1.5 m); yaw only, -0.32 rad → +0.32 rad (-18° → +18°, about 37° in total)\n- Timing: rotate from 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person (about 1.8 m tall) stands still 8 m ahead and slides right-to-left in frame\n- No parallax: mountains, buildings, trees and the person all shift by the same angle (focal length 330 px on a 539×208 card)\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the angle in whole degrees (-18° → +18°)\nWhen to use it: To reveal a wide location or to shift attention from one side of the scene to the other.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/025.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","固定机位，用 5 s 从左向右缓慢摇摄城市天际线。"],
  "026": ["camera",2,"垂直摇镜头","机位固定，向上或下转动镜头","Please use \"Tilt\" (ティルト), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #026\n\nWhat it is: Pivot the camera up or down\nWhat the sample shows: The camera stays in place and pivots upward, from a person at ground level up to the top of a tower.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position fixed (height 1.4 m); pitch only, -0.06 rad → +0.36 rad (-3° → +21°, about 24° in total)\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 7 m ahead; a 9.5 m tower (antenna tip at 11.8 m) stands 26 m away behind\n- On screen everything slides downward: the person leaves at the bottom while the tower top and its antenna enter\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the angle in whole degrees (-3° → +21°)\nWhen to use it: To show the height or scale of a building or a person.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/026.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从人物脚边缓慢向上摇镜头，直到塔顶。"],
  "027": ["camera",3,"推镜头","相机整体向主体靠近","Please use \"Dolly in\" (ドリーイン), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #027\n\nWhat it is: Move the camera toward the subject\nWhat the sample shows: The camera itself moves toward the subject; near objects grow and pass quickly while the distant mountains barely change.\nSpec:\n- Camera: moves forward (in depth) 0 m → 5.8 m; height 1.5 m, direction and focal length (330 px, shown as 24mm) fixed\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 8 m ahead; distance goes 8 m → 2.2 m, so they appear about 3.6× larger\n- Parallax: a foreground post (1.5 m left, 3.6 m deep) and a rock (1.6 m right, 4.8 m deep) pass out of frame; mountains 120 m+ away stay almost the same size\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- The top-right readout stays at 24mm (the difference from 04 Zoom in)\nWhen to use it: To move in on a person or detail while keeping a sense of depth.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/027.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","缓慢推镜头靠近她的脸，移动相机，不要变焦。"],
  "028": ["camera",4,"变焦推近","相机不动，通过镜头变焦放大","Please use \"Zoom in\" (ズームイン), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #028\n\nWhat it is: Magnify with the lens (camera stays put)\nWhat the sample shows: The camera does not move; only the focal length gets longer, so the whole picture enlarges by the same ratio.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position and direction fixed (height 1.5 m); only the focal length changes, 330 px → 1200 px (shown as 24mm → 87mm, about 3.6×)\n- Exponential interpolation: f = 330 × (8/2.2)^p, where p is a cubic ease-in-out from 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s)\n- Subject: a person stands still 8 m ahead; the final size matches 03 Dolly in (about 3.6×)\n- No parallax: the foreground post and rock, the person, buildings and mountains all scale by the same ratio (overlaps do not change)\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the focal length in mm (24mm → 87mm)\nWhen to use it: To direct attention to one point without moving the camera; it looks flatter and more observational than a dolly in.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/028.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","相机保持不动，用 3 s 变焦推近窗边的人物。"],
  "029": ["camera",5,"跟拍","相机随主体一起移动","Please use \"Tracking shot\" (トラッキング), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #029\n\nWhat it is: Move along with the subject\nWhat the sample shows: The camera moves sideways at the same speed as a walking person; the person stays centred while nearer posts sweep past faster.\nSpec:\n- Camera: moves right at a constant 1.7 m/s (x = -4.0 m → +4.0 m in 4.7 s); height 1.3 m, facing straight ahead; no easing\n- Subject: a person walks at the same x as the camera (7.5 m away) and stays in the centre of frame; legs and arms swing by sin(u×7)×0.42 rad\n- Parallax: posts every 1.6 m at 4 m depth sweep left fastest, then trees, then buildings (48 m away); mountains hardly move\n- Top-right readout shows \"→ 1.7m/s\"\n- Repeat: jumps back to the start every 4.7 s (posts and ground grid line up at the seam; background buildings and trees jump)\nWhen to use it: To follow a walking or running subject and keep the sense of movement while showing their action.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/029.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从正侧方跟拍行走的人物，相机与人物同速移动。"],
  "030": ["camera",6,"环绕镜头","相机绕主体移动","Please use \"Orbit (Arc shot)\" (オービット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #030\n\nWhat it is: Circle around the subject\nWhat the sample shows: The camera travels on a circle around the subject; the person stays centred while the trees and buildings behind sweep sideways.\nSpec:\n- Camera: travels on a circle of radius 6 m centred on the person (9 m ahead), from -0.95 rad → +0.95 rad (-54° → +54°, about 109° in total)\n- Direction: always faces the centre (yaw = -angle); height 1.7 m, pitch fixed at -0.07 rad (about 4° down)\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.6 s (3.1 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: the person does not move; a white dot on the face shifts sideways with the angle; a dashed circle of radius 1.3 m marks the ground\n- Background: 12 trees evenly spaced on a 10 m radius cross behind the person as the camera moves round\n- Return: hold 3.6–4.2 s, then cross-fade back over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows the angle (-54° → +54°)\nWhen to use it: To show a person or product in three dimensions, or to emphasise an entrance or a key moment.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/030.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用环绕镜头绕静立的人物拍摄半圈，始终保持人物居中。"],
  "031": ["camera",7,"升镜头","相机整体向上升起","Please use \"Crane up\" (クレーンアップ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #031\n\nWhat it is: Lift the camera up\nWhat the sample shows: The camera rises while tilting down until it looks down on the person.\nSpec:\n- Camera: rises from 1.4 m to 9 m while moving forward 0 m → 1.5 m\n- Direction: tilts down to keep the person (8 m ahead) in frame; pitch = -0.86 × atan2(height - 1.0, 8 - forward), about -2.5° → -44°\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: the person does not move; they get smaller as the camera rises, the ground grid fills the frame and the horizon leaves at the top\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the height (↑ 1.4m → ↑ 9.0m)\nWhen to use it: To pull away from a person at the end of a scene or to reveal how large the location is.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/031.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让相机从人物眼睛高度升起，直到看见整座城镇。"],
  "032": ["camera",8,"滑动变焦","主体大小不变，背景发生透视变化","Please use \"Dolly zoom (Vertigo)\" (ドリーズーム), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #032\n\nWhat it is: Subject stays, background warps\nWhat the sample shows: The camera pulls back while zooming in by the same ratio; the person keeps the same size and only the background closes in.\nSpec:\n- Camera: distance d to the person (8 m ahead) widens from 3.2 m → 8 m (a 4.8 m pull-back); height 1.3 m\n- Focal length: f = 330 × d/8 px, i.e. 132 px → 330 px (shown as 10mm → 24mm), keeping distance ÷ focal length constant\n- Timing: 0.5 s to 3.4 s (2.9 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: the person does not move and keeps the same height in frame; blue dashed lines 160 px wide at head (1.8 m) and feet show the size is constant\n- Background: buildings (48 m away) grow about 2.2× and mountains about 2.4×, closing in behind the person, while the ground in front of the person shrinks\n- Return: hold 3.4–4.2 s, then cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: For a moment of realisation, or to show unease or shock visually.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/032.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","在人物顿悟时做滑动变焦：保持脸的大小，让背景拉远。"],
  "033": ["camera",9,"焦点转移","在近处与远处之间切换对焦","Please use \"Rack focus\" (ラックフォーカス), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #033\n\nWhat it is: Shift focus between near and far\nWhat the sample shows: The camera does not move; focus shifts from a flower in the foreground to a person behind it, swapping which one is blurred.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position, direction and focal length all fixed (height 1.1 m); only the blur amounts change\n- Blur: the foreground flower (0.75 m left, 2 m away) goes 0 px → 7 px; the person and background (person 0.9 m right, 9 m away) go 6 px → 0 px; the ground grid uses 0.6× the background blur\n- Timing: 1.0 s to 2.6 s (1.6 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Focus marker: blue corner brackets travel in a straight line from the flower to the person, half-width shrinking 46 px → 30 px\n- Subject: neither the flower nor the person moves\n- Return: hold 2.6–4.2 s, then cross-fade back over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows focus distance (◎ 2m → ◎ 9m)\nWhen to use it: To move attention from foreground to background (or back) without cutting.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/033.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 1 s 将焦点从前景杯子转移到后方人物。"],
  "034": ["camera",10,"手持镜头","像手持相机一样轻微晃动","Please use \"Handheld\" (手持ち), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #034\n\nWhat it is: A slight shake, as if the camera were held by hand\nWhat the sample shows: Adds a small, irregular shake to the whole frame, as if the camera were held by hand instead of on a tripod.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position almost fixed; yaw, pitch, roll and height each get a sum of sine waves with different periods (T = 2π×u/4.7)\n- Yaw (rad) = 0.016·sin(3T) + 0.008·sin(7T+1) + 0.004·sin(13T+2), at most about ±1.6°\n- Pitch (rad) = 0.012·sin(4T+2) + 0.006·sin(9T+0.5) + 0.003·sin(17T+1.2), at most about ±1.2°\n- Roll (rad) = 0.02·sin(5T+1) + 0.008·sin(11T+3), at most about ±1.6°; height = 1.5 + 0.03·sin(6T) m\n- Subject: a person stands still 6.5 m ahead; the shake runs continuously with no easing or hold\n- All multipliers are integers, so it loops seamlessly every 4.7 s; top-right readout shows \"HANDHELD\"\nWhen to use it: To give a documentary feel or the sense of being present in the scene.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/034.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从后方手持跟拍步行人物，只保留轻微晃动。"],
  "035": ["camera",11,"FPV 穿越机镜头","以第一人称快速穿越场景","Please use \"FPV drone shot\" (FPV), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #035\n\nWhat it is: Fast, immersive fly-through\nWhat the sample shows: A first-person view flying low and fast between two rows of trees, banking from side to side.\nSpec:\n- Camera: flies forward at a constant 14 m/s (shown as 50km/h) with no easing; pitch fixed at -0.05 rad\n- Weave (T = 2π×u/4.7, two swings per 4.7 s): sideways 0.6·sin(2T-0.4) m, height 1.4 + 0.5·sin(2T) m\n- Bank: roll 0.22·sin(2T+0.6) rad (about ±12.6°), yaw 0.05·sin(2T) rad (about ±2.9°)\n- No subject. Trees 4.2 m tall stand 3.6 m to each side, every 8 m, the two rows offset by 4 m, and rush toward the camera\n- Speed lines: 10 radial strokes about 32–76 px long (longer toward the sides) in translucent grey, flowing outward and recycling\n- No hold and no cross-fade reset (the tree rows shift phase when it restarts every 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: For speed and immersion, or to fly through a location in one continuous move.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/035.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 FPV 穿越机镜头从树林间穿过，飞向河面。"],
  "036": ["camera",12,"荷兰角","倾斜相机，使地平线呈对角线","Please use \"Dutch angle\" (ダッチアングル), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #036\n\nWhat it is: Tilt the frame diagonally\nWhat the sample shows: A level camera rolls around its lens axis and holds with the horizon on a diagonal.\nSpec:\n- Camera: position fixed (height 1.5 m); roll only, 0 → 0.36 rad (about 21°); the whole picture turns around the frame centre\n- Timing: 0.6 s to 2.2 s (1.6 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Subject: a person stands still 7 m ahead; horizon, buildings and person all tilt by the same angle\n- Hold: stays tilted from 2.2 s to 4.2 s (time to read the tilted composition itself)\n- Return: cross-fade back to the level start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\n- Top-right readout shows the angle (∠ 0° → ∠ 21°)\nWhen to use it: To express unease, tension or the feeling that something is wrong.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/036.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给这个不安的场景使用约 15° 的荷兰角。"],
  "037": ["camera",13,"慢动作","放慢动作的播放速度","Please use \"Slow motion\" (スローモーション), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #037\n\nWhat it is: Play the action slower\nWhat the sample shows: In front of a fixed camera a person rises and falls slowly through a jump while leaves drift down slowly; the whole action is stretched out.\nSpec:\n- Camera: completely fixed (height 1.3 m); only the subject moves\n- Subject: a person 7 m away takes 3.8 s for one jump (0.5 s to 4.3 s); height = 4q(1-q)×1.1 m, a parabola peaking at 1.1 m, with q linear in time\n- Both arms are raised while airborne; the person stands still for 0.5 s before the jump and 0.4 s after landing\n- Leaves: 9 leaves fall from 3.4 m to the ground over 4.7 s while rotating, each offset by 1/9 of the cycle\n- Top-right readout shows \"120fps ×0.25\" (playback stretched 4×)\n- No hold and no cross-fade; loops seamlessly every 4.7 s\nWhen to use it: To let viewers study a brief action or expression, or to emphasise an emotional peak.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/037.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用慢动作展示水花溅起的瞬间。"],
  "038": ["camera",14,"速度渐变","在同一镜头中改变播放速度","Please use \"Speed ramp\" (スピードランプ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #038\n\nWhat it is: Change speed mid-shot\nWhat the sample shows: Within one shot the playback speed changes smoothly from fast to slow; a graph at bottom left shows the speed.\nSpec:\n- Camera: completely fixed (height 1.3 m); only the playback speed changes\n- Playback speed: 2.4× → 0.25×; the change takes 0.7 s (1.2 s to 1.9 s) with a quadratic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.45,0,0.55,1))\n- Subject: a person 8 m away runs from 6 m left toward the right; x = -6 + footage time × 2.0 m; they close in quickly during the fast section\n- Jump: a parabola while x is between -1.5 m and 2.5 m, peak 0.99 m, arms raised; take-off at about 0.94 s, most of the airtime plays in slow motion, landing at about 3.68 s\n- Graph: a 120×40 px speed curve at bottom left with a blue dot (radius 5 px) at the current time\n- Return: stops at 4.2 s, then cross-fades back over the last 0.5 s; top-right readout shows the rate (×2.4 → ×0.3)\nWhen to use it: To slow down only the key part of an action while keeping the lead-in quick.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/038.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给跳跃加速度渐变：先正常速度，到最高点放慢，再恢复正常。"],
  "039": ["camera",15,"延时摄影","把数小时压缩成几秒","Please use \"Time-lapse\" (タイムラプス), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #039\n\nWhat it is: Compress hours into seconds\nWhat the sample shows: With a fixed camera, 06:00 to 18:00 is compressed into a few seconds; sun, clouds, people and shadows move in fast forward.\nSpec:\n- Camera: completely fixed (height 1.6 m, pitch +0.08 rad, about 5° up)\n- Timing: 12 hours pass in 3.7 s (0.4 s to 4.1 s), cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- Sun: travels left to right along an arc, angle a = -1.25 rad → +1.25 rad; position (sin a×120, cos a×60 - 8) m at 170 m depth\n- Three clouds drift 140 m to the right in total, wrapping every 80 m; seven small figures each cross an 18 m width 6 times (odd and even ones in opposite directions)\n- Building shadows fall away from the sun and swing as it moves (translucent grey)\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s; the top-right clock runs 06:00 → 18:00 in 10-minute steps\nWhen to use it: To show a long stretch of time, or how a city, sky or task changes, in a short clip.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/039.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用延时摄影展示城市从黄昏到夜晚亮灯的过程。"],
  "040": ["camera",16,"定格","让动作暂停片刻","Please use \"Freeze frame\" (フリーズフレーム), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #040\n\nWhat it is: Pause the action for a beat\nWhat the sample shows: The picture stops at the moment a jumping person reaches the top, then resumes from the same frame 1.4 s later.\nSpec:\n- Camera: completely fixed (height 1.3 m); what stops is the footage time\n- Freeze: stops at 1.6 s and resumes at 3.0 s (1.4 s); footage time runs normally for 0–1.6 s, stays at 1.6 s while frozen, then continues as u-1.4\n- Subject: the jump of a person 7 m away is a parabola over footage time 0.6–2.6 s, peak 1.1 m; the freeze lands exactly on the peak (50% through)\n- Nine falling leaves also stop during the freeze; they fall 1.5× as fast as in 13 Slow motion\n- Freeze markers: a 5 px blue border and a pause icon at bottom centre (two blue bars on a 68×40 px white rounded box), fading in and out over 0.12 s\n- Top-right readout shows \"FREEZE\" only while frozen; no cross-fade reset\nWhen to use it: To emphasise a decisive moment, or to pause so a name or caption can be placed over the frame.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/040.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","她转身时定格 1 s，并显示姓名。"],
  "041": ["camera",17,"跳切","构图不变，跳过一段时间","Please use \"Jump cut\" (ジャンプカット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #041\n\nWhat it is: Same framing, skip ahead in time\nWhat the sample shows: Camera position and framing stay the same while the person's position and the clock jump; time is skipped inside one scene.\nSpec:\n- Join: a straight cut with no effect (0 frames); 5 shots of 0.94 s each (4.7 s ÷ 5)\n- Camera: identical position and framing in every shot (height 1.4 m, facing forward); the background does not move by a pixel\n- What changes: the person (7 m away) jumps in sideways position, -2.2 m → 1.4 m → -0.4 m → 2.4 m → 0.6 m; in shots 2 and 4 both arms are raised\n- Within each shot the person is still (the jump is shown only by the difference in position and pose)\n- Top-right clock: 10:02 → 10:17 → 10:41 → 11:06 → 11:30, showing that time was skipped in the same place\n- Shot 5 cuts straight back to shot 1\nWhen to use it: To tighten pauses in talk or work and raise the pace, or to show time passing quickly.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/041.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用相同构图的跳切快速略过准备过程。"],
  "042": ["camera",18,"匹配剪辑","利用相似形状或动作衔接镜头","Please use \"Match cut\" (マッチカット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #042\n\nWhat it is: Cut on a matching shape or motion\nWhat the sample shows: A thrown ball becomes, in the next shot, a sun at the same position and size; two different scenes are joined on a matching shape.\nSpec:\n- Join: a straight cut at 2.3 s (0 frames); the blue circle has the same position (120 px right, 46 px above centre) and radius 17 px on both sides\n- Outgoing shot (0–2.3 s): fixed camera (height 1.4 m); a person (1.2 m left, 7 m away) throws a ball from 0.5 s, cubic ease-out (about cubic-bezier(0.33,1,0.68,1))\n- Ball: travels from above the person's head (2.3 m high) to the match point; radius 5 px → 17 px, on an arc bulging up to 30 px\n- Incoming shot (2.3–4.7 s): a different place (no buildings, height 1.2 m); the blue circle in the same spot is now the sun and sinks 14 px over 2.4 s\n- Marker: a blue dashed circle of radius 26 px fades in and out within 0.7 s either side of the cut\n- Top-right readout shows \"SHOT 1\" → \"SHOT 2\"; at 4.7 s it cuts straight back to SHOT 1\nWhen to use it: To link two scenes far apart in time or place through a shared shape or motion.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/042.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从圆咖啡杯匹配剪辑到相同位置的满月。"],
  "043": ["camera",19,"甩镜头转场","快速横摇形成模糊并切入下一镜头","Please use \"Whip pan\" (ホイップパン), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #043\n\nWhat it is: Fast pan blur into the next shot\nWhat the sample shows: The camera swings sideways very fast and the next scene is swapped in during the streaked blur.\nSpec:\n- Join: 0.8 s, from 1.7 s to 2.5 s; in the first 0.4 s the outgoing shot swings away, in the last 0.4 s the incoming shot swings in and settles\n- First half: outgoing yaw 0 → +0.45 rad (about 26°), quadratic ease-in-out; second half: incoming yaw -0.45 rad → 0, same easing\n- Swap: a straight replacement at the 50% point, hidden because the blur is at its strongest\n- Blur: 9 renders spread over ±1.6 frames (at 30 fps) are averaged\n- Camera: height 1.4 m, fixed except during the swing; the subjects (a person in A, a car and city in B) do not move\n- Alternates A→B and B→A every 4.7 s (9.4 s for the round trip); top-right readout shows \"A → B\" / \"B → A\"\nWhen to use it: To change location or topic while keeping the energy up.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/043.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","向右甩镜头，落到下一个地点。"],
  "044": ["camera",20,"交叉溶解","两个镜头逐渐叠化切换","Please use \"Cross dissolve\" (クロスディゾルブ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #044\n\nWhat it is: Blend one shot into the next\nWhat the sample shows: The next picture is laid over the current one and its opacity rises until it takes over; both show through each other midway.\nSpec:\n- Join: 1.5 s, from 1.5 s to 3.0 s; the incoming picture's opacity goes 0 → 100%\n- Easing: quadratic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.45,0,0.55,1)); 50% at 2.25 s\n- The outgoing picture stays fully opaque underneath and the incoming one is drawn on top (the outgoing one is not faded out first)\n- Camera: fixed in both pictures (A at height 1.4 m; B at height 1.6 m, pitch +0.1 rad); the subjects do not move either\n- Only the outgoing picture shows for 0–1.5 s, only the incoming one for 3.0–4.7 s\n- Alternates A→B and B→A every 4.7 s (9.4 s for the round trip); top-right readout shows \"A → B\" / \"B → A\"\nWhen to use it: To convey a gentle passage of time or change of place, or to move into a memory.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/044.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 1 s 的交叉溶解，从清晨房间切换到同一房间的夜景。"],
  "045": ["camera",21,"划像转场","移动的边界逐步替换画面","Please use \"Wipe\" (ワイプ), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #045\n\nWhat it is: A moving edge replaces the shot\nWhat the sample shows: A vertical edge moves from left to right and the next picture replaces the current one behind it.\nSpec:\n- Join: 1.1 s, from 1.7 s to 2.8 s; the edge travels from just outside the left side (x = -4 px) to just outside the right side (x = 543 px)\n- Easing: cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1))\n- The incoming picture shows left of the edge and the outgoing one right of it; neither picture moves (a reveal by clipping, not a push)\n- Edge: a 4 px blue vertical line, visible only while it is moving\n- Camera: fixed in both pictures; the subjects do not move either\n- Alternates A→B and B→A every 4.7 s (9.4 s for the round trip); top-right readout shows \"A → B\" / \"B → A\"\nWhen to use it: To mark a clear change of scene or topic, or to switch between the two sides of a comparison.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/045.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从左向右划像，切换到下一场景。"],
  "046": ["camera",22,"突切","突然切到反差强烈的场景","Please use \"Smash cut\" (スマッシュカット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #046\n\nWhat it is: Abrupt cut to a contrasting scene\nWhat the sample shows: A quiet scene of a person asleep cuts with no warning straight to an intense one; the volume meter jumps at the same moment.\nSpec:\n- Join: a straight cut at 2.4 s (0 frames); no transition effect, the contrast does the work\n- Outgoing shot (0–2.4 s): fixed camera (height 1.2 m, focal length 330 px); a person lying down 7 m away, three \"z\" letters float up and fade; volume meter at about 0–1 of 8 bars (0.08±0.04)\n- Incoming shot (2.4–4.2 s): focal length 2.6× (858 px) for a tight framing, rolled -0.12 rad (about -7°); the person has both arms raised, with 18 radial blue lines\n- Shake in the incoming shot: roll ±0.03 rad (about 6 cycles per second) and yaw ±0.006 rad (about 8 per second); volume meter at 0.85±0.15, nearly full\n- Return: cross-fade back to the quiet shot over the last 0.5 s (quadratic ease-in-out)\n- Top-right readout shows \"♪ 静か\" (quiet) → \"♪ 大音量\" (loud)\nWhen to use it: For comedy or shock, showing in an instant the gap between calm and chaos or between expectation and reality.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/046.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","从安静的卧室突切到嘈杂的路口。"],
  "047": ["camera",23,"J 型剪辑","下一场景的声音先于画面进入","Please use \"J-cut\" (Jカット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #047\n\nWhat it is: Next scene's audio starts first\nWhat the sample shows: The next scene's audio starts before the picture changes; the picture is shown on top with video and audio timelines below.\nSpec:\n- Join: the picture is a straight cut; only the audio switches to the next scene (B) before the picture does. The offset is 20% of the timeline (0.72 s)\n- Playhead: moves left to right at constant speed over 3.6 s (0.4 s to 4.0 s); audio switches at 35% (about 1.66 s), picture at 55% (about 2.38 s)\n- In the offset section (35–55%) the picture is still A while the audio is already B; the section is marked with a pale blue band and two blue dashed lines\n- Layout: the top 134 px is the picture (fixed camera, subjects do not move); the bottom 74 px holds two timeline rows, video and audio (A grey, B pale blue, waveform on the audio row)\n- Labels: \"映像A / 映像B\" (video A / B) at bottom left of the picture; the audio now playing at bottom right (\"♪ Aの音\" grey → \"♪ Bの音\" blue)\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To build anticipation for the next scene, or to make a change of scene or speaker feel natural.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/047.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 J 型剪辑先引入下一场景的海浪声，再切换到海面。"],
  "048": ["camera",24,"L 型剪辑","前一场景的声音延续到下一画面","Please use \"L-cut\" (Lカット), one of the names in \"Camera moves & transitions\".\nMotion Prompt #048\n\nWhat it is: Previous scene's audio carries over\nWhat the sample shows: The previous scene's audio carries on for a while after the picture has changed; the picture is shown on top with video and audio timelines below.\nSpec:\n- Join: the picture is a straight cut; only the audio switches to the next scene (B) after the picture does. The offset is 20% of the timeline (0.72 s)\n- Playhead: moves left to right at constant speed over 3.6 s (0.4 s to 4.0 s); picture switches at 55% (about 2.38 s), audio at 75% (about 3.10 s)\n- In the offset section (55–75%) the picture is already B while the audio is still A; the section is marked with a pale blue band and two blue dashed lines\n- Layout: the top 134 px is the picture (fixed camera, subjects do not move); the bottom 74 px holds two timeline rows, video and audio (A grey, B pale blue, waveform on the audio row)\n- Labels: \"映像A / 映像B\" (video A / B) at bottom left of the picture; the audio now playing at bottom right (\"♪ Aの音\" grey → \"♪ Bの音\" blue)\n- Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)\nWhen to use it: To keep a speaker's voice running while showing the listener's reaction or related footage.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/048.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用 L 型剪辑保留她的说话声，同时切到听者的脸。"],
  "049": ["ui",1,"模态对话框","打开浮窗并暂时阻止操作背景","Please use \"Modal dialog\" (モーダル), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #049\n\nWhat it is: A window opens in the middle while the page behind dims\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Open\" dims the whole page and a small window scales up slightly into the centre; clicking × closes it.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. The cursor reaches the \"Open\" button (120×36, lower left) at 0.95 s and clicks at 1.0 s.\n- Open amount a: 0→1 over 1.0–1.32 s with easeOutCubic. A full-card scrim rgba(18,20,28) at opacity 0.42·a.\n- Window: white 280×140, radius 12, centred at (271, 97), shadow blur 24, offset y 8, alpha 0.25. Scale 0.9 + 0.1·a, opacity a.\n- Inside: a bold title bar, two text lines, a blue 88×30 button at lower right and × at top right.\n- Close: the cursor moves to × by 3.0 s and clicks at 3.3 s; a is multiplied by (1 − easeInOutCubic over 3.3–3.58 s).\nWhen to use it: Use it when the user must stop and deal with one thing, such as a confirmation or a short form.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/049.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","点击删除按钮后显示模态确认对话框，页面变暗约 40%，用 0.3 s 淡入并略微放大。"],
  "050": ["ui",2,"抽屉面板","从屏幕侧边滑出的面板","Please use \"Drawer (Off-canvas)\" (ドロワー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #050\n\nWhat it is: A menu panel slides in from the side of the screen\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Menu\" slides a tall panel in from the left; clicking outside slides it back.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. The cursor clicks the \"Menu\" button (110×34, top left) at 1.0 s.\n- Open amount a: 0→1 over 1.0–1.38 s with easeOutCubic. Full-card scrim rgba(18,20,28) at opacity 0.36·a.\n- Panel: white, 210 wide, full card height, x = −210 + 210·a so it slides in from the left edge. Shadow blur 22, alpha 0.25.\n- Inside: an avatar (radius 14) and name at the top, then four menu rows 32 px apart; the first row is selected with a light-blue band.\n- Close: the cursor clicks outside at (420, 120) at 3.3 s; a is multiplied by (1 − easeInOutCubic over 3.3–3.65 s) and the panel slides back.\nWhen to use it: Use it to keep navigation or filters off screen until needed, especially on mobile.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/050.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","点击菜单按钮后从左侧打开抽屉，宽度占屏幕 40%，用 0.4 s 滑入，页面略微变暗。"],
  "051": ["ui",3,"底部面板","从屏幕底部升起的面板","Please use \"Bottom sheet\" (ボトムシート), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #051\n\nWhat it is: A panel slides up from the bottom of the screen\nWhat the sample shows: A finger taps \"View details\" and a panel rises from the bottom; dragging its handle down closes it.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A finger (semi-transparent circle, radius 17, white rim) taps the \"View details\" pill (170×36, bottom centre) at 1.0 s.\n- Open amount: 0→1 over 1.05–1.45 s with easeOutCubic. Full-card scrim rgba(18,20,28) at opacity 0.36·a.\n- Sheet: white, 136 tall, top corners radius 18, top edge at y = 191 − 136·a. Shadow blur 22, offset y −4. A 52×6 grab handle at top centre.\n- Inside: a bold title bar and two rows with 26×26 icons.\n- Close: the finger lands on the handle (271, 68) at 2.75 s and drags down over 3.0–3.6 s; a is multiplied by (1 − easeInOutCubic over 3.0–3.6 s), so the sheet follows the finger off the bottom.\nWhen to use it: Use it on mobile to show details or choices while keeping the current screen in view.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/051.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","点击查看详情后弹出高度占屏幕 40% 的底部面板，0.4 s 升起，向下拖动关闭。"],
  "052": ["ui",4,"折叠面板","点击标题展开或收起内容","Please use \"Accordion\" (アコーディオン), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #052\n\nWhat it is: Click a heading to show or hide its content\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the first of three headings opens its content and pushes the rows below down; clicking again closes it.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Three headings (494 wide, 34 tall, radius 8, gap 6) with a down chevron at the right.\n- The cursor reaches the first heading at 0.95 s and clicks at 1.0 s and 3.3 s.\n- Open amount ex: 0→1 over 1.0–1.35 s with easeInOutCubic, then 1→0 over 3.3–3.62 s.\n- The first row grows from 34 to 92 tall (+58·ex) and pushes the rows below down; its two content lines are clipped to the row and fade in with opacity ex.\n- While open, the chevron rotates 180°·ex, the border turns light blue and the heading blue.\nWhen to use it: Use it for FAQs or long details where people scan the headings and open only what they need.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/052.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把常见问题做成折叠面板，点击后在 0.35 s 内展开，箭头旋转 180°。"],
  "053": ["ui",5,"下拉选择框","点击字段展开选项列表","Please use \"Dropdown (select)\" (ドロップダウン), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #053\n\nWhat it is: Click a field to drop a list of options below it\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the field opens four options below it; picking \"Nagoya\" closes the list and fills the field.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A 260×38 field (radius 8) shows a placeholder and a chevron; the cursor clicks it at 1.0 s.\n- Open amount: 0→1 over 1.0–1.25 s with easeOutCubic. The list (white 260×112, shadow blur 18) fades in while dropping 6 px. The chevron turns 180° and the field border becomes 2 px blue.\n- Four options 26 px apart (Tokyo, Osaka, Nagoya, Fukuoka in Japanese). As the cursor moves down, Osaka is highlighted light blue from 1.55 s and Nagoya from 1.95 s.\n- Click on Nagoya at 2.3 s: the list closes over 2.3–2.45 s (1 − easeInOutCubic); the placeholder fades out over 2.2–2.3 s and \"Nagoya\" fades in over 2.32–2.42 s.\n- Reset: Nagoya fades out over 3.9–4.08 s, then the placeholder returns over 4.1–4.3 s, so the two texts never overlap.\nWhen to use it: Use it in a form when people pick one value from a fixed list.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/053.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把地区字段做成下拉选择框，0.25 s 展开下方选项，选中后回填并收起。"],
  "054": ["ui",6,"文字提示","悬停时显示简短说明","Please use \"Tooltip\" (ツールチップ), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #054\n\nWhat it is: Hover over something to show a short label\nWhat the sample shows: Hovering over a \"?\" icon shows a short note in a dark bubble above it; it disappears when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A \"?\" icon (blue ring, radius 13) at (196, 121) next to a label.\n- The cursor only hovers, no click: it arrives on \"?\" at 1.05 s, stays until 3.15 s and leaves the card by 4.1 s.\n- Show amount a: 0→1 over 1.15–1.35 s with easeOutCubic; opacity a, rising 6 px into place.\n- Bubble: #26282c, 184×36, radius 8, top at y 64, with a 16-wide, 8-tall triangle pointing down at the icon; white 15 px text.\n- Hide: linear 1→0 over 3.25–3.45 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it to add a one-line hint to an icon or abbreviation without taking space on the page.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/054.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给问号图标加文字提示，悬停 0.2 s 后在上方显示，移开即隐藏。"],
  "055": ["ui",7,"气泡卡片","点击后显示指向触发按钮的小面板","Please use \"Popover\" (ポップオーバー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #055\n\nWhat it is: Click a button to open a small panel pointing at it\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Details\" opens a small white panel to its right with a pointer at the button; clicking OK inside closes it.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. An outlined blue \"Details\" button (108×36) at (24, 112); the cursor clicks it at 1.0 s.\n- Show amount a: 0→1 over 1.0–1.28 s with easeOutCubic; opacity a, sliding 6 px in from the right.\n- Panel: white 300×120, radius 10, at (156, 62), 1 px border, shadow blur 22, offset y 6. A 10-wide triangle on its left edge (y 122–138) points at the button.\n- Inside: a bold title bar, two text lines, an outlined 70×26 button and a blue 72×26 OK button.\n- Close: the cursor moves to OK (402, 157) by 3.0 s and clicks at 3.3 s; a is multiplied by (1 − easeInOutCubic over 3.3–3.5 s).\nWhen to use it: Use it for a short setting or confirmation that belongs right next to the button that opened it.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/055.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给详情按钮加右侧气泡卡片，0.3 s 展开，点击确定关闭。"],
  "056": ["ui",8,"轻提示","短消息出现后自动消失","Please use \"Toast notification\" (トースト), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #056\n\nWhat it is: A short message appears in a corner and goes away on its own\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Save\" slides a dark notice into the bottom-right corner; when its time bar runs out it slides away.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. The cursor clicks the blue \"Save\" button (110×36, bottom left) at 1.0 s and leaves to the bottom left.\n- Toast: #26282c, 214×52, radius 10, 18 px from the right and 16 px from the bottom; slides in 240 px from the right over 1.05–1.4 s with easeOutCubic.\n- Inside: a white check in a blue circle and white 15 px text \"Saved\".\n- A time-left line along the bottom (3 px tall) shrinks linearly from 194 px to 0 over 1.4–3.2 s.\n- Exit: slides 240 px out to the right over 3.2–3.55 s with easeInOutCubic.\nWhen to use it: Use it to confirm a result such as a save or send without interrupting the user.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/056.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","保存后在右下显示已保存轻提示，0.35 s 从右侧滑入，2 s 后自动消失。"],
  "057": ["ui",9,"标签页","点击标签切换内容面板","Please use \"Tabs\" (タブ), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #057\n\nWhat it is: Click a label to switch which panel is shown\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the tabs \"Overview, Pricing, Reviews\" in turn slides a blue underline across and swaps the content below.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Three tabs at x 24, 114, 204, widths 70, 70, 100; a 2 px divider at y 50 and a 4 px blue underline.\n- The cursor clicks the second tab at 1.0 s, the third at 2.2 s and the first at 3.4 s.\n- Underline: position and width move to the new tab over 0.25 s from each click with easeInOutCubic (from the third back to the first it passes through the middle).\n- Labels: selected is blue and bold, others grey; the switch happens at 1.1, 2.3 and 3.5 s.\n- Content: the old panel fades out linearly in 0.2 s; 0.1 s later the new one fades in over 0.2 s while rising 8 px.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show several related views in the same space and let people switch between them.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/057.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","价格页顶部放三个标签页，下划线用 0.25 s 滑动，内容用 0.2 s 叠化。"],
  "058": ["ui",10,"轮播图","横向滑动切换展示项","Please use \"Carousel\" (カルーセル), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #058\n\nWhat it is: Slides that move sideways to show one item at a time\nWhat the sample shows: Each click on the right arrow slides a row of three different images one step to the left, and the dot below moves.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Slides 330×138, radius 8, centred with an 18 px gap; the neighbours peek in at the edges.\n- White round buttons (radius 18, shadow blur 10) with chevrons at left and right; three dots below (current one blue 16×8, others 8×8).\n- The cursor clicks the right arrow (514, 88) at 1.0, 2.1 and 3.2 s.\n- Each click moves the row 348 px left (one slide plus gap) over 0.4 s with easeInOutCubic.\n- The three pictures (landscape, three circles, bar chart) repeat, so after three moves the first is back.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show several images or featured items in limited space, one at a time.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/058.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把顶部图片做成轮播图，右箭头每次用 0.4 s 切一张，下方显示位置圆点。"],
  "059": ["ui",11,"开关","切换设置的开启与关闭状态","Please use \"Toggle switch\" (トグルスイッチ), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #059\n\nWhat it is: Flip a setting on or off\nWhat the sample shows: The switches on the first two of three setting rows are turned on in turn, then off again.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Three setting rows 60 px apart with dividers. At x 450 a 64×34 track (radius 17) and a white knob (radius 13, shadow).\n- Clicks: row 1 on at 1.0 s, row 2 on at 1.8 s, row 1 off at 3.0 s, row 2 off at 3.6 s. Row 3 stays off.\n- Each switch takes 0.2 s with easeOutCubic; the knob slides 30 px (17 → 47).\n- The track colour blends from grey #d9d7d5 to blue #1f5ae8 with the switch progress.\nWhen to use it: Use it for settings that take effect immediately and have only two states.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/059.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","通知设置使用开关，滑块用 0.2 s 移动，开启时轨道变蓝。"],
  "060": ["ui",12,"分段控制器","一排相连按钮用于切换视图","Please use \"Segmented control\" (セグメントコントロール), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #060\n\nWhat it is: A row of joined buttons that switches the view\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking Day, Week or Month slides a blue highlight across and the bar chart below changes height.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A grey 300×40 base (radius 10) at (121, 12), split into three 100-wide segments: Day, Week, Month (in Japanese).\n- Selection: blue 92×32, radius 8, shadow blur 6; the selected label is white.\n- The cursor clicks Week at 1.0 s, Month at 2.1 s and Day at 3.3 s; the selection slides over 0.25 s each with easeInOutCubic.\n- Chart below: seven bars 34 wide, 58 px apart (the sixth is blue). Heights move between three data sets (about 30–85, 40–100, 60–115) together with the selection, eased the same way.\nWhen to use it: Use it to switch between two to four views of the same content, such as day, week and month.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/060.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","图表上方加日、周、月分段控制器，选中背景用 0.25 s 滑动，图表同步变化。"],
  "061": ["ui",13,"筛选标签","点击小标签组合筛选条件","Please use \"Filter chips\" (チップ), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #061\n\nWhat it is: Small pills you click to add or remove a filter\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the \"New\" and \"Free\" chips adds a check mark and turns them blue, and cards that do not match fade out.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Four chips (\"All, New, Popular, Free\" in Japanese): 34 tall, radius 17, width = text + 32, 10 px apart from the left.\n- Clicks: New on at 0.95 s, Free on at 1.75 s, New off at 3.0 s, Free off at 3.6 s.\n- Each change takes 0.15 s with easeOutCubic: the chip widens 18 px to make room for a check mark; fill light blue, border and text blue.\n- List below: four cards (242×54, two columns, two rows); cards that do not match drop from opacity 1 to 0.12.\nWhen to use it: Use it to let people narrow a list or search results by combining a few quick filters.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/061.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","列表上方加入筛选标签，选中后打勾并变蓝，0.15 s 内更新列表。"],
  "062": ["ui",14,"范围滑块","双滑块选择最小值与最大值","Please use \"Range slider\" (レンジスライダー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #062\n\nWhat it is: Two handles on one track pick a minimum and a maximum\nWhat the sample shows: On a price slider, the left handle is dragged right and the right handle left to narrow the range, then both go back.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Track: x 54–488, 8 tall, at y 120; the part between the two handles is blue. Range ¥0–¥10,000.\n- Handles: white, radius 13, 3 px blue rim; while dragged, radius 15 with a light-blue halo of radius 24.\n- Low handle: 0.1 → 0.3 (¥1,000 → ¥3,000) over 1.0–1.6 s, back over 3.55–3.9 s. High handle: 1.0 → 0.8 (¥10,000 → ¥8,000) over 2.1–2.6 s, back over 2.95–3.3 s. All easeInOutCubic.\n- A value bubble (28 tall) above each handle, blue with white text while dragged. The range \"¥1,000 – ¥10,000\" is shown in blue at top right, updated in ¥100 steps.\n- The cursor sits on the handle it drags (presses at 1.0, 2.1, 2.95 and 3.55 s).\nWhen to use it: Use it to filter by a range, such as price, date or size, with a minimum and a maximum.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/062.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","价格筛选改用范围滑块：两个滑块，拖动时在气泡中显示各自数值。"],
  "063": ["ui",15,"步进器","通过加减按钮逐次修改数值","Please use \"Stepper (+/−)\" (ステッパー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #063\n\nWhat it is: Plus and minus buttons that change a number by one\nWhat the sample shows: Pressing + three times raises the number from 1 to 4, and pressing − three times brings it back to 1; the number pops on each press.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A 200×60 box (radius 12) at (171, 52): \"−\" in the left 60 px, a blue \"+\" in the right 60 px, and a bold 30 px number in the middle.\n- Clicks: + at 0.9, 1.35, 1.8 s (1 → 4), − at 2.8, 3.25, 3.7 s (4 → 1).\n- The pressed segment is tinted light blue from 0.05 s before to 0.15 s after each click.\n- Number: on each press its scale goes linearly from 1.18 back to 1 over 0.25 s, and it is blue meanwhile.\nWhen to use it: Use it for small whole numbers changed one at a time, such as quantity or number of guests.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/063.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","数量字段使用步进器，加减每次变化 1，数字每次用 0.25 s 轻弹一下。"],
  "064": ["ui",16,"分页","通过页码切换列表页面","Please use \"Pagination\" (ページネーション), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #064\n\nWhat it is: Numbered buttons that move between pages\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking 2 and then 3 in the page numbers moves the blue circle and swaps the list above; finally it goes back to 1.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. \"‹ 1 2 3 4 5 ›\" centred, each 36 in diameter with 8 px gaps, at y 160. A blue circle (radius 18) marks the current page, with white text.\n- The cursor clicks 2 at 1.0 s, 3 at 2.1 s and 1 at 3.3 s.\n- The blue circle moves 44 px per page over 0.2 s each with easeInOutCubic (88 px at once from 3 back to 1).\n- The three-row list above dips in opacity 1 → 0 → 1 within 0.2 s either side of 1.05, 2.15 and 3.35 s, and its content changes at the dip.\nWhen to use it: Use it to split a long list, such as search results or articles, into numbered pages.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/064.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","搜索结果下方加分页，当前页蓝色圆圈用 0.2 s 移动，并替换列表内容。"],
  "065": ["ui",17,"汉堡菜单","三横线图标点击后展开菜单","Please use \"Hamburger menu\" (ハンバーガーメニュー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #065\n\nWhat it is: A three-line icon that opens the menu\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking the three-line icon at the header's right turns it into ×, and a menu drops down from under the header; clicking again closes it.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A white 44-tall header; three lines (24 long, 3 thick, 8 px apart) at (500, 22) on the right.\n- The cursor clicks at 1.0 s and 3.3 s. Open amount a: 0→1 over 1.0–1.3 s, 1→0 over 3.3–3.6 s, easeInOutCubic.\n- Lines to ×: the top and bottom lines move 8 px to the centre and rotate ±45°; the middle line fades with opacity 1 − a. Blue while open.\n- Menu: white, 140 tall, top at y = 44 − 140 + 140·a so it drops from under the header (clipped below the header), shadow blur 16, four items, the first blue.\nWhen to use it: Use it on narrow screens to tuck the main navigation behind one button.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/065.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","移动端页头右侧放汉堡菜单，点击后用 0.3 s 变成 ×，菜单从顶部展开。"],
  "066": ["ui",18,"面包屑导航","显示页面层级位置的链接路径","Please use \"Breadcrumbs\" (パンくずリスト), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #066\n\nWhat it is: A trail of links showing where the page sits in the site\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Courses\" in the breadcrumbs goes up to the list page; clicking a card there returns to the detail page.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. At the top \"Home › Courses › Web design\" (in Japanese, 17 px): links blue, current page black and bold; a divider at y 46.\n- The cursor hovers \"Courses\" (underline 0.9–1.2 s) and clicks at 1.0 s.\n- Up amount: 0→1 over 1.0–1.25 s with easeInOutCubic. \"› Web design\" fades out and \"Courses\" becomes the current page (black, bold).\n- Content cross-fades from a detail page (title and text) to a list of three cards (158×118, with a landscape picture).\n- Back: the cursor moves onto the first card (blue outline 2.45–2.8 s) and clicks at 2.7 s; the detail page returns over 2.7–2.95 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it on sites with deep hierarchies to show where the page is and give a way back up.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/066.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","文章上方加首页 › 课程 › 网页设计面包屑，当前页加粗且不作为链接。"],
  "067": ["ui",19,"巨型菜单","主导航展开的宽幅分组链接面板","Please use \"Mega menu\" (メガメニュー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #067\n\nWhat it is: A wide panel of grouped links that opens from the main menu\nWhat the sample shows: Hovering over \"Products\" in the header drops a full-width panel with three columns of links and an image; it closes when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A 42-tall header with \"Products, Pricing, Support\" (in Japanese, 16 px, each with a down chevron).\n- The cursor only hovers: it reaches \"Products\" at 1.0 s. Open amount a: 0→1 over 1.05–1.3 s with easeOutCubic; \"Products\" turns blue with an underline.\n- Panel: white, full width, 146 tall, dropping 12 px into place under the header while fading in with a. Shadow blur 18, offset y 8.\n- Inside: three columns 130 px apart (a blue heading and three links each) and a 104×112 picture at the right. The cursor moves down and the second link of the second column is highlighted light blue from 1.75 to 2.9 s.\n- Close: the cursor leaves the panel from 2.9 s; it fades over 3.15–3.4 s (1 − easeInOutCubic).\nWhen to use it: Use it on sites with many products or sections so visitors can see the whole range at once.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/067.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给页头的“产品”加上巨型菜单：悬停后用 0.25 s 展开全宽面板，包含三列链接和一张图。"],
  "068": ["ui",20,"步骤指示器","显示流程的当前步骤与进度","Please use \"Step indicator\" (ステップインジケーター), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #068\n\nWhat it is: Shows which step of a process you are on\nWhat the sample shows: Each click on \"Next\" turns the next of four step circles into a check and extends the blue line to the following step.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. Four steps (\"Details, Review, Payment, Done\" in Japanese) at x 80, 207, 334, 461, y 35; circles of radius 17 joined by a 4 px grey line.\n- The cursor clicks \"Next\" (110×38, bottom right) at 0.9, 1.7 and 2.5 s.\n- On each click the current step becomes a blue circle with a white check and the next becomes the current one (blue circle, white number). Steps not reached are white with a grey rim.\n- The blue line grows 127 px per click over 0.3 s with easeInOutCubic; after the third click all four are checked.\n- Reset: the indicator fades out over 3.75–4.05 s and fades back in at step 1 over 4.05–4.3 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it in multi-step flows such as sign-up or checkout to show progress and what is left.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/068.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","注册表单顶部放信息、确认、支付、完成四步指示器，已完成步骤显示勾。"],
  "069": ["ui",21,"骨架屏","加载时以灰色块预示内容布局","Please use \"Skeleton screen\" (スケルトン), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #069\n\nWhat it is: Grey shapes stand in for content while it loads\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking reload turns the list into grey blocks of the same shape with a sweeping shine; the content returns when loading ends.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A two-row list (a 96×56 picture and three text lines each). The cursor clicks the reload icon at top right at 1.0 s.\n- Over 1.05–1.2 s (linear) the content switches to grey #e9e7e5 rounded blocks of the same size and position.\n- Shine: a white band 160 wide (transparent at the edges, opacity 0.75 in the middle) sweeps from x −200 to x 742 every 0.9 s, drawn only over the blocks.\n- The content returns over 3.0–3.3 s (linear).\nWhen to use it: Use it for lists or cards that take a moment to load, so the layout is visible while people wait.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/069.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","列表加载时显示骨架屏，灰块形状对应内容，每 0.9 s 从左向右扫一道光。"],
  "070": ["ui",22,"加载转圈","旋转圆环表示等待","Please use \"Spinner\" (スピナー), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #070\n\nWhat it is: A spinning circle that means \"please wait\"\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Send\" washes the card white and a blue arc spins in the middle; when finished it changes to a check and fades.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. The cursor clicks \"Send\" (120×40, bottom centre) at 1.0 s.\n- Over 1.05–1.2 s (linear) a white scrim (opacity 0.78) and the spinner fade in over the whole card.\n- Spinner at (271, 92): a pale ring, radius 26, 6 thick, with a blue 243° (1.35π) arc on top (round caps), turning 1.3 times per second (468°/s).\n- Over 2.95–3.05 s the spinner fades; over 2.95–3.2 s a blue circle (radius 28) with a white check scales 0.7 → 1 (easeOutCubic).\n- Everything fades out linearly over 3.75–4.0 s.\nWhen to use it: Use it for short waits of unknown length, such as sending or saving.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/070.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","发送时在表单上方显示每秒转一圈多的加载圆环，完成后换成蓝色勾。"],
  "071": ["ui",23,"徽标","用小圆点或数字显示数量","Please use \"Badge\" (バッジ), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #071\n\nWhat it is: A small dot with a number showing a count\nWhat the sample shows: Each time a notification arrives, the blue dot on the bell in the header counts up 1, 2, 3; clicking the bell clears it.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A 54-tall header with a line-drawn bell at (482, 27) on the right.\n- Badge: a blue circle of radius 12 at the bell's top right (+12, −12), 2.5 px white rim, white 14 px number.\n- Notifications arrive at 0.7, 1.3 and 1.9 s: the count goes 1 → 2 → 3. The first scales in over 0.7–0.9 s with easeOutCubic.\n- Each arrival pops the scale from 1.3 back to 1 over 0.3 s and sends out a ripple ring (radius 12 → 28, opacity 0.5 → 0) over 0.5 s.\n- The cursor reaches the bell at 2.95 s and clicks at 3.0 s; the badge shrinks to 0 over 3.0–3.25 s with easeInOutCubic.\nWhen to use it: Use it to call attention to a count, such as unread messages or items in a cart.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/071.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","页头铃铛上显示未读数徽标，数量增加时弹跳 0.3 s，打开后消失。"],
  "072": ["ui",24,"空状态","列表没有内容时显示的界面","Please use \"Empty state\" (エンプティステート), one of the names in \"UI component names\".\nMotion Prompt #072\n\nWhat it is: The screen shown when there is nothing to list yet\nWhat the sample shows: Deleting the two list rows with their trash icons brings up an empty-box drawing, \"Nothing here yet\" and an \"Add\" button.\nSpec:\n- 4.5 s cycle on a 542×191 card. A two-row list (494×48, radius 8, a trash icon at the right).\n- The cursor clicks the trash icons at 0.95 s and 1.65 s. Each row slides 60 px left while fading out over 0.3 s (easeInOutCubic); the second row moves up 58 px into the first slot.\n- Over 1.95–2.3 s (linear) the empty state fades in while rising 8 px: a blue line drawing of an inbox tray, \"Nothing here yet\" (16 px, in Japanese) and a blue \"Add\" button (112×34).\n- The cursor clicks \"Add\" at 3.3 s; the empty state fades over 3.25–3.45 s and the two rows come back from the left over 3.35–3.7 s with easeOutCubic.\nWhen to use it: Use it for first-use screens or no-results pages to tell people what to do next.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/072.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/ui.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","列表为空时显示空状态：线描图标、“暂无内容”和添加按钮，用 0.35 s 淡入。"],
  "073": ["lp",1,"视差滚动","滚动时背景层比内容移动得慢","Please use \"Parallax scrolling\" (パララックススクロール), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #073\n\nWhat it is: On scroll, background layers move slower than the content\nWhat the sample shows: As the page scrolls down, the headline moves up normally while the sky and sun, far hills and near hills move more slowly.\nSpec:\n- A browser window with a 511 × 168 viewport. Scroll: 0→120 px at 0.3–1.9 s, 120→0 at 2.9–4.3 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- Each layer moves by scroll × factor: sky and sun 0.15, far hills 0.4, near hills 0.7.\n- Headline (28 px), button and the next section move at 1.0 (normal scrolling).\n- The next section (white) starts at the bottom of the hero (168 px) and slides over the slower background.\n- The scrollbar thumb on the right moves with the scroll.\nWhen to use it: Use it to give the hero or a section photo a sense of depth.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/073.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让首屏背景以滚动距离的 0.3× 移动，形成视差滚动。"],
  "074": ["lp",2,"滚动淡入","元素进入视口时逐渐出现","Please use \"Fade-in on scroll\" (スクロールでフェードイン), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #074\n\nWhat it is: Elements fade in as they scroll into view\nWhat the sample shows: As the page scrolls, the heading, the cards and the body text each rise into place and fade in when they enter the view.\nSpec:\n- Scroll: 0→95 px at 0.35–1.0 s, 95→200 px at 1.5–2.1 s, 200→0 at 3.2–4.4 s (all cubic ease-in-out).\n- Trigger line at 85% of the viewport height (143 px from the top). An element fires when its top edge passes above it (the Intersection Observer idea).\n- After firing, over 0.7 s: opacity 0→1 and offset 28 px below → 0 (cubic ease-out).\n- Three elements: the heading (172 px down the page), a row of three cards (206 px) and body text (334 px), all below the view at first. The cards in the row appear together.\n- When an element leaves the bottom of the view on the way back up, it is reset out of sight and plays again next time.\nWhen to use it: Use it on a long landing page to bring content in piece by piece as the reader scrolls.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/074.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","标题和卡片滚动进入视口时，从下方 30 px 在 0.6 s 内上移淡入。"],
  "075": ["lp",3,"吸顶页头","滚动时页头停留在屏幕顶部","Please use \"Sticky header\" (追従ヘッダー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #075\n\nWhat it is: The header stays at the top while the page scrolls\nWhat the sample shows: The announcement strip scrolls away, but the header below it stops at the top edge and the content scrolls underneath.\nSpec:\n- Scroll: 0→110 px at 0.4–1.3 s, 110→250 px at 1.9–2.8 s, 250→0 at 3.4–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- At the very top, a 22 px announcement strip (navy); below it a 34 px header (logo, three menu items, button).\n- Header position = max(22 − scroll, 0): once the strip is gone, it stops at the top edge (position: sticky; top: 0).\n- Over the next 24 px of scroll, a 12 px shadow under the header fades from 0 to 0.16 opacity.\n- The content (photo, heading, three cards) scrolls normally under the header.\nWhen to use it: Use it to keep the menu and the call-to-action within reach on a long page.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/075.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把页头设为吸顶，到达顶部后加一层柔和阴影。"],
  "076": ["lp",4,"滚动固定","区块固定，滚动推动内部内容变化","Please use \"Pinning\" (ピン留め), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #076\n\nWhat it is: A section stays fixed while scrolling advances its content\nWhat the sample shows: A navy section stops when it fills the view; further scrolling steps the number and photo through 1→2→3, then the section scrolls on.\nSpec:\n- Scroll: 0→500 px at 0.3–3.0 s, 500→0 at 3.5–4.5 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- The section (168 tall, navy) reaches the top at 110 px of scroll and stays there for the next 300 px (a GSAP ScrollTrigger pin).\n- Progress while pinned: p = (scroll − 110) / 300. A vertical line (124 long) on the left fills in orange with p.\n- At p = 1/3 and 2/3 (±0.07, cubic ease-in-out) it moves to the next step: the number (46 px) rolls up 52 px and the photo (226 × 124) slides up 124 px.\n- After 300 px the pin is released and the section scrolls up with the white section below it.\nWhen to use it: Use it to walk through steps, features or a before/after in one screen.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/076.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","固定三步骤区块，用户滚动时逐步切换照片和编号。"],
  "077": ["lp",5,"横向滚动","纵向滚动驱动内容横移","Please use \"Horizontal scroll\" (横スクロール), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #077\n\nWhat it is: Scrolling down moves the content sideways\nWhat the sample shows: As the page scrolls down, the section holds still and four numbered work cards travel to the left.\nSpec:\n- Scroll: 0→420 px at 0.3–3.0 s, 420→0 at 3.5–4.5 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- The heading \"WORKS\" scrolls away; the section reaches the top at 40 px of scroll and stays there.\n- Cards: four at 200 × 112, gap 20, side padding 34. Horizontal travel = 34·2 + 200·4 + 20·3 − 511 = 417 px.\n- Card x = start x − p × 417, with p = (scroll − 40) / 380: linear in scroll, no easing.\n- The scrollbar thumb moves down while the cards move sideways.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show work, case studies or products in a row inside a long vertical page.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/077.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把作品区做成横向滚动：向下滚动多少，卡片就向左移动多少。"],
  "078": ["lp",6,"滚动吸附","滚动结束时自动对齐区块","Please use \"Scroll snap\" (スクロールスナップ), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #078\n\nWhat it is: Scrolling settles exactly on the next section\nWhat the sample shows: After a small scroll, the page carries itself the rest of the way until the next section's top lines up with the top of the view.\nSpec:\n- Each section is as tall as the viewport (168 px). The first is pale blue, the second navy.\n- One snap per 2.4 s. At 0.45–0.85 s the user scrolls only 34 px (cubic ease-out).\n- At 0.9–1.5 s the page moves the remaining 134 px by itself and lines up the next section's top (cubic ease-out).\n- The second 2.4 s does the same upward, back to the first section (the behaviour of scroll-snap-type: y mandatory).\nWhen to use it: Use it for a page that should read one full screen at a time, like slides.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/078.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","让页面按区块滚动吸附，轻滚一下就落到下一节顶部。"],
  "079": ["lp",7,"滚动进度条","顶部条显示阅读进度","Please use \"Scroll progress bar\" (スクロールプログレスバー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #079\n\nWhat it is: A bar at the top shows how far you have read\nWhat the sample shows: As the article is read a bit at a time, the line along the top grows from the left and reaches the far end at the bottom of the page.\nSpec:\n- The article scrolls 0→430 px in four 110 px steps, each moving for 0.45 s then pausing 0.4 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- It returns 430→0 at 3.75–4.55 s.\n- A 6 px bar along the top of the viewport: light grey track, orange fill.\n- Fill width = 511 px × scroll / 430, the scroll fraction itself (the same as CSS animation-timeline: scroll()).\nWhen to use it: Use it on long articles to show how much is left to read.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/079.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","文章顶部放 4 px 厚的品牌橙色滚动进度条。"],
  "080": ["lp",8,"荧光笔标记动画","重点文字下方逐渐画出色带","Please use \"Highlighter animation\" (マーカーアニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #080\n\nWhat it is: A highlighter stroke is drawn under key words\nWhat the sample shows: As the copy scrolls into view, a yellow highlighter stroke is drawn left to right across the lower half of the key words.\nSpec:\n- Scroll: 0→90 px at 0.35–1.0 s, 90→180 px at 1.6–2.2 s, 180→0 at 3.3–4.4 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- Two lines of copy (20 px, bold) at 190 px and 290 px down the page, hidden below the view at first.\n- When a line's top passes the trigger line (80% of the viewport height, 134 px), the stroke under its key words starts.\n- Stroke: yellow #FFE36B, 11 tall, in the lower part of the text (8 px above to 3 px below the baseline). Width 0 → word width from the left over 0.8 s (cubic ease-out), drawn behind the text.\n- Lines that leave the bottom of the view are reset out of sight.\nWhen to use it: Use it in landing-page copy to make the one phrase that matters stand out as it is read.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/080.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","关键词进入视口时，在下方用 0.8 s 从左向右画出黄色荧光标记。"],
  "081": ["lp",9,"悬停抬升","悬停时元素抬高并加深阴影","Please use \"Hover lift\" (ホバーで浮き上がる), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #081\n\nWhat it is: On hover, the element rises with a deeper shadow\nWhat the sample shows: Only the card under the cursor lifts slightly and its shadow spreads; it settles back when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- Three cards (146 × 128, radius 10). The cursor rests on each, left to right, for about 1 s.\n- On hover the card rises 10 px over 0.3 s (cubic ease-out); on leave it returns over the same 0.3 s (like a CSS transition).\n- Shadow, changed together with the lift: blur 6→22 px, y offset 2→12 px, opacity 0.08→0.22.\n- Light grey page, white cards, so the shadow reads.\nWhen to use it: Use it to make cards and buttons look clickable.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/081.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给卡片加上悬停抬升：光标悬停时用 0.3 s 抬高 8 px，同时加深阴影。"],
  "082": ["lp",10,"悬停图片放大","图片在固定边框内放大","Please use \"Image zoom on hover\" (ホバーで画像ズーム), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #082\n\nWhat it is: The photo enlarges inside a fixed frame\nWhat the sample shows: The photo under the cursor slowly enlarges while its frame stays the same size, and shrinks back when the cursor leaves.\nSpec:\n- Two photo frames, 222 × 118 (radius 8). The cursor rests on the left one, then the right one, for about 1.5 s each.\n- On hover the content scales 1→1.15 from the centre over 0.5 s (cubic ease-out); on leave it returns over 0.5 s.\n- Anything outside the frame is clipped (overflow: hidden). The frame and the caption do not move.\nWhen to use it: Use it on photo grids (work, products, articles) to show which item is about to be chosen.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/082.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给作品照片加上悬停图片放大：外框不变，内容用 0.5 s 放大到 1.1×。"],
  "083": ["lp",11,"光标跟随","图形略带延迟地跟随指针","Please use \"Cursor follower\" (マウスストーカー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #083\n\nWhat it is: A shape trails the mouse pointer with a delay\nWhat the sample shows: As the cursor moves around the page, an orange circle follows it a little behind.\nSpec:\n- Cursor path: x = 255 + 175·sin(2πt/4.8), y = 86 + 46·sin(4πt/4.8) (a figure eight lying on its side, one lap per 4.8 s).\n- Circle: radius 17, orange, opacity 0.88, drawn under the cursor.\n- Follow rule: every frame (60 fps) it covers 12% of the remaining distance (x += (cursor x − x) × 0.12).\n- The arrow cursor stays visible.\nWhen to use it: Use it on brand sites and portfolios to add a playful, hands-on feel.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/083.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","全站加入光标跟随：一个直径 30 px 的橙色圆，稍有延迟地跟随光标。"],
  "084": ["lp",12,"磁吸按钮","按钮向附近光标偏移","Please use \"Magnetic button\" (マグネティックボタン), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #084\n\nWhat it is: The button is pulled toward a nearby cursor\nWhat the sample shows: As the cursor comes near, the button is drawn toward it and follows; when the cursor leaves, the button wobbles back to its place.\nSpec:\n- A 168 × 52 button (orange, radius 26) in the centre. The pull range is a 110 px radius from the button's centre.\n- Inside the range: target offset = (cursor − button centre) × 0.35; every frame (60 fps) the button covers 18% of the way to the target.\n- On leaving the range it returns from its current offset to 0 over 1.1 s with elastic.out(1, 0.3): 2^(−10x)·sin((x − 0.075)·2π/0.3) + 1.\n- The cursor enters from the left, circles the button and leaves to the right.\nWhen to use it: Use it on the one button you most want clicked, such as sign-up or contact.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/084.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把联系按钮做成磁吸按钮：向光标方向移动两者距离的 0.3×，移开后弹回原位。"],
  "085": ["lp",13,"涟漪效果","从点击位置扩散的圆形波纹","Please use \"Ripple effect\" (リップルエフェクト), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #085\n\nWhat it is: A ripple spreads from the point that was pressed\nWhat the sample shows: Each click sends a white circle out from the click point to fill the button, then it fades away.\nSpec:\n- Button 280 × 56 (orange, radius 10). Clicks at 0.7 s (left of centre) and 2.9 s (right of centre).\n- The circle is centred on the click point; its radius grows from 0 to the distance to the button's farthest corner over 0.6 s (cubic ease-out).\n- White at 0.4 opacity, fading to 0 between 0.3 and 0.8 s after the click.\n- The circle is clipped to the button (overflow: hidden); the label sits above it.\nWhen to use it: Use it to confirm a press on a button or list item right where it happened.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/085.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给提交按钮加上涟漪效果：点击时从点击处扩散出白色圆形，在 0.6 s 内淡去。"],
  "086": ["lp",14,"下划线动画","悬停时链接下划线从左展开","Please use \"Underline animation\" (下線アニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #086\n\nWhat it is: A link's underline grows from the left on hover\nWhat the sample shows: Under the link the cursor is on, an orange line grows from the left; when the cursor leaves, the line shrinks away to the right.\nSpec:\n- Three links (20 px, bold, 56 apart). The cursor rests on each, left to right, for about 1 s (hit area 6 px wider than the text on each side).\n- Underline: orange, 3 thick, 8 px below the baseline.\n- On hover, width 0→100% from the left end over 0.3 s (cubic ease-out).\n- On leave, the left end moves right over 0.3 s, so the line exits to the right (like scaleX with transform-origin on the right).\nWhen to use it: Use it on menu and text links to show where the pointer is, quietly.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/086.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","菜单链接悬停时下划线用 0.3 s 从左长出，移开时向右收起。"],
  "087": ["lp",15,"前后对比滑块","拖动分隔线比较处理前后","Please use \"Before/after slider\" (ビフォーアフタースライダー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #087\n\nWhat it is: Drag a divider to compare before and after\nWhat the sample shows: Dragging the line in the middle of the photo left and right changes how much of the grey \"before\" (left) and the coloured \"after\" (right) is shown.\nSpec:\n- Photo frame 359 × 140 (radius 10). Right: the edited photo in colour. Left: the same photo as the \"before\" (saturation removed, navy at 0.18 opacity on top).\n- The before image is clipped to the left of the divider. On the divider: a white line (3 wide) and a white circle (radius 17) with left/right arrows.\n- At 0.7 s the circle is grabbed; the divider goes 50%→20% (0.75–1.55 s) →82% (1.55–2.65 s) →50% (2.65–3.55 s), all cubic ease-in-out.\n- Released at 3.62 s. Labels BEFORE (top left) and AFTER (top right).\nWhen to use it: Use it on pages that sell a change: renovation, beauty, photo retouching.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/087.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","项目照片加入前后对比滑块，拖中线比较左侧处理前与右侧处理后。"],
  "088": ["lp",16,"离站挽留弹窗","访客准备离开时出现的弹窗","Please use \"Exit-intent popup\" (離脱防止ポップアップ), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #088\n\nWhat it is: A popup shown when the visitor is about to leave\nWhat the sample shows: When the cursor heads out through the top of the page (toward the tabs and close button), the page dims and a \"Wait!\" popup opens. The × closes it.\nSpec:\n- The cursor rises from the page toward the browser's address bar at 0.7–1.25 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- It fires when the cursor crosses the top edge of the viewport (y = 0, at about 1.07 s), the same test as mouseleave on document with clientY ≤ 0.\n- Opens 0.05–0.45 s after firing (cubic ease-out): backdrop navy 0→0.5 opacity; popup (260 × 132, radius 12) opacity 0→1 and scale 0.9→1.\n- Inside: a heading, a discount line (orange), a coupon button and an × at the top right.\n- Click on the × at 2.9 s; it disappears 0.03–0.25 s later (linear).\nWhen to use it: Use it to make one last offer to visitors who are about to leave without converting.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/088.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","光标从落地页顶部离开时，展示一次优惠券挽留弹窗。"],
  "089": ["lp",17,"预加载画面","页面加载期间显示的过渡界面","Please use \"Preloader\" (ローディング画面), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #089\n\nWhat it is: A screen shown while the page loads\nWhat the sample shows: On a navy screen the number under the logo counts from 0% to 100%; then the screen lifts away and the page underneath fades in.\nSpec:\n- A navy screen fills the viewport with a logo, a number (28 px) and a bar (180 × 4).\n- 0→100% at 0.25–2.1 s (cubic ease-out, rounded to whole numbers); the bar fills in orange at the same rate.\n- At 2.3–2.85 s the whole screen moves up 168 px and out (cubic ease-in-out).\n- The page heading and photo fade in 0→1 and rise from 14 px below at 2.35–2.95 s (cubic ease-out).\n- At 4.25–4.75 s the screen comes back down from the top, at 0% (the next load).\nWhen to use it: Use it on image- or video-heavy sites to turn the loading wait into a brand moment.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/089.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","做一个预加载画面：网站加载时显示标志与百分比，到 100% 后整屏上移退场。"],
  "090": ["lp",18,"懒加载","图片接近视口时才开始加载","Please use \"Lazy loading\" (遅延読み込み), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #090\n\nWhat it is: Images load only when they come into view\nWhat the sample shows: As grey placeholders scroll into view, a spinner turns in each, and the images fade in as they arrive. The top row is loaded from the start.\nSpec:\n- A 3 × 3 grid of 151 × 92 placeholders; the first row is shown from the start. Scroll: 0→110 px at 0.35–1.1 s, 110→225 px at 1.7–2.5 s, 225→0 at 3.5–4.5 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- Loading starts when a placeholder's top edge passes above the bottom of the viewport (168 px), with each column 0.12 s later than the one to its left.\n- For 0.45 s a spinner (radius 11, one turn per 0.8 s) turns in the placeholder's centre.\n- Then the image fades in 0→1 over 0.35 s (cubic ease-out). Unloaded placeholders show an image icon.\n- Placeholders that leave the bottom of the view are reset out of sight.\nWhen to use it: Use it on image-heavy pages to make the first view load faster.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/090.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","图片库使用懒加载，先显示灰色占位，载入后用 0.3 s 淡入。"],
  "091": ["lp",19,"无限滚动","滚动到底部时自动加载更多条目","Please use \"Infinite scroll\" (無限スクロール), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #091\n\nWhat it is: More items load automatically at the bottom\nWhat the sample shows: Scrolling down to the end of the list brings up a spinner, then three new items are added so reading can go on.\nSpec:\n- A list of items (331 × 44, radius 8, 52 apart) with a spinner (radius 10, one turn per 0.8 s) under the last item.\n- Scroll: 38→116 px at 0.25–0.85 s, 116→194 px at 1.15–1.75 s (cubic ease-in-out); it stops with the end of the list in view.\n- At 2.6 s three items are added: each fades 0→1 and rises from 10 px below over 0.35 s (cubic ease-out). The spinner moves to the new end.\n- Each cycle advances by three items (156 px). The content repeats every three items, so the end of the cycle looks the same as the start.\nWhen to use it: Use it for feeds and news lists that people should keep reading without paging.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/091.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","把新闻列表做成无限滚动：滚动到底部后显示加载圆环，每次追加十条。"],
  "092": ["lp",20,"页面转场","连接两个页面的过渡动画","Please use \"Page transition\" (ページ遷移アニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #092\n\nWhat it is: An animation that bridges two pages\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking a card in the work list sweeps an orange panel across from the left; the URL changes and the panel exits to the right on the detail page. \"Back to list\" returns the same way.\nSpec:\n- Click on a card at 0.8 s. At 0.9–1.3 s a panel (orange, full viewport, logo in the centre) enters from the left and covers everything (cubic ease-in-out).\n- At 1.3 s, while covered, the page and the URL in the address bar (/works → /works/02) switch.\n- At 1.4–1.85 s the panel exits to the right (cubic ease-in-out).\n- Click on \"← Back to list\" at 3.0 s: the panel enters at 3.1–3.5 s, the page switches at 3.5 s and the panel exits at 3.6–4.05 s.\n- The panel covers the whole viewport, header included.\nWhen to use it: Use it on brand sites and portfolios to link one page to the next.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/092.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","加上页面转场：点击链接时橙色面板从左向右扫过，再显示下一页。"],
  "093": ["lp",21,"平滑滚动","页内链接平滑移动到目标位置","Please use \"Smooth scroll\" (スムーススクロール), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #093\n\nWhat it is: In-page links glide to their target instead of jumping\nWhat the sample shows: Clicking \"Pricing\" in the menu glides the page down to the pricing section; the up arrow at the bottom right glides it back to the top.\nSpec:\n- At 0.9 s the \"Pricing\" menu item is clicked; scroll goes 0→296 px over 0.95–2.0 s (1.05 s, cubic ease-in-out).\n- Stop position = top of the pricing section (330 px) − fixed header height (34 px).\n- Once scroll passes 60 px, a round back-to-top button (radius 15) fades in over the next 40 px at the bottom right.\n- At 3.1 s that button is clicked; scroll goes 296→0 over 3.15–4.2 s (cubic ease-in-out).\n- While the pricing section is in view, \"Pricing\" in the menu turns orange.\nWhen to use it: Use it when a menu or table of contents jumps within the same page, so the reader sees where they went.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/093.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","菜单页内链接使用平滑滚动，停止在固定页头下方。"],
  "094": ["lp",22,"跑马灯","文字或标志组成连续滚动带","Please use \"Marquee\" (マーキー), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #094\n\nWhat it is: Text or logos scroll across in an endless band\nWhat the sample shows: Inside a navy band, large service names separated by orange dots keep moving to the left without a gap.\nSpec:\n- Band: 58 tall, navy, full viewport width. Text: 30 px, heavy weight, 1 px letter spacing, white.\n- One set is four words (WEB DESIGN / BRANDING / MOTION / UI/UX), 64 px apart, with an orange dot (radius 6) in each gap.\n- Each cycle (4.8 s) moves left by the width of one set (about 881 px here) at constant speed. The set is measured and the offset wraps by that width, so there is no visible seam.\n- The set is repeated until the viewport width is filled.\nWhen to use it: Use it to show service names, client logos or a tagline with energy.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/094.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","用跑马灯让服务名称从右向左无缝循环滚动，速度约 80 px/s。"],
  "095": ["lp",23,"动态渐变","背景颜色持续移动和交融","Please use \"Animated gradient\" (グラデーションアニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #095\n\nWhat it is: Background colours keep drifting and blending\nWhat the sample shows: Behind the headline, soft patches of orange, light orange, blue and light blue drift in circles and keep blending differently.\nSpec:\n- Base colour #FFF1EB, with four radial gradients on top (centre colour → transparent at the edge, each at 0.85 opacity).\n- Orange (radius 230), light orange #FFB08F (210), blue (240), light blue #9DB6FB (200).\n- Each centre travels an ellipse once per 4.8 s (x radii 70, 60, 80, 50; y radii 30, 40, 30, 35; start angles 0, 2.1, 4.2, 1.0 rad).\n- A white headline (34 px) and a button sit on top; only the gradient moves.\nWhen to use it: Use it to add movement and colour behind a hero or heading without using a photo.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/095.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","首屏用橙蓝缓慢交融的动态渐变背景，每 10 s 循环一次。"],
  "096": ["lp",24,"悬浮动画","元素轻柔地上下浮动","Please use \"Floating animation\" (ふわふわアニメーション), one of the names in \"Landing page & web effects\".\nMotion Prompt #096\n\nWhat it is: Elements bob gently up and down\nWhat the sample shows: Next to the headline, a phone, a heart badge and a rating chip each bob gently out of step, and the shadow under the phone grows and shrinks.\nSpec:\n- Phone (92 × 132): y = −8·sin(2πt/2.4), one bob per 2.4 s; a sine slows at both ends.\n- Heart badge (radius 20): y = −6·sin(2πt/1.6 + 1.2). Rating chip (76 × 30): y = −6·sin(2πt/2.4 + 2.4).\n- Shadow under the phone (54 × 6 ellipse): size and opacity scale by (1 + y/40), so it shrinks and fades as the phone rises.\n- Both periods (2.4 s and 1.6 s) divide 4.8 s, so the loop has no seam.\nWhen to use it: Use it to add quiet motion to product images, app mockups or decorative icons.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/096.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/lp.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","给首屏的手机图加上悬浮动画：上下浮动 8 px，每 2.4 s 往返一次。"],
  "097": ["photo",1,"逆光","光源位于主体后方","Please use \"Backlighting\" (逆光), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #097\n\nWhat it is: The light source sits behind the subject\nWhat the sample shows: The sun moves from outside the frame to directly behind the person's head; a thin bright edge appears around the figure, a pale warm haze covers the frame and the side facing the camera darkens.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). light is a flat amber #FFC75A shape, shadow a flat #33405A one\n- Sun: radius 20 px, from outside the frame (top left, x 40, y −40) to directly behind the head (x 270, y 56), with flat rings of 2.6× and 1.7× the radius (#FFE3A3 at 35% and 60%)\n- Outline: the figure is stroked with a 7 px line and then filled, leaving a 3.5 px bright edge outside it\n- Figure #4D5A75 → #33405A; sky #FAF9F7 → #FFF4DC; #FFE3A3 laid over the whole frame at 22%\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: For airy, glowing portraits or any image that should feel bathed in light.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/097.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","草地人像用逆光，低处太阳正对头后，发丝边缘发亮，带柔和薄雾。"],
  "098": ["photo",2,"轮廓光","后侧光勾勒主体边缘","Please use \"Rim light\" (リムライト), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #098\n\nWhat it is: A light from behind that outlines the subject's edge\nWhat the sample shows: The surroundings go dark and two lights behind the person, left and right, draw thin bright edges only along both sides of the head and shoulders; the plan at the bottom right shows where the two lights are.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). \n- Background: light scene → dark scene (sky #2B2D33, ground #24252A); figure #4D5A75 → #1F2128\n- Bright edges: two copies of the figure in amber #FFC75A, shifted 3.5 px left and right and 2.5 px up, placed behind the dark figure (3.5 px wide edges)\n- Plan at the bottom right (66×66 px): lights at ±135° seen from above (behind, left and right); top-right readout \"±135°\"\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: To separate a person or product from a dark background and show its shape.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/098.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","黑色背景人像，两侧后方打轮廓光，脸保持暗，只让头肩轮廓发亮。"],
  "099": ["photo",3,"剪影","主体成为明亮背景前的深色轮廓","Please use \"Silhouette\" (シルエット), one of the names in \"Photo looks, lighting & styles\".\nMotion Prompt #099\n\nWhat it is: The subject shows as a black shape against a bright sky\nWhat the sample shows: As the exposure is set for the bright evening sky, the person, buildings, lamp and tree turn into flat black shapes with no detail and only the sky stays bright.\nSpec:\n- Scene 1: a head-and-shoulders figure in front of a horizon at y 150 (head centre x 270, y 78, radius 29 px, no face or hair). \n- Sky: #FAF9F7 → #FFEDC4 at the top and a #FFCF73 band near the horizon (y 92–150)\n- Everything but the sky becomes #2A2D36, the far hills #4A4546; the figure #22252D\n- Sun: radius 20 px at x 404, sinking from y 60 to y 128, half hidden by the hills\n- Top-right readout: ±0.0 EV → −2.0 EV\n- Timing: the effect comes in from 0.4 s to 1.4 s, holds until 4.0 s and is gone again by 4.8 s (one pass = 5 s, cubic ease-in-out (about cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1)))\nWhen to use it: When the shape and pose should carry the picture, against a sunset or a bright window.\n\nReference implementation (Canvas 2D, a function whose picture depends only on the time): https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/en/e/099.txt\nShared helper code: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/photo.js\nKeep the shapes, timing and easing values of the reference implementation as they are, and change only the text, colours and assets to fit what I am making.","夕阳海滩上跳跃的人物剪影，按天空曝光，让人物和棕榈树变成纯黑。"],
};
